Critic's reasoning: [Forced acceptance after 3 attempt(s) without a clean accept — the required changes below are known issues carried forward for a future sprint to address, not resolved.] This is real progress on N3: several actionable attributes now have dedicated value categories, and the previous symbol/list typing contradiction is repaired. The bundle cannot be accepted intact because it duplicates an existing glossary construct, has canonical-order violations in normative examples, and overclaims symbolic coverage for an itinerary constraint whose required temple qualifier is absent. The listed vocabulary and type changes are self-contained, non-regressive increments and should land now.
Required changes (address every one explicitly): [{"target": "descriptive-value", "change": "Change the operation from add to revise. It already exists in the current glossary, so a second entry would be duplicate and conflicting; replace its state-inclusive semantics and example with the narrowed mod_/dom_ definition."}, {"target": "Generate", "change": "Correct the worked example to obey its own canonical ordering: target, content, duration, duration_unit, max_walk_duration, max_walk_duration_unit, stop_min_per_day. Also add a typed symbolic requirement field, such as stop_requirement -> entity-name/category-value, so 'at least one temple per day' is not reduced to an unqualified count."}, {"target": "Action", "change": "Correct the search_web worked example to its stated required-first then alphabetical optional order: target, availability, color, currency, location, max_price, shape. Do not retain examples that violate the canonical encoding rule."}, {"target": "attribute-name", "change": "Do not describe future category names as if they govern values now. For each transitional STRING attribute, explicitly state that it remains an N3 violation in the build phase and give a concrete next-step category specification; prioritize code-path-value, code-symbol-value, code-call-value, code-outcome-value, food-value, meal-value, message-structure-value, and procedure-value."}, {"target": "itinerary constraints", "change": "Define the semantics and value category for what a per-day minimum applies to, plus the scope of max walking duration (e.g. consecutive itinerary stops), rather than only accepting two numbers and units."}, {"target": "state-value", "change": "Add explicit canonical members and synonym mappings for state_full and state_empty, since they are required by the sampled household task and are not merely illustrative variants of warm/clean."}, {"target": "basis", "change": "Add canonical translation rules for closed-task decomposition and for choosing TASK versus CONVO versus GENERATE. In particular, specify when status checks are hoisted, which entity is target for order/customer support actions, and the canonical artifact/result type for multi-item generation."}]
Logic issues: ["The proposal adds descriptive-value even though descriptive-value already exists. This conflicts with the stated change operation and would create duplicate normative glossary entries rather than revise the residual bucket.", "Generate's Kyoto worked example violates its own canonical ordering: stop_min_per_day appears before max_walk_duration and max_walk_duration_unit, although optional attributes must be alphabetized.", "Action's mirror worked example violates its own canonical ordering: availability, currency, location, max_price, and shape are not emitted in alphabetical optional-attribute order.", "stop_min_per_day=1 cannot encode the source meaning 'at least one temple per day'; it expresses only an unqualified minimum count. The proposed claim that the constraint is symbolically covered is therefore overstated.", "The new attribute-name entry calls itself a complete index while numerous attributes still resolve only to STRING and a named future category. Naming an eventual category is not a present value-set rule under N3."]
Pre-KPI assessment: {"coverage": {"impact": "benefit", "reasoning": "The added shape, state, metric, locale, style, itinerary, browsing, and discount facilities cover several previously unsupported held-out constraints, including round mirrors, full/empty rolls, support discounts, and itinerary timing. However, the proposed stop_min_per_day attribute records only a number and cannot state that the required daily stop is a temple, while several code and content attributes remain opaque STRING payloads."}, "expressivity": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "The proposal adds first-class fields for several constraints previously hidden in content, but its itinerary example still loses the required temple category: stop_min_per_day=1 means only a count. Transitional STRING attributes continue to carry code paths, expected outcomes, policies, message structure, and substantive generation requests as prose rather than defined value sets."}, "determinism": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Dedicated value categories and the closed-for-encoding format rule improve convergence. Yet independent translations still diverge materially on TASK versus CONVO, target selection, status-query sequencing, artifact type, return type, and handle names; the new open categories also lack exhaustive synonym/canonicalization rules. The worked examples themselves violate the stated canonical attribute ordering."}, "interpretability": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Splitting state/style/locale/metric out of descriptive-value makes values easier to look up. But attribute-name calls itself a complete index while retaining dozens of unresolved future categories, and the duplicate add of the already-existing descriptive-value entry is structurally unclear. The overloaded rule that every vocabulary symbol statically counts as STRING also obscures category identity in general typed contexts."}, "improvement": {"impact": "benefit", "reasoning": "A weaker planner gains useful actionable structure from color, shape, state, discount percentage, support metrics, and numeric itinerary constraints. It still cannot reliably act on semantic constraints hidden in STRING content, such as the private-members feature behavior, the exact temple requirement, or a user-provided script that must be revised."}}
Simulated examples that exposed gaps: [{"item_id": "held-support-1", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "If the customer's order is late and they're a first-time buyer, offer a 10% discount; if they're a repeat buyer, offer free expedited shipping instead.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT HandleLateOrder\nTASK HandleLateOrder {\n  ACTION check_support_status(target=order, metric=metric_order_late) -> is_late : BOOL\n  ACTION check_support_status(target=customer, metric=metric_first_time_buyer) -> is_first_time : BOOL\n  ACTION check_support_status(target=customer, metric=metric_repeat_buyer) -> is_repeat : BOOL\n  IF is_late AND is_first_time THEN {\n    ACTION offer_discount(target=order, discount_percent=10)\n  } ELSE {\n    IF is_late AND is_repeat THEN {\n      ACTION offer_expedited_shipping(target=order)\n    }\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "metric-value and discount_percent directly help. The entity symbols are assumed available through existing entity-name under N6."}, {"item_id": "dev-code-1", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "Given a list of file paths, delete every file older than 30 days unless it's in the 'archive' folder.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT DeleteOldFiles\nTASK DeleteOldFiles(files : LIST[STRING]) {\n  FOR EACH file_path IN files {\n    ACTION file_age_days(target=file_path) -> age : NUMBER\n    ACTION path_in_folder(target=file_path, destination=\"archive\") -> is_archived : BOOL\n    IF age > 30 AND NOT is_archived THEN {\n      ACTION delete_file(target=file_path)\n    }\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The actionable control structure is present, but archive is a quoted STRING rather than a file-path/category value; code-path-value remains only a future target."}, {"item_id": "8c5ccffa-b88e-4928-9394-6d46cfd36e59", "source": "Mind2Web (osunlp/Mind2Web, train, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "What are today's Limited Time Offers deals?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FindLimitedTimeOffers\nTASK FindLimitedTimeOffers : LIST[REF[STRING]] {\n  ACTION search_web(target=deal, category=cat_limited_time_offers) -> deals : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  RETURN deals\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "Existing search-value category expresses the actionable category filter; this proposal is irrelevant to this item."}, {"item_id": "b49f88ac-b407-41af-a9e7-f5e4cd1f970a", "source": "Mind2Web (osunlp/Mind2Web, train, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Check the rating and user reviews for the game \"Deathloop\".", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT CheckDeathloopReviews\nTASK CheckDeathloopReviews : STRING {\n  ACTION search_web(target=deathloop) -> results : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION extract(target=results, limit=1) -> game : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION read_page(target=game, content=\"rating and user reviews\") -> reviews : STRING\n  RETURN reviews\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The search/read sequence is expressible, but the requested page fields remain a prose content selector rather than a defined metric/review category."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190912_052310_164968#2", "source": "ALFRED (json_2.1.0, train)", "nl": "To move a full roll of toilet paper and an empty roll to the counter.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT MoveToiletPaperRolls\nTASK MoveToiletPaperRolls {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=toilet_paper, state=state_full) -> full_roll : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=full_roll, destination=counter)\n  ACTION pick_up(target=toilet_paper, state=state_empty) -> empty_roll : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=empty_roll, destination=counter)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "state-value and the pick_up wiring make full and empty selection expressible through the category's open atomic-symbol rule."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190919_003451_692296#1", "source": "ALFRED (json_2.1.0, train)", "nl": "Move a sponge and bowl from a counter to a cupboard", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT MoveSpongeAndBowl\nTASK MoveSpongeAndBowl {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=sponge, source=counter) -> sponge : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=sponge, destination=cupboard)\n  ACTION pick_up(target=bowl, source=counter) -> bowl : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=bowl, destination=cupboard)\n  ACTION close_container(target=cupboard)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "No proposed change is needed; existing household actions cover the goal."}, {"item_id": "sphinx-doc__sphinx-8035", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified (princeton-nlp/SWE-bench_Verified, test, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Support defining specific :private-members: for autodoc.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT SupportPrivateMembers\nTASK SupportPrivateMembers {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=autodoc, file=\"sphinx/ext/autodoc/__init__.py\", actual_output=\"private-members documents all private members and accepts no selected members\", expected_output=\"private-members accepts selected member arguments like members\", content=\"support selected private-members\")\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "modify_code gives an action shape, but file, actual_output, expected_output, and content remain prose STRING channels with only future category names."}, {"item_id": "sphinx-doc__sphinx-7462", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified (princeton-nlp/SWE-bench_Verified, test, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "IndexError: pop from empty list for empty tuple type annotation.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FixEmptyTupleAnnotation\nTASK FixEmptyTupleAnnotation {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=sphinx, file=\"sphinx/domains/python.py\", reproduction_step=\"render Tuple[()] annotation\", actual_output=\"IndexError: pop from empty list\", expected_output=\"empty tuple annotation renders without error\")\n  ACTION modify_code(target=sphinx, file=\"sphinx/pycode/ast.py\", content=\"support empty tuple annotation parsing\")\n  ACTION run_tests(target=sphinx, file=\"docs/requirements.txt\")\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The sequence is captured, but every software-specific value is still an opaque STRING payload and does not realize N3."}, {"item_id": "c3312", "source": 