The question speech act is captured, but its geopolitical proposition remains prose."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-149175", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns)", "nl": "Write 10 funny tweets about how I found these two quahogs on the beach this afternoon", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT WriteFunnyQuahogTweets\nTASK WriteFunnyQuahogTweets : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_short_text, content=\"funny tweets about finding two quahogs on a beach this afternoon\", quantity=10, style=style_catchy, tone=tone_casual) -> tweets : STRING\n  RETURN tweets\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "quantity, style, tone, and artifact target are structured, but tweet form, humor, quahogs, beach, and event content remain prose."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-30995", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns)", "nl": "Add novel and useful ideas to my mental-health presentation script and send it to me.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ReviseMentalHealthPresentation\nTASK ReviseMentalHealthPresentation : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_structured_report, content=\"revise the supplied mental-health presentation script by adding novel and useful ideas\", audience=role_user, style=style_persuasive) -> presentation : STRING\n  RETURN presentation\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Generation and audience are represented, but supplied text, requested revisions, novelty, usefulness, and presentation structure are opaque content."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-69869", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns)", "nl": "Create personalities, dynamics, roles, appearances, and relationships for the listed fictional characters with Trinidad Osborn.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT CreateCharacterProfiles\nTASK CreateCharacterProfiles : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_character_profile, content=\"create personalities, dynamics, roles, appearances, and relationships for the supplied fictional-character ensemble and Trinidad Osborn\", style=style_narrative) -> profiles : STRING\n  RETURN profiles\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "artifact target and style are available, but the character list and all requested relationship details remain prose."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-65289", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns)", "nl": "Write a detailed, very long scene in which Chandler Hallow learns during filming that his wife and child died.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT WriteGriefScene\nTASK WriteGriefScene : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_story, content=\"detailed scene during filming where Chandler Hallow learns his wife and child died; depict hysteria and horror\", quantity=10000, style=style_narrative) -> scene : STRING\n  RETURN scene\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "A numeric quantity can approximate length, but scene events, people, emotional constraints, and the requested maximum length remain prose."}, {"item_id": "1775938591749", "source": "ThoughtTrace (SCAI-JHU/ThoughtTrace, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Please define literary fiction.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT DefineLiteraryFiction\nCONVO DefineLiteraryFiction {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"Define literary fiction\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The late-turn conversational ask is captured, but the term and definition request are content prose."}, {"item_id": "1775498956373", "source": "ThoughtTrace (SCAI-JHU/ThoughtTrace, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "I think this will really helped a lot because you did show me how to respond in a polite manner", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ThankForCoworkerScript\nCONVO ThankForCoworkerScript {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER acknowledge(content=\"The polite response script for a difficult coworker was helpful\", recipient=role_agent, tone=tone_polite)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Acknowledgement and tone are structured, but the underlying coworker-script subject remains prose."}, {"item_id": "1775791789755", "source": "ThoughtTrace (SCAI-JHU/ThoughtTrace, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "I woke up early, had coffee, and now I’m juggling a few things, finishing a report, preparing slides for tomorrow’s meeting, and squeezing in some exercise before dinner. I also need to figure out what to cook tonight that’s quick but healthy.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PlanWorkday\nCONVO PlanWorkday {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"Prioritize finishing a report, preparing tomorrow's meeting slides, exercising before dinner, and choosing a quick healthy dinner\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The request is represented as an ask, but tasks, temporal constraints, health criterion, and meal request remain content prose."}, {"item_id": "1775940921302", "source": "ThoughtTrace (SCAI-JHU/ThoughtTrace, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "The meal would be dinner for 4 people, I have 2 hours and no one has allergies. I have pork chops rice and baked beans on hand.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PlanPorkChopDinner\nCONVO PlanPorkChopDinner {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER inform(content=\"Plan dinner for four within two hours using pork chops, rice, and baked beans; no allergies\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The interaction act is available, but meal, ingredients, allergy state, and time constraint have no dedicated value categories."}]
