Shaper proposal: {"summary": "This increment makes itinerary constraints semantically typed, corrects canonical examples, explicitly records remaining STRING-governed attributes as N3 build-phase violations, and adds canonical routing/decomposition rules. It also repairs the residual descriptive-value category and makes full/empty object state canonical.", "note_position": "comply", "note_argument": "Every newly governed attribute value in this increment is constrained to a named glossary category, a defined literal form, a list thereof, or a typed binding. Remaining STRING channels are explicitly identified as unresolved N3 build-phase violations rather than described as governed value sets.", "foundations_overview": "BrainCode remains a typed context-free request language with explicit Bind-mediated composition. Canonical translation now routes a request to TASK when it requests an executable external action or deterministic workflow, to CONVO only when its source meaning is a speaker-attributed conversational turn or turn sequence, and to GENERATE when its sole requested result is a pure artifact; a request to generate and then deliver an artifact is a TASK containing GENERATE followed by the delivery Action. Closed-task decomposition emits prerequisite status checks immediately before the first branch that consumes them, in source-condition order; order-status checks target order, buyer-status checks target customer, and remedial support actions target order. A GENERATE producing one artifact has result type STRING, while one requested as a collection of independently usable artifacts has result type LIST[STRING].", "rebuttals": [], "changes": [{"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Action", "grammar": "action ::= \"ACTION\" operation-id \"(\" action-attrs? \")\" (\"->\" IDENT \":\" type)?\naction-attrs ::= action-attr (\",\" action-attr)*\naction-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value\n-- Each operation admits only its signature-listed attributes; target is first when present and remaining attributes are alphabetical.", "semantics": "An Action attribute is valid only when it is listed by the operation signature and its value has the governing category or literal form named by attribute-name; a category value may be a category symbol, a typed binding holding one, or a homogeneous list when that attribute permits LIST[STRING]. STRING remains accepted only for attributes explicitly marked as unresolved N3 build-phase violations in attribute-name. For search_web, target is required and optional attributes are emitted alphabetically. For support workflows, check_support_status uses target=order for order metrics and target=customer for buyer metrics; offer_discount and offer_expedited_shipping use target=order.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Find the lowest-priced gray round mirror in stock in Atlanta, under $20.", "braincode": "ACTION search_web(target=mirror, availability=avail_in_stock, color=color_gray, currency=curr_usd, location=atlanta, max_price=20, shape=shape_round) -> mirrors : LIST[REF[STRING]]\nACTION sort(target=mirrors, rank_direction=dir_asc, rank_field=rank_price) -> sorted_mirrors : LIST[REF[STRING]]"}, "glossary_gloss": "Action performs one external operation using only the attributes allowed for that operation. Attribute values must come from their named glossary value sets or their defined literal forms.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "This makes Action's attribute gate enforce the N3 distinction between governed symbolic values and still-open build-phase STRING violations, while repairing the normative canonical-order example.", "cites_source": "Why Agentic Systems Need Ontologies", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Generate", "grammar": "generation ::= \"GENERATE\" \"(\" generate-attr (\",\" generate-attr)* \")\" \"->\" IDENT \":\" gen_type\ngenerate-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value\n-- Legal attributes: target, audience, content, duration, duration_unit, format, locale, quantity, style, tone, stop_min_per_day, stop_requirement, max_walk_duration, max_walk_duration_unit.", "semantics": "GENERATE target is artifact-value; audience is recipient-value; tone, format, style, locale, and duration units use their corresponding value categories; numeric constraints use NUMBER. stop_requirement is an entity-name symbol, an entity-name-compatible typed binding, or a LIST[STRING] of such symbols, and identifies what each daily minimum counts. stop_min_per_day applies to each calendar day represented by the generated itinerary. max_walk_duration with max_walk_duration_unit bounds travel time between each pair of consecutive itinerary stops. target is first and all optional attributes follow alphabetically. content remains a STRING only as an explicitly unresolved N3 build-phase violation. A single requested artifact returns STRING; independently usable multiple artifacts return LIST[STRING].", "worked_example": {"nl": "Plan a 3-day Kyoto itinerary with at least one temple per day and no more than a 20-minute walk between consecutive stops.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PlanKyotoItinerary\nTASK PlanKyotoItinerary : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_itinerary, content=\"Kyoto itinerary\", duration=3, duration_unit=unit_day, max_walk_duration=20, max_walk_duration_unit=unit_minute, stop_min_per_day=1, stop_requirement=temple) -> plan : STRING\n  RETURN plan\n}"}, "glossary_gloss": "Generate creates a pure artifact with typed output and structured constraints. An itinerary minimum can now say both how many stops are needed and what kind of stop qualifies.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "The prior numeric minimum lost the required temple qualifier. Reusing entity-name provides a typed existing category rather than adding an unnecessary itinerary-only value primitive.", "cites_source": "HTML", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Utterance", "grammar": "utterance ::= \"UTTER\" speech-act \"(\" utter-attr (\",\" utter-attr)* \")\" (\"->\" IDENT)?\nspeech-act ::= operation-vocabulary member\nutter-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value", "semantics": "Only audience, content, recipient, target, and tone are legal UTTER attributes and they must be alphabetical. recipient and audience require recipient-value, tone requires tone-value, and target requires its attribute-name governing category. content remains a transitional STRING payload and an explicit unresolved N3 build-phase violation; it is not a glossary value set. A bound UTTER result has type STRING and must use content, content_2, content_3, and so on.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Ask the manager politely for a status update.", "braincode": "CONVO StatusRequest {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"status update\", recipient=role_manager, tone=tone_polite)\n  }\n}"}, "glossary_gloss": "Utterance records a speech act in a conversation turn. Its recipient and tone use glossary symbols, while content is still explicitly tracked as a temporary build-phase text channel.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Utterance already uses governed metadata, but its semantics must not imply that transitional content STRING is compliant with N3.", "cites_source": "Why Agentic Systems Need Ontologies", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "attribute-name", "glossary_gloss": "This is the index of legal attribute names and the exact current category or literal rule for each attribute. An attribute marked N3 violation still accepts STRING during the build phase, but its listed replacement category is a required next step rather than a present governing value set.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "target", "gloss": "Action subject: entity-name; Generate artifact: artifact-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "recipient", "gloss": "Message recipient from recipient-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "audience", "gloss": "Artifact audience from recipient-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "tone", "gloss": "Tone from tone-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "format", "gloss": "Output form from format-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "style", "gloss": "Production style from style-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "locale", "gloss": "Locale from locale-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "duration_unit", "gloss": "Duration unit from duration-unit-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "max_walk_duration_unit", "gloss": "Walking-duration unit from duration-unit-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "currency", "gloss": "Currency from currency-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "state", "gloss": "Object condition from state-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "shape", "gloss": "Object shape from shape-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "color", "gloss": "Product color from product-attribute-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "size", "gloss": "Product size from product-attribute-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "gender", "gloss": "Product demographic facet from product-attribute-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "metric", "gloss": "Queryable status from metric-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "relation", "gloss": "Placement relation from spatial-relation.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "destination", "gloss": "Destination from entity-name or location-name.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "source", "gloss": "Source from entity-name or location-name.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "origin", "gloss": "Travel origin from location-name.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "location", "gloss": "Location from location-name.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "stop_requirement", "gloss": "Required itinerary-stop class from entity-name.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "quantity", "gloss": "Count as NUMBER.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "duration", "gloss": "Duration magnitude as NUMBER.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "stop_min_per_day", "gloss": "Daily minimum count as NUMBER.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "max_walk_duration", "gloss": "Consecutive-stop walking bound as NUMBER.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "file", "gloss": "N3 violation: STRING pending code-path-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "method", "gloss": "N3 violation: STRING pending code-symbol-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "property", "gloss": "N3 violation: STRING pending code-symbol-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "call", "gloss": "N3 violation: STRING pending code-call-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "assertion", "gloss": "N3 violation: STRING pending code-assertion-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "expected_output", "gloss": "N3 violation: STRING pending code-outcome-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "actual_output", "gloss": "N3 violation: STRING pending code-outcome-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "reproduction_step", "gloss": "N3 violation: STRING pending code-repro-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "revision", "gloss": "N3 violation: STRING pending code-change-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "procedure", "gloss": "N3 violation: STRING pending procedure-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "food", "gloss": "N3 violation: STRING pending food-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "meal", "gloss": "N3 violation: STRING pending meal-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "message_structure", "gloss": "N3 violation: STRING pending message-structure-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "content", "gloss": "N3 violation: STRING pending symbolic message-content-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "policy", "gloss": "N3 violation: STRING pending policy-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "amenity", "gloss": "N3 violation: STRING pending amenity-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "ticket", "gloss": "N3 violation: STRING pending ticket-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "seat", "gloss": "N3 violation: STRING pending seat-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "All other existing listed attributes retain their current explicitly named category or literal rule: dates use ISO_DATE, deadlines/showtimes use UTC_TIMESTAMP, booleans use BOOL, numeric bounds use NUMBER, search fields use search-value, platform uses platform-name, and itinerary/route are LIST[STRING] of entity-name or location-name symbols. No STRING-governed member is N3-compliant; every such member must name a concrete replacement category.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Require one temple per day on an itinerary.", "braincode": "GENERATE(target=art_itinerary, stop_min_per_day=1, stop_requirement=temple) -> itinerary : STRING"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "The previous wording incorrectly treated planned categories as current value sets. This revision separates actual governed values from named, concrete N3 remediation work and adds the missing itinerary qualifier attribute.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "state-value", "glossary_gloss": "State-value gives canonical symbols for an object's condition when an Action needs to select or assert that condition. Full and empty are distinct, explicit states rather than inferred variants.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "state_warm", "gloss": "Warm or heated condition.", "nl_synonyms": ["warm", "hot"]}, {"symbol": "state_cold", "gloss": "Cold or chilled condition.", "nl_synonyms": ["cold", "chilled"]}, {"symbol": "state_microwaved", "gloss": "Has been microwaved.", "nl_synonyms": ["microwaved"]}, {"symbol": "state_clean", "gloss": "Clean condition.", "nl_synonyms": ["clean"]}, {"symbol": "state_dirty", "gloss": "Dirty condition.", "nl_synonyms": ["dirty"]}, {"symbol": "state_full", "gloss": "Contains its intended material or remaining usable amount.", "nl_synonyms": ["full", "filled"]}, {"symbol": "state_empty", "gloss": "Contains no intended material or usable remaining amount.", "nl_synonyms": ["empty", "used up"]}], "membership_rule": "An atomic symbol matching state_[a-z_]+ naming an object condition. New states are added as glossary members and are never free text.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Move a full roll and an empty roll of toilet paper to the counter.", "braincode": "ACTION pick_up(target=toilet_paper, state=state_full) -> full_roll : REF[STRING]\nACTION place(target=full_roll, destination=counter)\nACTION pick_up(target=toilet_paper, state=state_empty) -> empty_roll : REF[STRING]\nACTION place(target=empty_roll, destination=counter)"}, "change_type": "MINOR", "rationale": "The sampled household task requires stable canonical encodings for full and empty; relying only on an open prefix rule weakens lookup and synonym determinism.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "descriptive-value", "glossary_gloss": "Descriptive-value is only a residual category for entity modifiers and genuinely unclassified domain concepts. It does not contain states, tones, roles, currencies, artifact types, units, styles, locales, or metrics because each has its own category.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "mod_mixed_case", "gloss": "Mixed-case modifier.", "nl_synonyms": ["mixed case"]}, {"symbol": "dom_safari", "gloss": "Safari domain concept.", "nl_synonyms": ["safari"]}, {"symbol": "dom_pain", "gloss": "Pain domain concept.", "nl_synonyms": ["pain"]}, {"symbol": "dom_ovr", "gloss": "One-versus-rest domain concept.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "dom_sgi", "gloss": "SGI domain concept.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "Members use mod_ for an entity modifier or dom_ for a domain concept not yet assigned a dedicated category. state_, style_, locale_, metric_, role_, tone_, curr_, art_, and unit_ are invalid here and must use their dedicated categories.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Generate a narrative safari plan.", "braincode": "GENERATE(target=art_plan, content=\"safari\", style=style_narrative) -> plan : STRING"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "This replaces, rather than duplicates, the existing category and removes its obsolete state-inclusive interpretation now that state-value governs state symbols.", "addresses_note": "N3"}], "_provider_used": "openai", "_model_used": "gpt-5.6-terra"}
Critic assessment: {"decision": "needs-rework", "kpi_assessment": {"coverage": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Structured itinerary constraints and explicit full/empty states improve coverage for the Kyoto and household items. However, the revised Action rule describes target as category-governed/entity-name while its own examples use REF and LIST[REF[STRING]] bindings as targets; read literally, this rejects ordinary follow-on actions such as place(target=full_roll) and sort(target=mirrors), reducing existing closed-task coverage."}, "expressivity": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "stop_requirement plus defined consecutive-stop walking scope preserves the formerly lost \"one temple per day\" qualifier, and state_full/state_empty preserve a real household distinction. But compatibility with a selected motherboard remains unrepresentable, and STRING-bound values can still be passed as purported category values without a defined provenance rule."}, "determinism": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "The repaired attribute-order examples and stated TASK/CONVO/GENERATE routing rules improve canonicalization. Yet target has incompatible readings across the proposed Action semantics, attribute-name vocabulary, and worked examples, while category symbols and arbitrary STRING bindings share static type STRING; translators cannot deterministically decide whether a binding is eligible as an entity/category value."}, "interpretability": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "The proposal clearly labels remaining STRING channels as N3 violations rather than falsely calling them governed sets, and the new itinerary fields are readable. Conversely, terms such as \"entity-name-compatible typed binding\" and the operational meaning of category-valid bindings are undefined, while the target rule cannot explain the proposal's own sort/place examples."}, "improvement": {"impact": "benefit", "reasoning": "A weaker executor gains useful structure from explicit temple-per-day and walking-between-consecutive-stops constraints, state_full/state_empty, and the routing/decomposition guidance. These improvements are meaningful even though Action target typing must be repaired before the full planning benefit is reliable."}}, "simulations": [{"item_id": "dev-embodied-2", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "Put both pillows from the sofa onto the armchair, one at a time.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PlacePillows\nTASK PlacePillows {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=pillow, source=sofa) -> pillow_1 : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=pillow_1, destination=armchair, relation=on)\n  ACTION pick_up(target=pillow, source=sofa) -> pillow_2 : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=pillow_2, destination=armchair, relation=on)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "state-value is irrelevant. The expression exposes the Action target contradiction: place must accept the REF binding pillow_1/pillow_2, not only entity-name."}, {"item_id": "dev-email-2", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "If my manager hasn't replied by Friday, send a polite follow-up; otherwise do nothing.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FollowUpManager\nTASK FollowUpManager CONTEXT execution_date=\"2025-06-03\" {\n  ACTION check_replied(target=role_manager, deadline=\"2025-06-06T23:59:59Z\") -> replied : BOOL\n  IF NOT replied THEN {\n    ACTION send_email(recipient=role_manager, tone=tone_polite, content=\"follow-up\")\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Recipient, tone, condition, and deadline are structured, but content remains the explicitly unresolved STRING channel and therefore violates N3."}, {"item_id": "e344b89e-767a-4618-ba82-4b81cdcba280", "source": "Mind2Web", "nl": "add a motherboard under $200 and a compatible processor at any price to the shopping cart.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT AddCompatibleParts\nTASK AddCompatibleParts {\n  ACTION search_web(target=motherboard, currency=curr_usd, max_price=200) -> motherboards : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION extract(target=motherboards, limit=1) -> motherboard_pick : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION add_to_cart(target=motherboard_pick)\n  ACTION search_web(target=processor) -> processors : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION check_support_status(target=processor, metric=metric_compatibility) -> compatible : BOOL\n  IF compatible THEN {\n    ACTION extract(target=processors, limit=1) -> processor_pick : REF[STRING]\n    ACTION add_to_cart(target=processor_pick)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The price constraint is structured, but metric_compatibility cannot state compatibility with motherboard_pick. The Action target rule also conflicts with the list/ref targets used by extract and add_to_cart."}, {"item_id": "f118238f-ef8f-4b63-9159-a81e981ef46e", "source": "Mind2Web", "nl": "Add decorative LED Candles to the cart.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT AddCandles\nTASK AddCandles {\n  ACTION search_web(target=decorative_led_candles) -> candles : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION extract(target=candles, limit=1) -> candle : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION add_to_cart(target=candle)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The object is in entity-name. This still relies on the intended, but not coherently specified, acceptance of list/ref targets by Action operations."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190906_214148_552057#1", "source": "ALFRED", "nl": "get a cup ready for coffee", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT GetCupReady\nTASK GetCupReady {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=cup, source=refrigerator) -> cup_1 : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION heat(target=cup_1)\n  ACTION place(target=cup_1, destination=coffee_maker, relation=under)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The task is expressible using existing operations and spatial relation. The action target defect remains relevant because heat/place consume a REF binding."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190908_102045_139402#1", "source": "ALFRED", "nl": "To put the toilet paper away.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PutAwayToiletPaper\nTASK PutAwayToiletPaper {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=toilet_paper, source=toilet) -> roll : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=roll, destination=holder, location=wall, relation=on)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "Existing entity and spatial categories cover the actionable core. As above, place(target=roll) requires a REF-compatible target rule."}, {"item_id": "sympy__sympy-15345", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified", "nl": "mathematica_code gives wrong output with Max: mathematica_code(Max(x,2)) should output Max[x,2] but outputs Max(2, x).", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FixMathematicaCode\nTASK FixMathematicaCode {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=mathematica_code, file=\"sympy/printing/mathematica.py\", method=\"mathematica_code\", assertion=\"mathematica_code(Max(x,2))\", expected_output=\"Max[x,2]\", actual_output=\"Max(2, x)\")\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The code path, symbol, assertion, and outcomes all use attribute-name members explicitly labelled unresolved N3 STRING violations. The proposal correctly exposes, but does not cure, this gap."}, {"item_id": "django__django-15098", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified", "nl": "Django i18n_patterns does not support locales containing script and region, such as en-Latn-US; update it so these routes resolve successfully.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FixLocalePattern\nTASK FixLocalePattern {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=django, file=\"django/utils/translation/trans_real.py\", method=\"i18n_patterns\", reproduction_step=\"configure en-latn-us and en-Latn-US routes\", expected_output=\"200 U! for script-and-region locale routes\", actual_output=\"404 not found for script-and-region locale routes\")\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The core fix is representable only through the still-untyped STRING code attributes. No symbolic category yet captures locale-tag behavior, reproduction, expected result, or actual result."}, {"item_id": "c5957", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "thanks how long will this take me to make?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FlatbreadDuration\nCONVO FlatbreadDuration {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"how long will the high-protein flatbread recipe take to make\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The conversational speech act and recipient are structured, but the recipe referent and requested duration remain prose content. Under N4's override, this is not an acceptable final fallback."}, {"item_id": "c436", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "And could you suggest some pintoresque towns nearby?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT BilbaoNearbyTowns\nCONVO BilbaoNearbyTowns {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"suggest picturesque towns near Bilbao\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Conversation form is captured, but the geographic relation, town class, and recommendation substance remain in transitional content."}, {"item_id": "c996", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "Do you think you will fall in love?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT AskAboutAILove\nCONVO AskAboutAILove {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"whether the assistant will fall in love\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "UTTER captures the question-directed-to-agent structure, but the proposition is a STRING content payload."}, {"item_id": "c4939", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "How did marriage come to the world", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT AskMarriageOrigins\nCONVO AskMarriageOrigins {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"how marriage originated\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The request is structurally a question, but its semantic subject and historical-explanation request are not symbolically represented."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-129421", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "Continue with more details about how linear algebra is applied in ChatGPT-style language models.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ExplainLLMLinearAlgebra\nTASK ExplainLLMLinearAlgebra : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_technical_explanation, audience=role_user, content=\"continue with more detailed explanation of linear algebra in ChatGPT-style language models, with concrete examples\", locale=locale_en_us, style=style_technical, tone=tone_casual) -> explanation : STRING\n  RETURN explanation\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Artifact type, audience, locale, style, and tone are governed values, but the required technical subject, depth, continuity, and examples remain STRING content. The independent translations diverged sharply between GAP and a similar GENERATE form."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-148973", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "The gang attends a school run by Billy Dee Williams that teaches people how to be cool, which is plagued by a pterodactyl.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT GenerateComedyScript\nTASK GenerateComedyScript : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_script, audience=role_user, content=\"continue the Scooby gang comedy script: school run by Billy Dee Williams teaches coolness and is plagued by a pterodactyl\", style=style_narrative) -> script : STRING\n  RETURN script\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The requested artifact and narrative style are structured, but characters, setting, scenario, continuation relation, and comedic substance are prose content."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-142592", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "Please write steps for homiletics and engaging Christian sermons.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT GenerateHomileticsSteps\nTASK GenerateHomileticsSteps : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_structured_report, audience=role_user, content=\"steps for homiletics and engaging Christian sermons\", format=format_numbered_list) -> guide : STRING\n  RETURN guide\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The numbered structured-artifact request is represented, but the homiletics subject and engagement constraint remain content STRING."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-22638", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "next response", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT CollaborationEmailReply\nCONVO CollaborationEmailReply {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"write the recipient's next response to the collaboration-introduction email\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The request is clearly conversational and refers to prior turn context, but the intended email-response content and source-message linkage have no symbolic representation."}, {"item_id": "1775955172098", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "My budget is 1 million Chilean pesos.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ReviseItalyBudget\nCONVO ReviseItalyBudget {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER inform(content=\"revise the one-week architecture-focused Italy itinerary for a budget of 1000000 Chilean pesos\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The amount is embedded in content because no budget attribute or Chilean-peso currency symbol/category is supplied for this conversational itinerary revision. This is a missing structured constraint category, not merely open prose substance."}, {"item_id": "1775612391896", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "The 'Job Hunt Tracker' actually sounds perfect since I'm starting to apply for internships next month. I like the idea of adding a 'Status' field. But how should I handle the 'Update' part in React? Like, when I click 'Edit', should it open a new page or a modal?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT AskReactUpdateDesign\nCONVO AskReactUpdateDesign {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"for a React and Node job-hunt tracker, compare modal versus new-page design for editing an application status\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The turn and question act are present, but software concepts, alternatives, and evaluation criteria remain content STRING."}, {"item_id": "1775448065619", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "I am looking for a way to save time and eat better.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ReviseMealPrep\nCONVO ReviseMealPrep {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER inform(content=\"revise the high-protein three-day meal-prep plan to save time and improve eating\", recipi