resses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Action", "grammar": "action ::= \"ACTION\" operation-id \"(\" action-attrs? \")\" (\"->\" IDENT \":\" type)?\naction-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value\n-- target is first when present; remaining attributes are alphabetical.\n-- Target domains: selector operations (search_web, pick_up, browse_trending) accept entity-name; list operations (sort, extract) accept LIST[REF[STRING]]; selected-object operations (place, heat, chill, rinse, slice, pour, add_to_cart) accept REF[STRING]; check_replied accepts recipient-value; check_support_status accepts entity-name or REF[STRING]; code operations accept platform-name or entity-name; other signatures state their named target category.", "semantics": "Each Action accepts only signature-listed attributes whose values satisfy attribute-name's governing domain and provenance rule. Target is operation-specific: search_web and pick_up select an entity-name; sort and extract consume LIST[REF[STRING]]; place, heat, chill, rinse, slice, pour, and add_to_cart consume a selected REF[STRING]; check_replied consumes recipient-value; check_support_status consumes an entity-name or selected REF[STRING]. search_web additionally permits compatible_with=REF[STRING], meaning every returned candidate is compatible with that selected reference; compatible_with follows target and precedes other optional attributes alphabetically. STRING remains valid only for attributes explicitly marked unresolved N3 build-phase violations.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Add a motherboard under $200 and a compatible processor to the cart.", "braincode": "ACTION search_web(target=motherboard, currency=curr_usd, max_price=200) -> motherboards : LIST[REF[STRING]]\nACTION extract(target=motherboards, limit=1) -> motherboard_pick : REF[STRING]\nACTION add_to_cart(target=motherboard_pick)\nACTION search_web(target=processor, compatible_with=motherboard_pick) -> processors : LIST[REF[STRING]]\nACTION extract(target=