l_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "All existing members retain their current stated domains. Attributes not listed as unresolved N3 violations must name a category, typed reference domain, NUMBER, BOOL, ISO_DATE, UTC_TIMESTAMP, or another glossary-defined literal rule; STRING alone is never a governed category domain.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Search for processors compatible with the selected motherboard.", "braincode": "ACTION search_web(target=processor, compatible_with=motherboard_pick) -> processors : LIST[REF[STRING]]"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "This corrects the false claim that all Action targets are entity-name values and adds explicit governed entries for compatibility and budget.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Generate", "grammar": "generation ::= \"GENERATE\" \"(\" generate-attr (\",\" generate-attr)* \")\" \"->\" IDENT \":\" gen_type\n-- Legal attributes: target, audience, budget, content, currency, duration, duration_unit, format, locale, quantity, style, tone, stop_min_per_day, stop_requirement, max_walk_duration, max_walk_duration_unit.", "semantics": "GENERATE target requires artifact-value; audience requires recipient-value; tone, format, style, locale, currency, and duration units require their named categories; numeric constraints including budget require NUMBER. budget is the maximum total monetary cost in currency. stop_requirement accepts an entity-name symbol, semantic-category-value symbol, a provenance-valid binding in either category, or a homogeneous LIST[STRING] retaining one of those provenances. stop_min_per_day counts only stops matching stop_requirement. max_walk_duration bounds each consecutive pair of stops. target is first and optional attributes follow alphabetically. content remains an explicitly unresolved build-phase STRING channel.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Plan a three-day Kyoto itinerary with one temple per day, a 20-minute walking limit, and a $1,000 budget.", "braincode