Critic's decision: needs-rework
Critic's reasoning: The bundle substantively addresses every prior required change: it introduces provenance, operation-specific target domains, compatibility filtering, and structured budgets. Those are net-positive for coverage and agent planning, but the provenance-union mechanism, class-category overlap, and incomplete Action signature table leave the revised language logically underspecified. The two vocabulary additions are independently sound and can land now; the dependent construct revisions need the listed repairs before acceptance.
Required changes (address every one explicitly): [{"target": "Types & Lexicon", "change": "Define a concrete grammar and static-checking syntax for provenance-qualified bindings and finite provenance unions, or remove union acceptance until it has such syntax. Specify how provenance is assigned to direct symbols, retained through LET, list literals, Action/Generate results, parameters, and task-call results; an unannotated STRING must never acquire provenance."}, {"target": "Action", "change": "Publish a complete normative signature table for every existing operation, including legal attributes, required/optional status, each attribute domain, result type/provenance, and canonical order. Replace the non-normative statement that unspecified operations 'state their named target category'; it currently leaves heat, slice, rinse, place, modify_code, run_tests, and existing search operations underspecified."}, {"target": "semantic-category-value", "change": "Eliminate the overlap with entity-name or define a non-overlapping boundary. The current entity-name rule already defines class-like nouns such as temple, while semantic-category-value also defines class_temple; specify one canonical category and encoding rule for generic classes versus concrete named entities, then revise all itinerary examples consistently."}, {"target": "attribute-name", "change": "Add individually indexed entries and exact domains for every remaining attribute used by all constructs and Action signatures, including max_price, min_rating, rank_field, rank_direction, limit, availability, genre, category, platform, deadline, date, and all code-operation attributes. Mark only deliberately transitional STRING attributes as N3 violations and name their replacement category."}, {"target": "Generate", "change": "Define quantity's measurement semantics or add a governed unit/value mechanism for output length. In particular, state how an exact word-count requirement is encoded so quantity=100 cannot ambiguously mean characters, sections, items, or words."}, {"target": "basis", "change": "Continue the N3 build by replacing the remaining STRING-governed attribute channels with named glossary categories, starting with code-path/code-symbol/code-change/test-assertion values and symbolic message/artifact content. Retaining them for build-phase coverage is permitted, but they must remain explicitly tracked as unresolved violations."}]
Logic issues: ["The proposal permits a finite provenance union but supplies neither a type grammar nor an annotation form for declaring one, so two translators cannot know how to encode or validate a union-valued binding.", "semantic-category-value duplicates entity-name for generic classes: entity-name is already defined as a discrete entity class, while class_temple is also a temple class. The same stop requirement consequently has two category-valid encodings.", "The Action revision says every signature-listed attribute is validated but does not actually provide complete signatures for most retained operations. The phrase 'other signatures state their named target category' is undefined normative behavior rather than a signature.", "The revised attribute-name category says existing members retain their domains, but N3 requires every attribute to have an exact listed value domain. Important existing attributes and code-operation fields remain only partially indexed or explicitly STRING-governed.", "The proposed 100-word generation cannot be expressed precisely: quantity=100 has no unit or output-length semantics."]
Pre-KPI assessment: {"coverage": {"impact": "benefit", "reasoning": "Operation-specific targets preserve previously difficult selected-object pipelines: add_to_cart can consume a selected reference, sort/extract can consume lists, and compatible_with preserves the motherboard/processor dependency. Structured budget, currency, and itinerary-stop constraints improve coverage for the exposed planning requests, although software and prose-content attributes remain transitional STRING channels."}, "expressivity": {"impact": "benefit", "reasoning": "The proposal adds previously missing structured meaning for compatibility, monetary budgets, currency, stop classes, and revision of itinerary budget constraints. The simulations still require prose STRING payloads for code details and open-content requests, so the improvement is real but incomplete under N3/N4."}, "determinism": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Canonical target-first/alphabetical attribute ordering and provenance validation improve convergence for Action and Generate. However, provenance unions are permitted without a grammar for declaring them, entity-name and semantic-category-value overlap on generic classes such as temple, and most Action signatures remain referenced rather than exhaustively specified; translators therefore still have multiple plausible encodings."}, "interpretability": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "A reader can now distinguish a named entity selector, selected REF, and list-of-REF target in important shopping and embodied pipelines. But the new static provenance system is underspecified syntactically, and the semantic-category-value category duplicates the current entity-name definition of class-like nouns, making category choice difficult to recover reliably."}, "improvement": {"impact": "benefit", "reasoning": "The structured shopping and itinerary expressions give a weaker agent useful executable constraints that prose content or an unqualified compatibility metric would hide. This is especially clear in the processor-compatible-with-selected-motherboard and Chilean-peso budget cases."}}
Simulated examples that exposed gaps: [{"item_id": "dev-embodied-2", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "Put both pillows from the sofa onto the armchair, one at a time.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT MovePillows\nTASK MovePillows {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=pillow, source=sofa) -> pillow_1 : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=pillow_1, destination=armchair, relation=on)\n  ACTION pick_up(target=pillow, source=sofa) -> pillow_2 : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=pillow_2, destination=armchair, relation=on)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The revised Action target domains help: pick_up selects entity-name and place consumes REF[STRING]. The exact necessity of relation=on remains a canonicalization question."}, {"item_id": "dev-embodied-1", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "Rinse the mug in the sink, then put it in the coffee maker.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT RinseThenPlace\nTASK RinseThenPlace {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=mug) -> mug_ref : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION rinse(target=mug_ref, destination=sink)\n  ACTION place(target=mug_ref, destination=coffee_maker, relation=in)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "Selected-object target validation is directly useful for rinse and place."}, {"item_id": "86afd67c-1bff-455c-baa7-e18dcb64b0f3", "source": "Mind2Web", "nl": "Find comedy tv shows on netflix sorted by audience score.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FindComedyShows\nTASK FindComedyShows : LIST[REF[STRING]] {\n  ACTION search_web(target=tv_show, genre=genre_comedy, platform=netflix) -> tv_shows : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION sort(target=tv_shows, rank_direction=dir_desc, rank_field=rank_rating) -> sorted_tv_shows : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  RETURN sorted_tv_shows\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The list target for sort is covered. rank_rating is the available proxy for audience score; a dedicated audience-score ranking distinction would be needed if that distinction matters."}, {"item_id": "bf469f30-6628-4017-b963-672645d7feab", "source": "Mind2Web", "nl": "Find the highest rated dog collar under 10 dollar.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FindDogCollar\nTASK FindDogCollar : LIST[REF[STRING]] {\n  ACTION search_web(target=dog_collar, currency=curr_usd, max_price=10) -> collars : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION sort(target=collars, rank_direction=dir_desc, rank_field=rank_rating) -> sorted_collars : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  RETURN sorted_collars\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "Currency and numeric maximum are governed. The proposal's operation-specific list target makes the sorting stage well typed."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190907_223758_523581#1", "source": "ALFRED", "nl": "Microwave a slice of apple and place it on the table.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT MicrowaveApple\nTASK MicrowaveApple {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=apple) -> apple_ref : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION slice(target=apple_ref) -> apple_slice : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION heat(target=apple_slice, destination=microwave) -> heated_slice : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=heated_slice, destination=table, relation=on)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The proposed selected-object domains support slice, heat, and place. The complete return and optional-attribute signature of heat must still be stated normatively."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190908_224836_919680#2", "source": "ALFRED", "nl": "Put a microwaved slice of apple on the table in the corner.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PutMicrowavedApple\nTASK PutMicrowavedApple {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=apple, state=state_microwaved) -> apple_slice : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=apple_slice, destination=table, location=corner, relation=on)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The existing state-value category captures the requested object state; selected-object placement is covered by the Action revision."}, {"item_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-11578", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified", "nl": "Fix LogisticRegressionCV probabilistic scoring so the LogisticRegression constructed in _log_reg_scoring_path inherits multi_class, and test the correction.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FixLogisticRegressionScoring\nTASK FixLogisticRegressionScoring {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=sklearn, file=\"sklearn/linear_model/logistic.py\", method=\"_log_reg_scoring_path\", revision=\"construct LogisticRegression with multi_class=multi_class and preserve relevant constructor parameters\")\n  ACTION run_tests(target=sklearn, content=\"test multinomial probabilistic scorer behavior\")\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The code-file, method, revision, and test details remain explicitly unresolved STRING attributes. The Action proposal does not add the missing code-value categories."}, {"item_id": "django__django-13112", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified", "nl": "Fix makemigrations crashing for a ForeignKey with a mixed-case Django app name.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FixMixedCaseMigration\nTASK FixMixedCaseMigration {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=django, file=\"django/db/models/fields/related.py\", revision=\"preserve mixed-case installed app names when resolving lazy ForeignKey references\")\n  ACTION run_tests(target=django, content=\"mixed-case app-name ForeignKey migration regression test\")\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The actionable software-fix core is represented only through transitional STRING fields; N3-compliant code path, code change, and assertion categories are still absent."}, {"item_id": "c6516", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "Can you give me some great places to visit in the Netherlands?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT SuggestNetherlandsPlaces\nCONVO SuggestNetherlandsPlaces {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"recommend great places to visit in the Netherlands\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The speech act and recipient are structured, but the request substance remains an unresolved content STRING, violating N3 and N4."}, {"item_id": "c3388", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "hi how hs your day been?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PainConversation\nCONVO PainConversation {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"how has your day been\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n  TURN t2 SPEAKER=USER REPLY_TO t1 {\n    UTTER correct(content=\"ask how my day has been\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n  TURN t3 SPEAKER=USER REPLY_TO t2 {\n    UTTER inform(content=\"my day has been boring and I have been in pain for nearly three years\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n  TURN t4 SPEAKER=USER REPLY_TO t3 {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"tell me a joke to distract me from pain\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Conversation sequencing is represented, but all conversational substance remains prose content rather than glossary values."}, {"item_id": "c2067", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "Can you breifly explain American politics to me?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT AmericanPoliticsConversation\nCONVO AmericanPoliticsConversation {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"briefly explain American politics\", recipient=role_agent, tone=tone_concise)\n  }\n  TURN t2 SPEAKER=USER REPLY_TO t1 {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"why is the Supreme Court part of government\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n  TURN t3 SPEAKER=USER REPLY_TO t2 {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"are Supreme Court justices elected by the people\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n  TURN t4 SPEAKER=USER REPLY_TO t3 {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"if appointed by the president, how is that fair\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The follow-up sequence and concise-register request are captured, but political content is an unresolved STRING payload."}, {"item_id": "c2904", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "Tell me about what is happening in New Zealand Politically", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT CurrentAotearoaPolitics\nCONVO CurrentAotearoaPolitics {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"explain current political developments in New Zealand\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n  TURN t2 SPEAKER=USER REPLY_TO t1 {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"state whether your information is current\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n  TURN t3 SPEAKER=USER REVISES t1 {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"explain current political events in Aotearoa for 2023\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "REVISES captures the correction structure, but its substantive time/place/topic constraints remain prose content."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-73283", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "Introduce the topic of the impact of dam construction on seasonal precipitation pattern, land use/cover, and socio-economic conditions in semi-arid Eastern Sudan.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT IntroduceDamTopic\nTASK IntroduceDamTopic : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_technical_explanation, content=\"introduce impacts of dam construction on seasonal precipitation, land use cover, and socio-economic conditions in semi-arid Eastern Sudan\") -> introduction : STRING\n  RETURN introduction\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Artifact type is governed, but the requested subject matter remains an explicit unresolved content STRING."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-76731", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "Try to squeeze some Holy Blood and Holy Grail-like conspiracy ideas from The Brothers Karamazov.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT CompareLiteraryThemes\nCONVO CompareLiteraryThemes {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"identify Holy Blood and Holy Grail-like conspiracy themes in The Brothers Karamazov\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The request is a question to the agent, but its literary entities and comparison relation have no symbolic content encoding."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-137561", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "Write a story of when Gloopy and Glitter met the scientist, who is amazed they can speak.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT WriteGloopiterMeeting\nTASK WriteGloopiterMeeting : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_story, content=\"story in which Gloopy and Glitter meet a scientist who is amazed that they can speak\") -> story : STRING\n  RETURN story\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The requested artifact is structured as art_story, but characters, events, and the premise remain prose and violate N3/N4."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-78000", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "Add a binding signature line to the speaker-to-client high-demand speaking-engagement contract.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ReviseSpeakerContract\nTASK ReviseSpeakerContract : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_contract, content=\"speaker-to-client high-demand speaking engagement contract including a binding client signature and date line\") -> contract : STRING\n  RETURN contract\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The artifact target is governed under the assumed complete glossary, but contractual parties, obligations, and signature requirement remain unresolved prose content."}, {"item_id": "1776009617894", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "Can you suggest a posting schedule to help the Hamoudi educational YouTube channel grow quickly in its first month?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PlanHamoudiSchedule\nTASK PlanHamoudiSchedule : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_plan, content=\"first-month posting schedule for the Hamoudi educational YouTube channel, optimized for growth\") -> schedule : STRING\n  RETURN schedule\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Planning artifact structure is present, but channel identity, publishing cadence, and growth goal are all hidden in content STRING."}, {"item_id": "1775429344935", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "Help me to create a text about my decision to go to Japan to learn about SGI. Only 100 words.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT WriteJapanSGIText\nTASK WriteJapanSGIText : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_short_text, content=\"personal decision to travel to Japan to learn about SGI\", quantity=100) -> text : STRING\n  RETURN text\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "quantity=100 has no stated word-count unit or semantics, so the exact 100-word constraint is not preserved; the topic also remains prose content."}, {"item_id": "1775752130482", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "Hello, I want to plan a 3 day safari in eastern cape south africa.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PlanEasternCapeSafari\nTASK PlanEasternCapeSafari : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_itinerary, content=\"safari in Eastern Cape South Africa\", duration=3, duration_unit=unit_day) -> itinerary : STRING\n  RETURN itinerary\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Duration and its unit are governed, but the destination and safari subject remain content STRING rather than structured location/category values."}, {"item_id": "1775479438859", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "Gain a short certification if it opens a stable field: examples in UK context?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT SuggestUKCertifications\nTASK SuggestUKCertifications : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_plan, content=\"short UK certifications that can lead to stable mortgage-friendly employment\") -> recommendations : STRING\n  RETURN recommendations\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The answer artifact is represented, but jurisdiction, certification concepts, job fields, and mortgage criterion are all prose payload."}]
