Proposed changes available for this translation:
- [revise] Types & Lexicon: grammar `type ::= "NUMBER" | "STRING" [ "<" category-id ">" ] | "BOOL" | "LIST" "[" type "]" | "REF" "[" type "]"
category-id ::= a glossary vocabulary-category name
value ::= STRING | NUMBER | IDENT | "TRUE" | "FALSE" | list_lit | diff
list_lit ::= "[" value ("," value)* "]"` — A direct glossary symbol has static type STRING<its-category>; an unquoted symbol may belong to exactly one category in the position where it is used. A quoted STRING literal has type STRING with no category qualifier. LET, parameters, Task returns, task-call results, and Action/Generate results retain their declared type exactly. A list literal has type LIST[T] only when every member has exactly T; thus LIST[STRING<entity-name>] is distinct from LIST[STRING<semantic-category-value>]. No provenance unions exist. A category-governed attribute accepts only a direct member, or a binding/list whose declared type exactly matches its permitted category domain. REF[STRING] and LIST[REF[STRING]] never carry descriptive-category provenance.
- [revise] Action: grammar `action ::= "ACTION" operation-id "(" action-attr ("," action-attr)* ")" ("->" IDENT ":" type)?
action-attr ::= attribute-name "=" value
