  {
   "op": "revise",
   "construct_name": "Generate",
   "grammar": "generation ::= \"GENERATE\" \"(\" generate-attr (\",\" generate-attr)* \")\" \"->\" IDENT \":\" gen_type\n-- Legal attributes: target, audience, budget, content, currency, duration, duration_unit, format, locale, quantity, quantity_unit, style, tone, stop_min_per_day, stop_requirement, max_walk_duration, max_walk_duration_unit.",
   "semantics": "GENERATE target requires artifact-value; audience requires recipient-value; tone, format, style, locale, currency, and units require their named categories; numeric constraints require NUMBER. quantity is exact only when paired with quantity_unit: quantity_unit=unit_word means exactly that many whitespace-delimited output words after rendering; quantity_unit=unit_item means exactly that many top-level generated items. budget is the maximum total monetary cost in currency. stop_requirement requires semantic-category-value, and stop_min_per_day counts only matching class members. content requires content-value; plain STRING remains a transitional build-phase alternative until N4 closes it. Target is first and all remaining attributes are alphabetical.",
   "worked_example": {
    "nl": "Write exactly 100 words about a decision to study SGI in Japan.",
    "braincode": "GENERATE(target=art_short_text, content=content_decision_study_sgi_japan, quantity=100, quantity_unit=unit_word) -> text : STRING"
   },
   "glossary_gloss": "Generate creates a non-effectful artifact with governed descriptive constraints. A numeric output length is exact only when its measurement unit is stated.",
   "change_type": "MAJOR",
   "rationale": "Quantity now preserves the distinction between words and generated items, while content receives a symbolic replacement category.",
   "cites_source": "HTML",
   "addresses_note": "N3"
  },
  {
   "op": "revise",
   "construct_name": "Utterance",
   "grammar": "utterance ::= \"UTTER\" speech-act \"(\" utter-attr (\",\" utter-attr)* \")\" (\"->\" IDENT)?\nutter-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value\n-- Legal attributes: audience, budget, content, currency, recipient, target, tone.",
   "semantics": "UTTER attributes are alphabetical. recipient and audience require recipient-value; tone requires tone-value; target requires entity-name or artifact-value according to the speech act; budget is NUMBER and currency is currency-value. content requires content-value; a STRING content value remains an explicit transitional N3 violation until the closing phase. A bound UTTER result is STRING and must use content, content_2, content_3, and so on.",
   "worked_example": {
    "nl": "Ask the manager politely for a status update.",
    "braincode": "CONVO StatusRequest {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=content_status_update, recipient=role_manager, tone=tone_polite)\n  }\n}"
   },
   "glossary_gloss": "Utterance records a speech act using named recipients, tones, targets, and symbolic content values. Temporary quoted content remains visibly marked as a build-phase exception.",
   "change_type": "MAJOR",
   "rationale": "This makes the intended N3-compliant content domain available to conversational requests without prematurely removing the existing coverage channel.",
   "cites_source": "Why Agentic Systems Need Ontologies",
   "addresses_note": "N3"
