mum rating as NUMBER.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "limit", "gloss": "Maximum extracted count as NUMBER.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "color", "gloss": "Color from product-attribute-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "size", "gloss": "Size from product-attribute-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "gender", "gloss": "Demographic facet from product-attribute-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "shape", "gloss": "Shape from shape-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "state", "gloss": "Condition from state-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "platform", "gloss": "Platform from platform-name.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "location", "gloss": "Location from location-name.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "origin", "gloss": "Travel origin from location-name.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "destination", "gloss": "Destination from entity-name or location-name.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "source", "gloss": "Source from entity-name, location-name, or code-value as specified by the operation.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "relation", "gloss": "Spatial relation from spatial-relation.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "compatible_with", "gloss": "Selected compatible object as REF[STRING].", "nl_synonyms": ["compatible with"]}, {"symbol": "date", "gloss": "Calendar date using ISO_DATE.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "deadline", "gloss": "Deadline using UTC_TIMESTAMP.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "metric", "gloss": "Status metric from metric-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "discount_percent", "gloss": "Percentage from NUMBER in the inclusive range 0 through 100.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "trending", "gloss": "Boolean trending filter.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "file", "gloss": "Code path from code-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "method", "gloss": "Code symbol from code-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "property", "gloss": "Code symbol from code-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "call", "gloss": "Code-call symbol from code-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "assertion", "gloss": "Test assertion from code-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "expected_output", "gloss": "Expected code outcome from code-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "actual_output", "gloss": "Actual code outcome from code-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "reproduction_step", "gloss": "Reproduction case from code-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "revision", "gloss": "Code change from code-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "This index is exhaustive for attributes currently used by BrainCode constructs and Action signatures. NUMBER, BOOL, ISO_DATE, UTC_TIMESTAMP, REF[STRING], and LIST[REF[STRING]] are glossary-defined literal or type domains; all remaining domains name a vocabulary category. New attributes must be added here with one exact domain before use.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Find the highest-rated dog collar under ten dollars.", "braincode": "ACTION search_web(target=dog_collar, currency=curr_usd, max_price=10) -> collars : LIST[REF[STRING]]\nACTION sort(target=collars, rank_direction=dir_desc, rank_field=rank_rating) -> sorted_collars : LIST[REF[STRING]]"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "This replaces partial and implicit attribute governance with an individually look-upable domain for every currently used attribute.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Generate", "grammar": "generation ::= \"GENERATE\" \"(\" generate-attr (\",\" generate-attr)* \")\" \"->\" IDENT \":\" gen_type\n-- Legal attributes: target, audience, budget, content, currency, duration, duration_unit, format, locale, quantity, quantity_unit, style, tone, stop_min_per_day, stop_requirement, max_walk_duration, max_walk_duration_unit.", "semantics": "GENERATE target requires artifact-value; audience requires recipient-value; tone, format, style, locale, currency, and units require their named categories; numeric constraints require NUMBER. quantity is exact only when paired with quantity_unit: quantity_unit=unit_word means exactly that many whitespace-delimited output words after rendering; quantity_unit=unit_item means exactly that many top-level generated items. budget is the maximum total monetary cost in currency. stop_requirement requires semantic-category-value, and stop_min_per_day counts only matching class members. content requires content-value; plain STRING remains a transitional build-phase alternative until N4 closes it. Target is first and all remaining attributes are alphabetical.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Write exactly 100 words about a decision to study SGI in Japan.", "braincode": "GENERATE(target=art_short_text, content=content_decision_study_sgi_japan, quantity=100, quantity_unit=unit_word) -> text : STRING"}, "glossary_gloss": "Generate creates a non-effectful artifact with governed descriptive constraints. A numeric output length is exact only when its measurement unit is stated.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Quantity now preserves the distinction between words and generated items, while content receives a symbolic replacement category.", "cites_source": "HTML", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Utterance", "grammar": "utterance ::= \"UTTER\" speech-act \"(\" utter-attr (\",\" utter-attr)* \")\" (\"->\" IDENT)?\nutter-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value\n-- Legal attributes: audience, budget, content, currency, recipient, target, tone.", "semantics": "UTTER attributes are alphabetical. recipient and audience require recipient-value; tone requires tone-value; target requires entity-name or artifact-value according to the speech act; budget is NUMBER and currency is currency-value. content requires content-value; a STRING content value remains an explicit transitional N3 violation until the closing phase. A bound UTTER result is STRING and must use content, content_2, content_3, and so on.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Ask the manager politely for a status update.", "braincode": "CONVO StatusRequest {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=content_status_update, recipient=role_manager, tone=tone_polite)\n  }\n}"}, "glossary_gloss": "Utterance records a speech act using named recipients, tones, targets, and symbolic content values. Temporary quoted content remains visibly marked as a build-phase exception.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "This makes the intended N3-compliant content domain available to conversational requests without prematurely removing the existing coverage channel.", "cites_source": "Why Agentic Systems Need Ontologies", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "semantic-category-value", "glossary_gloss": "Semantic-category-value names an abstract class used as a constraint, not a selectable physical entity. It is the only canonical category for generic itinerary-stop requirements.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "class_temple", "gloss": "The abstract class of temples.", "nl_synonyms": ["temple", "temples"]}, {"symbol": "class_town", "gloss": "The abstract class of towns.", "nl_synonyms": ["town", "towns"]}], "membership_rule": "Members match class_[a-z_]+ and denote abstract semantic classes only. Use entity-name for a selectable object or place kind in an Action target; use semantic-category-value for a generic qualification such as stop_requirement. A translator must encode a generic requested stop class as class_<name>, never as an entity-name.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Require at least one temple each day.", "braincode": "GENERATE(target=art_itinerary, content=content_kyoto_itinerary, stop_min_per_day=1, stop_requirement=class_temple) -> plan : STRING"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "The explicit selector-versus-constraint boundary eliminates the prior two valid encodings of a generic itinerary class.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "entity-name", "glossary_gloss": "Entity-name names a selectable kind of object, place, service, or artifact participant. It is used to select or act on a thing, not to express an abstract semantic class constraint.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "mug", "gloss": "Selectable drinking cup.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "apple", "gloss": "Selectable apple.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "temple", "gloss": "Selectable temple entity kind.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "coffee_maker", "gloss": "Selectable coffee-making appliance.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "An entity-name is an atomic [a-z_]+ symbol denoting a selectable entity kind. It is valid for Action selector targets and destinations where the signature permits it. It is never valid for stop_requirement; generic class constraints use semantic-category-value.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Search for a temple.", "braincode": "ACTION search_web(target=temple) -> temples : LIST[REF[STRING]]"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Revising the category's boundary makes its relationship to semantic-category-value non-overlapping and deterministic.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "code-value", "glossary_gloss": "Code-value supplies atomic symbols for code paths, program symbols, requested changes, test assertions, and code outcomes. Its prefixes determine which code attribute may use a member.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "path_sklearn_linear_model_logistic_py", "gloss": "The scikit-learn logistic module path.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "sym_log_reg_scoring_path", "gloss": "The _log_reg_scoring_path program symbol.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "chg_inherit_multi_class", "gloss": "Change requiring a constructed estimator to inherit multi_class.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "assert_multinomial_scorer", "gloss": "Assertion that multinomial probabilistic scoring succeeds.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "Members are atomic symbols with exactly one prefix: path_ for file/source paths, sym_ for methods/classes/functions/properties, call_ for call patterns, chg_ for requested code changes, assert_ for test assertions, outcome_ for expected or actual outcomes, and repro_ for reproduction cases. file and source require path_; method/property require sym_; call requires call_; revision requires chg_; assertion requires assert_; expected_output/actual_output require outcome_; reproduction_step requires repro_.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Fix LogisticRegressionCV scoring and test it.", "braincode": "ACTION modify_code(target=sklearn, file=path_sklearn_linear_model_logistic_py, method=sym_log_reg_scoring_path, revision=chg_inherit_multi_class)\nACTION run_tests(target=sklearn, assertion=assert_multinomial_scorer)"}, "change_type": "MINOR", "rationale": "One namespaced category provides the separately governed code-path, code-symbol, code-change, and test-assertion value sets while keeping code expressions atomic.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "content-value", "glossary_gloss": "Content-value names an atomic structured topic, request substance, message purpose, or artifact premise. It replaces prose content where the required symbolic member exists.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "content_status_update", "gloss": "A request for a status update.", "nl_synonyms": ["status update"]}, {"symbol": "content_kyoto_itinerary", "gloss": "A Kyoto itinerary subject.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "content_decision_study_sgi_japan", "gloss": "A personal decision to travel to Japan to study SGI.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "content_mixed_case_foreign_key_regression", "gloss": "A mixed-case Django app-name ForeignKey regression test purpose.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "Members match content_[a-z_]+ and each names one glossary-defined atomic proposition, topic, request purpose, premise, or message substance. A translator uses a listed canonical member or adds a member through a future vocabulary sprint; it may not place a phrase inside content when N4 closes transitional STRING.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Give me a story premise about Gloopy and Glitter meeting a scientist.", "braincode": "GENERATE(target=art_story, content=content_gloopy_glitter_meet_scientist) -> story : STRING"}, "change_type": "MINOR", "rationale": "This begins replacing opaque message and artifact content with glossary-governed symbols without removing existing build-phase STRING coverage.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "duration-unit-value", "glossary_gloss": "This category supplies governed measurement units for durations and generated-output quantities. Word and item units make output-length constraints precise.", "closed": true, "members": [{"symbol": "unit_second", "gloss": "Second.", "nl_synonyms": ["seconds", "sec"]}, {"symbol": "unit_minute", "gloss": "Minute.", "nl_synonyms": ["minutes", "min"]}, {"symbol": "unit_hour", "gloss": "Hour.", "nl_synonyms": ["hours"]}, {"symbol": "unit_day", "gloss": "Day.", "nl_synonyms": ["days"]}, {"symbol": "unit_week", "gloss": "Week.", "nl_synonyms": ["weeks"]}, {"symbol": "unit_month", "gloss": "Month.", "nl_synonyms": ["months"]}, {"symbol": "unit_year", "gloss": "Year.", "nl_synonyms": ["years"]}, {"symbol": "unit_word", "gloss": "Rendered whitespace-delimited word.", "nl_synonyms": ["words"]}, {"symbol": "unit_item", "gloss": "Top-level generated list or report item.", "nl_synonyms": ["items", "entries"]}], "membership_rule": null, "worked_example": {"nl": "Write exactly 100 words.", "braincode": "GENERATE(target=art_short_text, content=content_decision_study_sgi_japan, quantity=100, quantity_unit=unit_word) -> text : STRING"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Adding output-count units resolves the ambiguity of quantity while reusing the existing governed-unit mechanism.", "addresses_note": "N3"}], "_provider_used": "openai", "_model_used": "gpt-5.6-terra"}
Critic assessment: {"decision": "needs-rework", "kpi_assessment": {"coverage": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Code and symbolic-content categories improve coverage for SWE-bench, generated artifacts, and conversations. However, the proposed Action table declares itself exhaustive while omitting currently expressible operations such as open_container, close_container, turn_on, turn_off, select_filter, apply_filters, and existing domain actions such as booking; revising entity-name with only four members also risks deleting existing entities such as rag, sink, box, keys, chair, and mirror. This is a coverage regression during N2's build phase."}, "expressivity": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "The new code-value, content-value, semantic-category-value, and output-unit mechanisms preserve distinctions previously hidden in STRING, including expected versus actual output and exact word counts. But the action-table omissions make some existing closed tasks unexpressible, and content-value remains a single opaque proposition symbol that cannot yet compositionally preserve the substantial content of detailed code reports or long creative specifications."}, "determinism": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Category-qualified STRING types, the semantic-class/entity boundary, and alphabetized attributes are genuine improvements. The independent translations agree on the main pipelines for deleting old files, moving a rag, and modifying code, but disagree on target symbols, handle names, code path symbols, whether to include ENTRYPOINT, and the store-setting gap. The proposed Action table also introduces undeclared union notation (P|E and E|location-name), while Types declares exact matching and no unions."}, "interpretability": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "The individually indexed attribute domains and namespaced code prefixes make many values more inspectable. Interpretability is harmed by an allegedly complete Action signature table that silently removes existing operations, by undefined syntax for category-id and type unions, and by a broad content-value category whose member glosses may conceal arbitrarily complex propositions."}, "improvement": {"impact": "benefit", "reasoning": "For supported tasks, explicit code fields, typed category provenance, exact quantity units, and the entity-versus-semantic-class distinction would help a weaker planner preserve important constraints. The benefit is limited by missing operation signatures and the remaining transitional STRING channels."}}, "simulations": [{"item_id": "dev-code-1", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "Given a list of file paths, delete every file older than 30 days unless it's in the 'archive' folder.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT DeleteOldFiles\nTASK DeleteOldFiles(files: LIST[STRING<code-value>]) {\n  FOR EACH f IN files {\n    ACTION file_age_days(file=f) -> age : NUMBER\n    ACTION path_in_folder(file=f, source=path_archive) -> in_archive : BOOL\n    IF age > 30 AND NOT in_archive THEN {\n      ACTION delete_file(target=file_system, file=f)\n    }\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "code-value and qualified LIST typing support the file-path pipeline; target=file_system is assumed to be an entity-name member under N6."}, {"item_id": "dev-email-1", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "Draft a reply to my professor asking for a two-day extension on the assignment, and keep it formal.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT DraftExtension\nTASK DraftExtension : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_email, audience=role_professor, content=content_request_two_day_assignment_extension, format=format_email, tone=tone_formal) -> draft : STRING\n  RETURN draft\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "content-value and governed tone, audience, and format encode the core request; required category members are assumed under N6."}, {"item_id": "b7082615-e6e1-4981-b51b-9259671d1adf", "source": "Mind2Web", "nl": "Change your store to the one nearest to 07055", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ChangeStore\nTASK ChangeStore {\n  ACTION search_web(target=store, location=zip_07055) -> stores : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION sort(target=stores, rank_direction=dir_asc, rank_field=rank_distance) -> sorted_stores : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION extract(target=sorted_stores, limit=1) -> nearest_store : REF[STRING]\n  -- no well-typed Action exists to set nearest_store as the active store\n}", "coverage": "Fail", "notes": "The selector portion is expressible only if a ZIP-code literal/category exists, but no operation can perform the requested store change. The proposed exhaustive Action table therefore fails the actionable core."}, {"item_id": "e2adf8f1-547d-4671-96c1-4a21a56e135d", "source": "Mind2Web", "nl": "View the upcoming schedule from Otis St@Summer St to City Point of the transit near South Station for today.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ViewTransitSchedule\nTASK ViewTransitSchedule CONTEXT execution_date=\"2026-09-30\" {\n  ACTION search_transit(origin=otis_st_summer_st, destination=city_point, date=\"2026-09-30\") -> routes : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  -- no signature selects South Station, chooses the City Point route, or views its upcoming schedule\n}", "coverage": "Fail", "notes": "search_transit helps, but the route-selection and schedule-viewing core is absent from the proposed exhaustive Action table."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190908_120422_949453#2", "source": "ALFRED", "nl": "Move a red rag into a sink.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT MoveRedRag\nTASK MoveRedRag {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=rag, color=color_red) -> rag_ref : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=rag_ref, destination=sink, relation=in)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "pick_up and place retain the selected-object pipeline; entity-name members are assumed to include rag and sink."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190906_165121_524545#3", "source": "ALFRED", "nl": "Put a box with keys in it on a chair.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PutBoxOnChair\nTASK PutBoxOnChair {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=keys) -> keys_ref : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=keys_ref, destination=box, relation=in)\n  ACTION pick_up(target=box) -> box_ref : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=box_ref, destination=chair, relation=on)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The required containment ordering is preserved. This relies on box, keys, and chair remaining entity-name members; the proposed replacement entity-name member list must not erase them."}, {"item_id": "sphinx-doc__sphinx-7757", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified", "nl": "The default value for positional only argument has vanished.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FixPositionalOnlyDefault\nTASK FixPositionalOnlyDefault {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=sphinx, file=path_sphinx_util_inspect_py, actual_output=outcome_positional_only_default_missing, expected_output=outcome_positional_only_default_shown, reproduction_step=repro_py_function_positional_only_default, revision=chg_restore_positional_only_default_rendering)\n  ACTION run_tests(target=sphinx, assertion=assert_positional_only_default_rendered)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "code-value provides appropriate governed slots for file, expected/actual behavior, reproduction, revision, and assertion."}, {"item_id": "django__django-15268", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified", "nl": "Optimize multiple AlterFooTogether operations into one.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT OptimizeAlterTogether\nTASK OptimizeAlterTogether {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=django, file=path_django_db_migrations_operations_models_py, method=sym_reduce_operations, reproduction_step=repro_adjacent_alter_unique_and_index_together, revision=chg_coalesce_adjacent_alter_together_operations)\n  ACTION run_tests(target=django, assertion=assert_alter_together_operations_coalesced)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The new code-value category helps encode the closed actionable core, assuming the complete category under N6."}, {"item_id": "c7033", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "What is an objectively stronger video game, Marvel's Spider-Man 2 or Baldur's Gate 3? But you must pick one.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT CompareGames\nCONVO CompareGames {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=content_compare_spider_man_2_baldurs_gate_3)\n  }\n  TURN t2 SPEAKER=USER REPLY_TO t1 {\n    UTTER insist(content=content_require_single_choice)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "content-value can carry the request substance symbolically, but insist is absent from operation-vocabulary and the factual comparison criteria and required answer choice lack a compositional representation."}, {"item_id": "c1182", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "How to approach a girl; give me best pick up lines; make them more realistic and likely to work in real life.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PickupAdvice\nCONVO PickupAdvice {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=content_advice_approach_person)\n  }\n  TURN t2 SPEAKER=USER REPLY_TO t1 {\n    UTTER ask(content=content_generate_pickup_lines)\n  }\n  TURN t3 SPEAKER=USER REVISES t2 {\n    UTTER ask(content=content_realistic_respectful_pickup_lines)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Conversation sequencing and correction are preserved, but content-value is opaque and no glossary category expresses realism, consent, creativity, or practical effectiveness as independent constraints."}, {"item_id": "c224", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "Why does it seem a lot of people are extremely right-wing the last couple of years?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ExplainPoliticalShift\nCONVO ExplainPoliticalShift {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=content_explain_recent_right_wing_shift)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The speech act is expressible, but causal-analysis content remains an opaque content-value rather than structured factors and temporal scope."}, {"item_id": "c1448", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "What do you think of the outcomes of the elections in the Netherlands from yesterday?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT AnalyzeDutchElection\nCONVO AnalyzeDutchElection {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=content_analyze_netherlands_election_outcomes_yesterday)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The request is captured at the content-symbol level, but temporal grounding for yesterday and the requested evaluative analysis are not separately represented."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-58610", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "Continue Part 3 about Zack's flirtishly and charming nature kicking in.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ContinueCrossover\nTASK ContinueCrossover : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_script, content=content_continue_zack_helltaker_part_3_flirtatious_charming, style=style_narrative) -> continuation : STRING\n  RETURN continuation\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The continuation intent, artifact kind, and style are represented, but the extensive prior-story state, named cast, and requested scene dynamics are compressed into one opaque content-value."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-149438", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "Write a hilarious script where the Scooby gang and Scrappy-Doo react to badly translated sentences in a comedy 17+ way.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT GenerateTranslationRoast\nTASK GenerateTranslationRoast : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_script, content=content_scooby_gang_roast_bad_translation, style=style_comedic, tone=tone_humorous) -> script : STRING\n  RETURN script\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Artifact, broad content, and comedy style are expressible, but the 17+ constraint, named character behavior, quotation structure, and source sentence are not independently encoded."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-113201", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "Rewrite this table of profitable AI-automated online earning methods to be more comprehensive, preserve the first column, remove every <br />, and output a table.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT RewriteEarningTable\nTASK RewriteEarningTable : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_table, content=content_rewrite_ai_automated_earning_methods_table, format=format_table, style=style_detailed) -> table : STRING\n  RETURN table\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The output format and broad transformation goal are represented, but preserving the input first column, replacing each markup break, and the supplied table contents are hidden in content-value."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-155336", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "Monetag Review (2024): Is It a Best AdSense Alternative. Give me a summarize.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT SummarizeMonetagReview\nTASK SummarizeMonetagReview : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_summary, content=content_summarize_monetag_adsense_review_2024, tone=tone_concise) -> summary : STRING\n  RETURN summary\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The summary speech intent and concise register are retained, but the source article, year, comparison criteria, and factual claims are all bundled into one content symbol."}, {"item_id": "1776020181361", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "My MacBook Pro 2017 gets hot and the fan makes noise when I work. What can I do to reduce that? The laptop is closed and updated as far as its series permits.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT AdviseLaptopCooling\nCONVO AdviseLaptopCooling {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=content_reduce_macbook_pro_2017_heat_fan_noise)\n  }\n  TURN t2 SPEAKER=USER REVISES t1 {\n    UTTER correct(content=content_laptop_closed_and_os_update_limit)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The correction structure is captured, but model, symptoms, physical-access restriction, and update limitation are not decomposed into independently checkable attributes."}, {"item_id": "1775963744772", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "I specifically want to learn jazz and classical piano, so please focus your advice on that.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT AdvisePianoLearning\nCONVO AdvisePianoLearning {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=content_beginner_piano_learning)\n  }\n  TURN t2 SPEAKER=USER REVISES t1 {\n    UTTER ask(content=content_focus_beginner_jazz_and_classical_piano)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The revision ordering and advice request are preserved, but beginner status, limited budget, one-month target, and genre-specific learning constraints remain opaque content."}, {"item_id": "1775837106479", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "Please help me come up with the invite wording for my 9-year-old daughter's princess-themed birthday party this week at a play venue.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT GenerateBirthdayInvite\nTASK GenerateBirthdayInvite : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_invitation, audience=role_party_guest, content=content_nine_year_old_princess_play_venue_birthday_invitation, tone=tone_friendly) -> invitation : STRING\n  RETURN invitation\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Recipient/audience, artifact, tone, and broad event content are encoded, but age, timing, guest count, venue details, RSVP fields, and princess-theme wording are not structured."}, {"item_id": "1775973360170", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "Plan my weekly days as I go to school until 2pm and work from 4pm to 8pm; make it appealing and friendly, considering cereal and strong coffee in the morning and a late-morning snack.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PlanSchoolWorkWeek\nTASK PlanSchoolWorkWeek : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_weekly_schedule, content=content_school_until_2pm_work_4pm_8pm_coffee_cereal_snack_routine, tone=tone_friendly, format=format_table) -> schedule : STRING\n  RETURN schedule\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The requested artifact, friendly register, table format, and broad schedule substance are captured, but the fixed time blocks and meal preferences are not modeled as separate scheduling constraints."}], "cross_check": {"used": true, "agreement": "partial", "notes": "Anthropic and Gemini converge on the delete-old-files and red-rag action sequences, and both identify a missing final store-setting action. They diverge on target names, handle names, inclusion of entrypoints, code symbols, and treatment of missing