category-id ::= [a-z0-9-]+
value ::= STRING | NUMBER | IDENT | "TRUE" | "FALSE" | list_lit | diff
list_lit ::= "[" value ("," value)* "]"
diff ::= IDENT "-" NUMBER
IDENT ::= [a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*
STRING ::= "\"" ( [^"\\\n] | "\\\"" | "\\\\" | "\\n" | "\\t" | "\\u" HEXHEXHEXHEX )* "\""
COMMENT ::= "#" through end of physical line.` — A bare glossary symbol has static type STRING<its-category>; an unquoted symbol belongs to exactly one category. A quoted STRING literal has type STRING with no category qualifier. LET, parameters, Task returns, task-call results, and Action/Generate results retain their declared type exactly. A list literal has type LIST[T] only when every member has exactly T; thus LIST[STRING<entity-name>] is distinct from LIST[STRING<semantic-category-value>]. No provenance unions exist: an attribute in a signature must declare exactly one category, and an argument must match it exactly. REF[STRING] and LIST[REF[STRING]] carry no category provenance.
- [revise] Action: grammar `action ::= "ACTION" operation-id "(" action-attr ("," action-attr)* ")" ("->" IDENT ":" type)?
action-attr ::= attribute-name "=" value
-- target is first; remaining attributes are alphabetical.` — Every signature is normative; bracketed attributes are optional. Overloads resolve by exact attribute type. Result references REF[STRING] carry no category provenance. Search/Nav: search_web(target:STRING<entity-name>,[availability:STRING<search-value>,category:STRING<search-value>,color:STRING<product-attribute-value>,currency:STRING<currency-value>,genre:STRING<search-value>,gender:STRING<product-attribute-value>,location:STRING<location-name>,max_price:NUMBER,min_rating:NUMBER,platform:STRING<platform-name>,shape:STRING<shape-value>,size:STRING<product-attribute-value>,trending:BOOL])->LIST[REF[STRING]]; search_travel(origin:STRING<location-name>,destination:STRING<location-name>,date:ISO_DATE)->LIST[REF[STRING]]; search_transit(origin:STRING<location-name>,destination:STRING<location-name>,date:ISO_DATE)->LIST[REF[STRING]]; browse_trending(target:STRING<entity-name>,[location:STRING<location-name>])->LIST[REF[STRING]]; open_page(target:STRING<entity-name>); open_page(target:STRING<platform-name>); read_page(target:STRING<entity-name>)->STRING; read_page(target:STRING<platform-name>)->STRING. Interact: click(target:STRING<entity-name>); select_filter(target:STRING<entity-name>); apply_filters(target:STRING<entity-name>); fill_field(target:STRING<entity-name>,content:STRING<content-value>); submit(target:STRING<entity-name>). List/Extract: extract(target:LIST[REF[STRING]],limit:NUMBER)->REF[STRING]; sort(target:LIST[REF[STRING]],rank_direction:STRING<search-value>,rank_field:STRING<search-value>)->LIST[REF[STRING]]; create_list(target:STRING<entity-name>)->REF[STRING]; add_to_list(target:REF[STRING],content:STRING<content-value>). Physical: pick_up(target:STRING<entity-name>,[color:STRING<product-attribute-value>,shape:STRING<shape-value>,source:STRING<entity-name>,state:STRING<state-value>])->REF[STRING]; pick_up(target:STRING<entity-name>,[color:STRING<product-attribute-value>,shape:STRING<shape-value