 "changes": [
  {
   "op": "revise",
   "construct_name": "Types & Lexicon",
   "grammar": "type ::= \"NUMBER\" | \"STRING\" [ \"<\" category-id \">\" ] | \"BOOL\" | \"LIST\" \"[\" type \"]\" | \"REF\" \"[\" type \"]\"\ncategory-id ::= [a-z0-9-]+\nvalue ::= STRING | NUMBER | IDENT | \"TRUE\" | \"FALSE\" | list_lit | diff\nlist_lit ::= \"[\" value (\",\" value)* \"]\"\ndiff ::= IDENT \"-\" NUMBER\nIDENT ::= [a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*\nSTRING ::= \"\\\"\" ( [^\"\\\\\\n] | \"\\\\\\\"\" | \"\\\\\\\\\" | \"\\\\n\" | \"\\\\t\" | \"\\\\u\" HEXHEXHEXHEX )* \"\\\"\"\nCOMMENT ::= \"#\" through end of physical line.",
   "semantics": "A bare glossary symbol has static type STRING<its-category>; an unquoted symbol belongs to exactly one category. A quoted STRING literal has type STRING with no category qualifier. LET, parameters, Task returns, task-call results, and Action/Generate results retain their declared type exactly. A list literal has type LIST[T] only when every member has exactly T; thus LIST[STRING<entity-name>] is distinct from LIST[STRING<semantic-category-value>]. No provenance unions exist: an attribute in a signature must declare exactly one category, and an argument must match it exactly. REF[STRING] and LIST[REF[STRING]] carry no category provenance.",
   "worked_example": {
    "nl": "Use a bound itinerary-stop class.",
    "braincode": "LET required_stop : STRING<semantic-category-value> = class_temple\nGENERATE(target=art_itinerary, topic=topic_kyoto_trip, stop_min_per_day=1, stop_requirement=required_stop) -> plan : STRING"
   },
   "glossary_gloss": "A glossary symbol carries its category in its type, such as STRING<recipient-value>. Ordinary quoted text is only STRING and cannot be used where a specific glossary category is required.",
   "change_type": "MAJOR",
   "rationale": "Supplies concrete syntax and propagation rules for category provenance, resolving union ambiguity and providing exact typing for attributes.",
   "cites_source": "Why Agentic Systems Need Ontologies",
   "addresses_note": "N3"
  },
  {
   "op": "revise",
   "construct_name": "Action",
   "grammar": "action ::= \"ACTION\" operation-id \"(\" action-attr (\",\" action-attr)* \")\" (\"->\" IDENT \":\" type)?\naction-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value\n-- target is first; remaining attributes are alphabetical.",
   "semantics": "Every signature is normative; bracketed attributes are optional. Overloads resolve by exact attribute type. Result references REF[STRING] carry no category provenance. Search/Nav: search_web(target:STRING<entity-name>,[availability:STRING<search-value>,category:STRING<search-value>,color:STRING<product-attribute-value>,currency:STRING<currency-value>,genre:STRING<search-value>,gender:STRING<product-attribute-value>,location:STRING<location-name>,max_price:NUMBER,min_rating:NUMBER,platform:STRING<platform-name>,shape:STRING<shape-value>,size:STRING<product-attribute-value>,trending:BOOL])->LIST[REF[STRING]]; search_travel(origin:STRING<location-name>,destination:STRING<location-name>,date:ISO_DATE)->LIST[REF[STRING]]; search_transit(origin:STRING<location-name>,destination:STRING<location-name>,date:ISO_DATE)->LIST[REF[STRING]]; browse_trending(target:STRING<entity-name>,[location:STRING<location-name>])->LIST[REF[STRING]]; open_page(target:STRING<entity-name>); open_page(target:STRING<platform-name>); read_page(target:STRING<entity-name>)->STRING; read_page(target:STRING<platform-name>)->STRING. Interact: click(target:STRING<entity-name>); select_filter(target:STRING<entity-name>); apply_filters(target:STRING<entity-name>); fill_field(target:STRING<entity-name>,content:STRING<content-value>); submit(target:STRING<entity-name>). List/Extract: extract(target:LIST[REF[STRING]],limit:NUMBER)->REF[STRING]; sort(target:LIST[REF[STRING]],rank_direction:STRING<search-value>,rank_field:STRING<search-value>)->LIST[REF[STRING]]; create_list(target:STRING<entity-name>)->REF[STRING]; add_to_list(target:REF[STRING],content:STRING<content-value>). Physical: pick_up(target:STRING<entity-name>,[color:STRING<product-attribute-value>,shape:STRING<shape-value>,source:STRING<entity-name>,state:STRING<state-value>])->REF[STRING]; pick_up(target:STRING<entity-name>,[color:STRING<product-attribute-value>,shape:STRING<shape-value>,location:STRING<location-name>,state:STRING<state-value>])->REF[STRING]; place(target:REF[STRING],destination:STRING<entity-name>,[relation:STRING<spatial-relation>,state:STRING<state-value>]); place(target:REF[STRING],location:STRING<location-name>,[relation:STRING<spatial-relation>,state:STRING<state-value>]); heat(target:REF[STRING],[destination:STRING<entity-name>])->REF[STRING]; chill(target:REF[STRING],[destination:STRING<entity-name>])->REF[STRING]; rinse(target:REF[STRING],[destination:STRING<entity-name>])->REF[STRING]; slice(target:REF[STRING])->REF[STRING]; pour(target:REF[STRING],destination:STRING<entity-name>); open_container(target:REF[STRING]); close_container(target:REF[STRING]); turn_on(target:REF[STRING]); turn_off(target:REF[STRING]). Shopping/Booking: add_to_cart(target:REF[STRING]); save_favorite(target:REF[STRING]); set_active_store(target:REF[STRING]); book(target:REF[STRING]); select_schedule(target:REF[STRING]). Comm/Status: send_email(recipient:STRING<recipient-value>,[content:STRING<content-value>,tone:STRING<tone-value>]); send_message(recipient:STRING<recipient-value>,[content:STRING<content-value>,tone:STRING<tone-value>]); call(recipient:STRING<recipient-value>,[content:STRING<content-value>]); check_replied(target:STRING<recipient-value>,deadline:UTC_TIMESTAMP)->BOOL; check_support_status(target:STRING<entity-name>,metric:STRING<metric-value>)->BOOL; check_support_status(target:REF[STRING],metric:STRING<metric-value>)->BOOL; offer_discount(target:STRING<entity-name>,[content:STRING<content-value>,discount_percent:NUMBER]); offer_discount(target:REF[STRING],[content:STRING<content-value>,discount_percent:NUMBER]); offer_expedited_shipping(target:STRING<entity-name>); offer_expedited_shipping(target:REF[STRING]). Code/Files: modify_code(target:STRING<platform-name>,file:STRING<code-value>,[method:STRING<code-value>,property:STRING<code-value>,call:STRING<code-value>,assertion:STRING<code-value>,expected_output:STRING<code-value>,actual_output:STRING<code-value>,reproduction_step:STRING<code-value>,revision:STRING<code-value>]); modify_code(target:STRING<entity-name>,file:STRING<code-value>,[method:STRING<code-value>,property:STRING<code-value>,call:STRING<code-value>,assertion:STRING<code-value>,expected_output:STRING<code-value>,actual_output:STRING<code-value>,reproduction_step:STRING<code-value>,revision:STRING<code-value>]); run_tests(target:STRING<platform-name>,[assertion:STRING<code-value>,content:STRING<content-value>]); run_tests(target:STRING<entity-name>,[assertion:STRING<code-value>,content:STRING<content-value>]); add_file(target:STRING<platform-name>,file:STRING<code-value>,[content:STRING<content-value>]); add_file(target:STRING<entity-name>,file:STRING<code-value>,[content:STRING<content-value>]); delete_file(target:STRING<platform-name>,file:STRING<code-value>); delete_file(target:STRING<entity-name>,file:STRING<code-value>); file_age_days(file:STRING<code-value>)->NUMBER; path_in_folder(file:STRING<code-value>,source:STRING<code-value>)->BOOL. custom_<domain>_<action> requires target:STRING<entity-name> and may use content:STRING<content-value>. Prefix restrictions for code-value: file/source require path_; method/property require sym_; call requires call_; revision requires chg_; assertion requires assert_; expected_output/actual_output require outcome_; reproduction_step requires repro_.",
   "worked_example": {
