  "nl": "Search the best and the easiests creeper farms that are efortless to build and provide me a lot of gunpowder",
  "trajectory_steps": [
   "assistant: # Best & Easiest Creeper Farms in Minecraft\n\nHere are the top creeper farms ranked by **ease of build** and **gunpowder output**:\n\n---\n\n## 🏆 1. Simple Platform Creeper Farm (Easiest)\n**Output:** ~200-400 gunpowder/hour\n\n### How it works:\n- Build a dark platform (or multiple) at least **128 blocks above the ground** (or over an ocean)\n- Trapdoors on the ceiling (2 blocks high) to prevent Endermen/skeletons\n- Cats in the center push creepers off the edges\n- Creepers fall to their death into hoppers below\n\n### Materials needed:\n- Solid blocks (any)\n- Trapdoors (wooden or iron)\n- Cats (tamed ocelots/strays)\n- Hoppers + chests\n- Water channels (optional for funneling)\n\n**Why it's the best for beginners:** Minimal redstone, simple concept.\n\n---\n\n## 🥈 2. Shulkercraft's Creeper Farm\n**Output:** ~2,000+ gunpowder/hour\n\n- Multiple spawning platforms stacked\n- Uses cats to scare creepers into water streams\n- Creepers funnel to a central drop shaft\n- Very popular YouTube tutorial (easy to follow step-by-step)\n\n### Key features:\n- Carpet on trapdoors to block spiders\n- Buttons/slabs to prevent spider spawns\n- Usually 4-8 layers of spawning platforms\n\n---\n\n## 🥉 3. Wattles' Simple Creeper Farm\n**Output:** ~500-800 gunpowder/hour\n\n- Single or dual platform design\n- Cat-based pushing mechanic\n- Extremely beginner-friendly\n- Can be built in survival early game\n\n---\n\n## 📌 Key Tips for ALL Creeper Farms:\n\n| Tip | Why |\n|-----|-----|\n| **Build over an ocean** | No caves below = no mob cap competition |\n| **Build at Y=200+** | Ensures no mobs spawn elsewhere |\n| **Use trapdoors on ceiling** | 2-block gap only allows creepers (blocks Endermen) |\n| **Buttons or carpet on floors** | Prevents spider spawns |\n| **Use Looting III sword** | If using manual kill, massively boosts drops |\n| **Light up surrounding caves** | Improves spawn rates in the farm |\n| **AFK spot matters** | Stay 24-128 blocks from spawning platforms |\n\n---\n\n## 🔍 Recommended YouTubers for Tutorials:\n1. **Shulkercraft** – Best visual step-by-step guides\n2. **Wattles** – Beginner-friendly explanations\n3. **Rays Works** – More technical/optimized designs\n4. **ianxofour** – Compact and clever designs\n5. **Dusty Dude** – Simple survival-friendly farms\n\n---\n\n## Quick Recommendation:\n\n> **If you want EASY → Wattles' or a simple single-platform farm**\n>\n> **If you want MAXIMUM gunpowder → Shulkercraft's multi-layer farm**\n\nThe Shulkercraft design is the sweet spot — it's not hard to build and produces insane amounts of gunpowder. You'll have more gunpowder than you'll ever need for fireworks and TNT! 💥",
