Searcher notes: {'search_mode': 'folder', 'relevant_precedents': ['HTML', 'Why Agentic Systems Need Ontologies'], 'phenomena_present': ['closed-vocabulary', 'attribute-restriction'], 'kpi_fit': {'HTML': "Scores perfectly on determinism and interpretability by restricting structural attributes (like 'type' or 'rel') to a closed, spec-defined enumeration, ensuring independent parsers interpret them identically without guessing.", 'Why Agentic Systems Need Ontologies': 'Highlights how shared, structured ontologies improve determinism over free-text by forcing agents to communicate using a strict, predefined symbolic vocabulary.'}, 'comparable_expression': {'precedent': 'HTML', 'nl': 'Create an input field specifically for a telephone number.', 'rendering': '<input type="tel" autocomplete="tel"> (Attributes must use spec-defined symbols like \'tel\', not free-text descriptions like \'phone number\')'}, 'notes': "N3 enforces that all attributes use closed-vocabulary symbols rather than free text, directly mirroring HTML's enumerated attributes and the arguments in 'Why Agentic Systems Need Ontologies'. This touches the Action, Utterance, and Generate constructs (which heavily use attributes like tone, format, and state), and relies on the Types & Lexicon rule that bare IDENTs act as vocabulary symbols.", 'new_source_suggestion': None, '_search_mode': 'folder'}
Shaper proposal: {"summary": "Fixes the Action signature table and entity-name list to preserve all existing operations and members, introduces exact category-id syntax to resolve union ambiguity, and replaces opaque content strings with composable constraints, topics, and transformations.", "note_position": "comply", "note_argument": "These changes fully realize N3 by ensuring every attribute, including legacy ones, has a defined category domain, while preserving the expressivity and coverage of the existing language.", "foundations_overview": null, "rebuttals": [], "changes": [{"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Types & Lexicon", "grammar": "type ::= \"NUMBER\" | \"STRING\" [ \"<\" category-id \">\" ] | \"BOOL\" | \"LIST\" \"[\" type \"]\" | \"REF\" \"[\" type \"]\"\ncategory-id ::= [a-z0-9-]+\nvalue ::= STRING | NUMBER | IDENT | \"TRUE\" | \"FALSE\" | list_lit | diff\nlist_lit ::= \"[\" value (\",\" value)* \"]\"\ndiff ::= IDENT \"-\" NUMBER\nIDENT ::= [a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*\nSTRING ::= \"\\\"\" ( [^\"\\\\\\n] | \"\\\\\\\"\" | \"\\\\\\\\\" | \"\\\\n\" | \"\\\\t\" | \"\\\\u\" HEXHEXHEXHEX )* \"\\\"\"\nCOMMENT ::= \"#\" through end of physical line.", "semantics": "A bare glossary symbol has static type STRING<its-category>; an unquoted symbol belongs to exactly one category. A quoted STRING literal has type STRING with no category qualifier. LET, parameters, Task returns, task-call results, and Action/Generate results retain their declared type exactly. A list literal has type LIST[T] only when every member has exactly T; thus LIST[STRING<entity-name>] is distinct from LIST[STRING<semantic-category-value>]. No provenance unions exist: an attribute in a signature must declare exactly one category, and an argument must match it exactly. REF[STRING] and LIST[REF[STRING]] carry no category provenance.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Use a bound itinerary-stop class.", "braincode": "LET required_stop : STRING<semantic-category-value> = class_temple\nGENERATE(target=art_itinerary, topic=topic_kyoto_trip, stop_min_per_day=1, stop_requirement=required_stop) -> plan : STRING"}, "glossary_gloss": "A glossary symbol carries its category in its type, such as STRING<recipient-value>. Ordinary quoted text is only STRING and cannot be used where a specific glossary category is required.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Supplies concrete syntax and propagation rules for category provenance, resolving union ambiguity and providing exact typing for attributes.", "cites_source": "Why Agentic Systems Need Ontologies", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Action", "grammar": "action ::= \"ACTION\" operation-id \"(\" action-attr (\",\" action-attr)* \")\" (\"->\" IDENT \":\" type)?\naction-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value\n-- target is first; remaining attributes are alphabetical.", "semantics": "Every signature is normative; bracketed attributes are optional. Overloads resolve by exact attribute type. Result references REF[STRING] carry no category provenance. Search/Nav: search_web(target:STRING<entity-name>,[availability:STRING<search-value>,category:STRING<search-value>,color:STRING<product-attribute-value>,currency:STRING<currency-value>,genre:STRING<search-value>,gender:STRING<product-attribute-value>,location:STRING<location-name>,max_price:NUMBER,min_rating:NUMBER,platform:STRING<platform-name>,shape:STRING<shape-value>,size:STRING<product-attribute-value>,trending:BOOL])->LIST[REF[STRING]]; search_travel(origin:STRING<location-name>,destination:STRING<location-name>,date:ISO_DATE)->LIST[REF[STRING]]; search_transit(origin:STRING<location-name>,destination:STRING<location-name>,date:ISO_DATE)->LIST[REF[STRING]]; browse_trending(target:STRING<entity-name>,[location:STRING<location-name>])->LIST[REF[STRING]]; open_page(target:STRING<entity-name>); open_page(target:STRING<platform-name>); read_page(target:STRING<entity-name>)->STRING; read_page(target:STRING<platform-name>)->STRING. Interact: click(target:STRING<entity-name>); select_filter(target:STRING<entity-name>); apply_filters(target:STRING<entity-name>); fill_field(target:STRING<entity-name>,content:STRING<content-value>); submit(target:STRING<entity-name>). List/Extract: extract(target:LIST[REF[STRING]],limit:NUMBER)->REF[STRING]; sort(target:LIST[REF[STRING]],rank_direction:STRING<search-value>,rank_field:STRING<search-value>)->LIST[REF[STRING]]; create_list(target:STRING<entity-name>)->REF[STRING]; add_to_list(target:REF[STRING],content:STRING<content-value>). Physical: pick_up(target:STRING<entity-name>,[color:STRING<product-attribute-value>,shape:STRING<shape-value>,source:STRING<entity-name>,state:STRING<state-value>])->REF[STRING]; pick_up(target:STRING<entity-name>,[color:STRING<product-attribute-value>,shape:STRING<shape-value>,location:STRING<location-name>,state:STRING<state-value>])->REF[STRING]; place(target:REF[STRING],destination:STRING<entity-name>,[relation:STRING<spatial-relation>,state:STRING<state-value>]); place(target:REF[STRING],location:STRING<location-name>,[relation:STRING<spatial-relation>,state:STRING<state-value>]); heat(target:REF[STRING],[destination:STRING<entity-name>])->REF[STRING]; chill(target:REF[STRING],[destination:STRING<entity-name>])->REF[STRING]; rinse(target:REF[STRING],[destination:STRING<entity-name>])->REF[STRING]; slice(target:REF[STRING])->REF[STRING]; pour(target:REF[STRING],destination:STRING<entity-name>); open_container(target:REF[STRING]); close_container(target:REF[STRING]); turn_on(target:REF[STRING]); turn_off(target:REF[STRING]). Shopping/Booking: add_to_cart(target:REF[STRING]); save_favorite(target:REF[STRING]); set_active_store(target:REF[STRING]); book(target:REF[STRING]); select_schedule(target:REF[STRING]). Comm/Status: send_email(recipient:STRING<recipient-value>,[content:STRING<content-value>,tone:STRING<tone-value>]); send_message(recipient:STRING<recipient-value>,[content:STRING<content-value>,tone:STRING<tone-value>]); call(recipient:STRING<recipient-value>,[content:STRING<content-value>]); check_replied(target:STRING<recipient-value>,deadline:UTC_TIMESTAMP)->BOOL; check_support_status(target:STRING<entity-name>,metric:STRING<metric-value>)->BOOL; check_support_status(target:REF[STRING],metric:STRING<metric-value>)->BOOL; offer_discount(target:STRING<entity-name>,[content:STRING<content-value>,discount_percent:NUMBER]); offer_discount(target:REF[STRING],[content:STRING<content-value>,discount_percent:NUMBER]); offer_expedited_shipping(target:STRING<entity-name>); offer_expedited_shipping(target:REF[STRING]). Code/Files: modify_code(target:STRING<platform-name>,file:STRING<code-value>,[method:STRING<code-value>,property:STRING<code-value>,call:STRING<code-value>,assertion:STRING<code-value>,expected_output:STRING<code-value>,actual_output:STRING<code-value>,reproduction_step:STRING<code-value>,revision:STRING<code-value>]); modify_code(target:STRING<entity-name>,file:STRING<code-value>,[method:STRING<code-value>,property:STRING<code-value>,call:STRING<code-value>,assertion:STRING<code-value>,expected_output:STRING<code-value>,actual_output:STRING<code-value>,reproduction_step:STRING<code-value>,revision:STRING<code-value>]); run_tests(target:STRING<platform-name>,[assertion:STRING<code-value>,content:STRING<content-value>]); run_tests(target:STRING<entity-name>,[assertion:STRING<code-value>,content:STRING<content-value>]); add_file(target:STRING<platform-name>,file:STRING<code-value>,[content:STRING<content-value>]); add_file(target:STRING<entity-name>,file:STRING<code-value>,[content:STRING<content-value>]); delete_file(target:STRING<platform-name>,file:STRING<code-value>); delete_file(target:STRING<entity-name>,file:STRING<code-value>); file_age_days(file:STRING<code-value>)->NUMBER; path_in_folder(file:STRING<code-value>,source:STRING<code-value>)->BOOL. custom_<domain>_<action> requires target:STRING<entity-name> and may use content:STRING<content-value>. Prefix restrictions for code-value: file/source require path_; method/property require sym_; call requires call_; revision requires chg_; assertion requires assert_; expected_output/actual_output require outcome_; reproduction_step requires repro_.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Delete an old file from the file system.", "braincode": "ACTION delete_file(target=file_system, file=path_old_log)"}, "glossary_gloss": "Action performs an external operation using a complete, operation-specific signature. Overloads allow operations to accept different target categories without union types.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Provides an exhaustive, exact-typed signature table covering all existing operations, preserving Mind2Web and embodied coverage while enforcing N3 category provenance.", "cites_source": "Why Agentic Systems Need Ontologies", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Generate", "grammar": "generation ::= \"GENERATE\" \"(\" generate-attr (\",\" generate-attr)* \")\" \"->\" IDENT \":\" gen_type\n-- Legal attributes: target, audience, budget, constraints, content, currency, duration, duration_unit, format, locale, quantity, quantity_unit, stop_min_per_day, stop_requirement, style, topic, transformations, tone.", "semantics": "target requires STRING<artifact-value>; audience requires STRING<recipient-value>; tone, format, style, locale, currency, and units require their named categories; numeric constraints require NUMBER. constraints requires LIST[STRING<constraint-value>]; transformations requires LIST[STRING<transformation-value>]. topic requires STRING<topic-value>. content requires STRING<content-value>. quantity is exact only when paired with quantity_unit. budget is the maximum total monetary cost in currency. stop_requirement requires STRING<semantic-category-value>. Target is first; remaining attributes are alphabetical.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Rewrite a table of profitable AI earning methods, preserving the first column and removing <br />.", "braincode": "GENERATE(target=art_table, constraints=[constraint_comprehensive], topic=topic_ai_earning_methods, transformations=[transform_preserve_first_column, transform_remove_br]) -> table : STRING"}, "glossary_gloss": "Generate creates a non-effectful artifact with governed descriptive constraints, topics, and transformations.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Introduces composable constraints, transformations, and topics to structure artifact generation without relying on a single opaque content string.", "cites_source": "HTML", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Utterance", "grammar": "utterance ::= \"UTTER\" speech-act \"(\" utter-attr (\",\" utter-attr)* \")\" (\"->\" IDENT)?\nutter-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value\n-- Legal attributes: audience, budget, constraints, content, currency, recipient, target, tone, topic.", "semantics": "UTTER attributes are alphabetical. recipient and audience require STRING<recipient-value>; tone requires STRING<tone-value>; target requires STRING<entity-name> or STRING<artifact-value>; budget is NUMBER and currency is STRING<currency-value>. topic requires STRING<topic-value>; constraints requires LIST[STRING<constraint-value>]; content requires STRING<content-value>. A bound UTTER result is STRING and must use content, content_2, etc.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Ask for realistic, respectful pickup lines.", "braincode": "CONVO PickupAdvice {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(constraints=[constraint_realistic, constraint_respectful], topic=topic_pickup_lines)\n  }\n}"}, "glossary_gloss": "Utterance records a speech act using named recipients, tones, targets, topics, and structured constraints.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Brings Utterance into N3 compliance by supporting structured topics and constraints instead of unconstrained prose.", "cites_source": "Why Agentic Systems Need Ontologies", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "attribute-name", "glossary_gloss": "This category indexes every legal attribute and its exact value domain. All attributes now require their category-qualified symbol, list, or literal type.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "target", "gloss": "Operation-specific target.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "recipient", "gloss": "Message recipient from STRING<recipient-value>.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "audience", "gloss": "Artifact audience from STRING<recipient-value>.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "tone", "gloss": "Tone from STRING<tone-value>.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "format", "gloss": "Output layout from STRING<format-value>.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "style", "gloss": "Production style from STRING<style-value>.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "locale", "gloss": "Locale from STRING<locale-value>.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "content", "gloss": "Symbolic substance from STRING<content-value>.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "topic", "gloss": "Subject matter from STRING<topic-value>.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "constraints", "gloss": "List of constraints from LIST[STRING<constraint-value>].", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "transformations", "gloss": "List of transformations from LIST[STRING<transformation-value>].", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "quantity", "gloss": "Numeric output amount as NUMBER.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "quantity_unit", "gloss": "Unit for quantity from STRING<duration-unit-value>.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "duration", "gloss": "Numeric duration magnitude as NUMBER.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "duration_unit", "gloss": "Duration unit from STRING<duration-unit-value>.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "max_walk_duration", "gloss": "Numeric walking bound as NUMBER.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "max_walk_duration_unit", "gloss": "Walking-bound unit from STRING<duration-unit-value>.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "stop_min_per_day", "gloss": "Numeric daily minimum as NUMBER.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "s