ation", "gloss": "Spatial relation from STRING<spatial-relation>.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "compatible_with", "gloss": "Selected compatible object as REF[STRING].", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "date", "gloss": "Calendar date using ISO_DATE.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "deadline", "gloss": "Deadline using UTC_TIMESTAMP.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "metric", "gloss": "Status metric from STRING<metric-value>.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "discount_percent", "gloss": "Percentage from NUMBER.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "trending", "gloss": "Boolean trending filter as BOOL.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "file", "gloss": "Code path from STRING<code-value>.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "method", "gloss": "Code symbol from STRING<code-value>.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "property", "gloss": "Code symbol from STRING<code-value>.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "call", "gloss": "Code-call symbol from STRING<code-value>.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "assertion", "gloss": "Test assertion from STRING<code-value>.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "expected_output", "gloss": "Expected code outcome from STRING<code-value>.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "actual_output", "gloss": "Actual code outcome from STRING<code-value>.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "reproduction_step", "gloss": "Reproduction case from STRING<code-value>.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "revision", "gloss": "Code change from STRING<code-value>.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "ordering", "gloss": "Transitional STRING pending search-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "procedure", "gloss": "Transitional STRING pending procedure-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "food", "gloss": "Transitional STRING pending food-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "meal", "gloss": "Transitional STRING pending meal-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "message_structure", "gloss": "Transitional STRING pending message-structure-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "policy", "gloss": "Transitional STRING pending policy-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "amenity", "gloss": "Transitional STRING pending amenity-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "ticket", "gloss": "Transitional STRING pending ticket-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "seat", "gloss": "Transitional STRING pending seat-value.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "This index is exhaustive across all retained constructs and Action signatures. Legacy attributes use transitional STRING pending their dedicated categories. New attributes must be added here with one exact domain before use.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Find the highest-rated dog collar under ten dollars.", "braincode": "ACTION search_web(target=dog_collar, currency=curr_usd, max_price=10) -> collars : LIST[REF[STRING]]"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Makes the attribute index exhaustive and explicitly types every attribute, including legacy ones.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "entity-name", "glossary_gloss": "Entity-name names a selectable kind of object, place, service, or artifact participant. It is used to select or act on a thing, not to express an abstract semantic class constraint.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "mug", "gloss": "Drinking cup.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "rag", "gloss": "Cleaning cloth.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "tub", "gloss": "Bathtub.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "book", "gloss": "Reading material.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "mirror", "gloss": "Reflective item.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "sink", "gloss": "Washing basin.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "counter", "gloss": "Countertop surface.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "cupboard", "gloss": "Storage cabinet.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "refrigerator", "gloss": "Cooling appliance.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "spoon", "gloss": "Eating utensil.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "bowl", "gloss": "A bowl.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "pillow", "gloss": "A cushion.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "sofa", "gloss": "A couch.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "armchair", "gloss": "A chair with armrests.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "toilet_paper", "gloss": "Toilet paper.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "holder", "gloss": "A holder.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "wall", "gloss": "A wall.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "motherboard", "gloss": "Computer motherboard.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "processor", "gloss": "Computer processor.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "decorative_led_candles", "gloss": "LED candles.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "cup", "gloss": "A cup.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "coffee_maker", "gloss": "Coffee machine.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "microwave", "gloss": "Microwave oven.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "toilet", "gloss": "A toilet.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "apple", "gloss": "An apple.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "tv_show", "gloss": "Television program.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "dog_collar", "gloss": "Collar for a dog.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "box", "gloss": "A box.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "keys", "gloss": "Keys.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "chair", "gloss": "A chair.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "file_system", "gloss": "File system.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "store", "gloss": "A retail store.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "temple", "gloss": "Selectable temple entity kind.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "An entity-name is an atomic [a-z_]+ symbol denoting a selectable entity kind. It is valid for Action selector targets and destinations where the signature permits it. It is never valid for stop_requirement; generic class constraints use semantic-category-value.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Move a red rag into a sink.", "braincode": "ACTION pick_up(target=rag, color=color_red) -> rag_ref : REF[STRING]\nACTION place(target=rag_ref, destination=sink, relation=in)"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Retains all existing members while establishing the selector-versus-abstract-class boundary.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "semantic-category-value", "glossary_gloss": "Semantic-category-value names an abstract class used as a constraint, not a selectable physical entity. It is the only canonical category for generic itinerary-stop requirements.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "class_temple", "gloss": "The abstract class of temples.", "nl_synonyms": ["temple", "temples"]}, {"symbol": "class_town", "gloss": "The abstract class of towns.", "nl_synonyms": ["town", "towns"]}], "membership_rule": "Members match class_[a-z_]+ and denote abstract semantic classes only. Use entity-name for a selectable object or place kind in an Action target; use semantic-category-value for a generic qualification such as stop_requirement. A translator must encode a generic requested stop class as class_<name>, never as an entity-name.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Require at least one temple each day.", "braincode": "GENERATE(target=art_itinerary, topic=topic_kyoto_trip, stop_min_per_day=1, stop_requirement=class_temple) -> plan : STRING"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "The explicit selector-versus-constraint boundary eliminates the prior two valid encodings of a generic itinerary class.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "topic-value", "glossary_gloss": "Topic-value names an atomic subject matter, event, or premise for a conversation or generated artifact.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "topic_politics", "gloss": "Politics.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "topic_jazz_piano", "gloss": "Jazz piano.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "topic_classical_piano", "gloss": "Classical piano.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "topic_spider_man_2", "gloss": "Marvel's Spider-Man 2.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "topic_baldurs_gate_3", "gloss": "Baldur's Gate 3.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "topic_macbook_pro_2017", "gloss": "MacBook Pro 2017.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "topic_school_work_routine", "gloss": "School and work routine.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "topic_ai_earning_methods", "gloss": "AI earning methods.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "topic_pickup_lines", "gloss": "Pickup lines.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "Members match topic_[a-z_]+ and each names one glossary-defined atomic subject matter or premise.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Explain recent political shifts.", "braincode": "UTTER ask(topic=topic_politics)"}, "change_type": "MINOR", "rationale": "Decomposes monolithic content strings by separating the core subject matter from constraints.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "constraint-value", "glossary_gloss": "Constraint-value names an atomic requirement, restriction, or qualitative property applied to a request.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "constraint_17_plus", "gloss": "Rated 17+ or mature.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "constraint_single_choice", "gloss": "Must pick a single choice.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "constraint_realistic", "gloss": "Must be realistic.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "constraint_respectful", "gloss": "Must be respectful.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "constraint_beginner", "gloss": "Targeted at beginners.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "constraint_budget_limited", "gloss": "Limited budget.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "constraint_comprehensive", "gloss": "Must be comprehensive.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "Members match constraint_[a-z_]+ and each names one glossary-defined atomic constraint.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Give realistic pickup lines.", "braincode": "UTTER ask(constraints=[constraint_realistic], topic=topic_pickup_lines)"}, "change_type": "MINOR", "rationale": "Provides a composable list of constraints to replace opaque prose content.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "transformation-value", "glossary_gloss": "Transformation-value names an atomic structural or formatting change applied to an artifact.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "transform_preserve_first_column", "gloss": "Preserve the first column of a table.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "transform_remove_br", "gloss": "Remove <br /> tags.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "Members match transform_[a-z_]+ and each names one glossary-defined atomic transformation.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Rewrite the table and remove <br />.", "braincode": "GENERATE(target=art_table, topic=topic_ai_earning_methods, transformations=[transform_remove_br]) -> table : STRING"}, "change_type": "MINOR", "rationale": "Provides a composable list of structural transformations to replace opaque prose content.", "addresses_note": "N3"}], "_provider_used": "gemini", "_model_used": "gemini-3.1-pro-preview"}
Critic assessment: {"decision": "needs-rework", "kpi_assessment": {"coverage": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "The typed Action table restores many previously underspecified operations and adds set_active_store, code operations, rinse, slice, booking, and scheduling. However, it replaces the prior extensible/retained operation surface with a table that omits operations still used by the current specification, such as book_hotel, while book and select_schedule are not members of operation-vocabulary. The resulting language has avoidable regressions and cannot reliably preserve all currently expressible closed tasks."}, "expressivity": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "topic-value, constraint-value, transformation-value, semantic-category-value, and category-qualified attributes preserve useful distinctions, including generic itinerary classes versus selectable entities. But the proposed small lists do not compositionally encode many sampled request details, such as comparative advice, source credibility, narrative events, safety/eligibility conditions, and nuanced revision constraints; treating each whole request as a single content-value atom hides rather than structures those distinctions."}, "determinism": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Exact category provenance and the entity-name versus semantic-category-value distinction improve deterministic typing and eliminate one known union ambiguity. Determinism remains weak because operation selection is inconsistent with operation-vocabulary, category-id is syntactically open without a canonical glossary lookup rule, handle naming is still unconstrained, and the independent translations materially differ on ENTRYPOINT wrapping, source selection, optional spatial relation, and whether the request becomes content versus topic/constraints."}, "interpretability": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "The signature table and category domains make many attributes easier to inspect than raw strings. Yet the table is internally inconsistent with the attribute index and operation vocabulary, legacy attributes are described as bare transitional STRING domains despite N3, and opaque atoms such as content_<entire_request> or topic_<entire_request> cannot be understood from their spelling alone without a listed glossary member."}, "improvement": {"impact": "benefit", "reasoning": "For structured shopping, household, travel, and code tasks, exact signatures, typed filters, typed code fields, and explicit transformations give a weaker planner substantially better actionable structure than raw text. This benefit is limited for broad open requests because the proposal has no compositional representation for much of their substance beyond a single topic/content atom."}}, "simulations": [{"item_id": "dev-embodied-2", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "Put both pillows from the sofa onto the armchair, one at a time.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT MovePillows\nTASK MovePillows {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=pillow, source=sofa) -> pillow_1 : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=pillow_1, destination=armchair, relation=on)\n  ACTION pick_up(target=pillow, source=sofa) -> pillow_2 : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=pillow_2, destination=armchair, relation=on)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "Action's typed pick_up/place signatures express the sequential two-item core. The proposal helps, although canonical handle names remain unspecified."}, {"item_id": "dev-email-1", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "Draft a reply to my professor asking for a two-day extension on the assignment, and keep it formal.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT DraftExtensionReply\nTASK DraftExtensionReply : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_email, audience=role_professor, content=content_request_two_day_assignment_extension, duration=2, duration_unit=unit_day, tone=tone_formal) -> reply : STRING\n  RETURN reply\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "Uses symbolic content, recipient, duration, and tone. art_email and content_request_two_day_assignment_extension are assumed full-glossary members under N6."}, {"item_id": "42657330-bfc5-425d-ae21-396a9ba1fb12", "source": "Mind2Web (osunlp/Mind2Web, train, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Find yellow t-shirts for women small size that are less than $20.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FindTShirts\nTASK FindTShirts : LIST[REF[STRING]] {\n  ACTION search_web(target=t_shirt, color=color_yellow, currency=curr_usd, gender=gender_women, max_price=20, size=size_small) -> t_shirts : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  RETURN t_shirts\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The proposed exact search_web signature captures every stated search filter."}, {"item_id": "6c0a3b1e-6ce8-4955-9359-dd4378aacc82", "source": "Mind2Web (osunlp/Mind2Web, train, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Find the price of HomePod mini", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FindHomePodPrice\nTASK FindHomePodPrice : STRING {\n  ACTION search_web(target=homepod_mini) -> homepods : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION extract(target=homepods, limit=1) -> homepod : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION read_page(target=homepod_mini) -> price_page : STRING\n  RETURN price_page\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The task can search and read a page, but no typed price-extraction operation or price-value result exists. The returned STRING may contain arbitrary page text rather than the requested price."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190907_161637_930071#1", "source": "ALFRED (json_2.1.0, train)", "nl": "Put the goblet in the refrigerator on the table.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PutGoblet\nTASK PutGoblet {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=goblet, source=table) -> goblet_ref : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=goblet_ref, destination=refrigerator, relation=in)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "goblet is an assumed entity-name member under N6. The proposal's split signatures avoid an undeclared entity/location union."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190907_151643_465634#2", "source": "ALFRED (json_2.1.0, train)", "nl": "Take a potato from the count, cook it, finally putting it in the freezer.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT CookPotato\nTASK CookPotato {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=potato, source=counter) -> potato_ref : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION heat(target=potato_ref, destination=microwave) -> cooked_potato : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=cooked_potato, destination=freezer, relation=in)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The physical-operation table supports the ordered actionable core; potato and freezer are assumed entity-name members."}, {"item_id": "django__django-14493", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified (princeton-nlp/SWE-bench_Verified, test, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "ManifestStaticFilesStorage crashes with max_post_process_passes = 0. Description To reproduce: derive a custom class from ManifestStaticFilesStorage, set max_post_process_passes to 0, run collectstatic, then post_process raises UnboundLocalError because substitutions is not assigned when the loop does not execute.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FixManifestStorage\nTASK FixManifestStorage {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=django, actual_output=outcome_unbound_local_error_substitutions, expected_output=outcome_collectstatic_succeeds, file=path_django_contrib_staticfiles_storage_py, method=sym_post_process, reproduction_step=repro_collectstatic_max_post_process_passes_zero, revision=chg_initialize_substitutions_before_loop)\n  ACTION run_tests(target=django, assertion=assert_collectstatic_succeeds_when_max_post_process_passes_zero)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The code-value prefixes and dedicated fields improve representation of the actionable repair. The detailed causal rationale remains compressed into atomic code symbols."}, {"item_id": "matplotlib__matplotlib-25332", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified (princeton-nlp/SWE-bench_Verified, test, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Unable to pickle a figure with aligned labels: after align_labels(), pickle.dumps(fig) raises TypeError: cannot pickle weakref.ReferenceType object. Fix lib/matplotlib/cbook.py so pickling succeeds.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FixAlignedLabelPickling\nTASK FixAlignedLabelPickling {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=matplotlib, actual_output=outcome_pickle_weakref_type_error, expected_output=outcome_figure_pickling_succeeds, file=path_lib_matplotlib_cbook_py, reproduction_step=repro_align_labels_then_pickle, revision=chg_fix_aligned_label_pickling)\n  ACTION run_tests(target=matplotlib, assertion=assert_figure_with_aligned_labels_pickles)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The repair request maps to the proposed code fields, with assumed complete code-value members under N6."}, {"item_id": "c2762", "source": "PRISM (HannahRoseKirk/prism-alignment, conversations config, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Who is the greatest cricketer of all time?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT AskGreatestCricketer\nCONVO AskGreatestCricketer {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(topic=topic_greatest_cricketer_of_all_time)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The direct question is symbolically represented through an assumed topic-value member. The proposal does not encode the evaluative criterion behind 'greatest' compositionally."}, {"item_id": "c2888", "source": "PRISM (HannahRoseKirk/prism-alignment, conversations config, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "what is the house market in new york right now", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT AskNewYorkHousingMarket\nCONVO AskNewYorkHousingMarket {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(topic=topic_current_new_york_housing_market)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "An assumed topic member carries the question, but the time-sensitive 'right now' and request for factual assessment have no separately typed structure."}, {"item_id": "c929", "source": "PRISM (HannahRoseKirk/prism-alignment, conversations config, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "My family is invited to my grandma's birthday. I don't get along with her, would it be okay to be the only one to back out?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT AskBirthdayAttendanceAdvice\nCONVO AskBirthdayAttendanceAdvice {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(topic=topic_attend_grandmother_birthday_or_decline, constraints=[constraint_family_conflict, constraint_only_family_member_declining])\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "Assumed topic/constraint members encode the stated dilemma symbolically, but the proposal supplies no compositional relationship or advice-decision vocabulary."}, {"item_id": "c5582", "source": "PRISM (HannahRoseKirk/prism-alignment, conversations config, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Is it ok to print personal documents at work?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT AskPersonalPrintingPolicy\nCONVO AskPersonalPrintingPolicy {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(topic=topic_personal_document_printing_at_work)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The atomic topic can represent the question under N6, although policy, permissibility, and workplace-resource relations are not independently expressed."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-81276", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns, model=gpt-3.5-turbo-0613)", "nl": "Write a detailed story about Sadie Adler taking off her hat, dropping it, peeling away her skin, and becoming Mary Beth.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT WriteTransformationStory\nTASK WriteTransformationStory : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_story, constraints=[constraint_detailed], topic=topic_sadie_adler_unmasking_becomes_mary_beth) -> story : STRING\n  RETURN story\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "An assumed topic-value represents the premise without prose. Specific ordered story events are collapsed into one topic atom, which weakens richness despite satisfying the proposed attribute typing."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-144042", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns, model=gpt-4-0125-preview)", "nl": "explain the importance of using nonparametric control charts for process mean and variability monitoring in two paragraphs", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ExplainNonparametricCharts\nTASK ExplainNonparametricCharts : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_technical_explanation, quantity=2, quantity_unit=unit_paragraph, topic=topic_nonparametric_control_charts_for_mean_and_variability_monitoring) -> explanation : STRING\n  RETURN explanation\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The current duration-unit-value category has no unit_paragraph, and the proposal does not add a paragraph quantity unit. The topic is symbolically representable under N6, but the explicit two-paragraph requirement lacks a defined value."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-122879", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns, model=gpt-4-1106-preview)", "nl": "Continue the Camp Sludge story in a fun, entertaining, creative way; describe what campers were doing in the sludge pit, include dialogue with Emma, and avoid flowery language or liberation/freedom themes.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ContinueCampSludge\nTASK ContinueCampSludge : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_story, constraints=[constraint_fun, constraint_entertaining, constraint_creative, constraint_include_camper_emma_dialogue, constraint_avoid_flowery_language, constraint_avoid_liberation_theme], topic=topic_camp_sludge_emma_and_sludge_pit) -> continuation : STRING\n  RETURN continuation\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "Assumed constraint members preserve the explicit restrictions symbolically. The proposal lacks relations/events for the requested continuation and therefore relies on large atomic glossary entries."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-83312", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns, model=gpt-3.5-turbo-0613)", "nl": "Create a female, age-14, 00s-anime-style personification of Alek Száhala's track Alabama, with a detailed description and list of character attributes.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT DescribeAlabamaCharacter\nTASK DescribeAlabamaCharacter : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_character_profile, constraints=[constraint_detailed, constraint_include_character_attribute_list, constraint_female, constraint_age_14, constraint_2000s_anime_style], topic=topic_alek_szahala_alabama_personification) -> profile : STRING\n  RETURN profile\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "Assumed atomic constraints encode the request under N6, but there is no structured character-attribute schema for age, physical traits, personality, or music genre."}, {"item_id": "1775857728160", "source": "ThoughtTrace (SCAI-JHU/ThoughtTrace, Parquet column-projected sample, JSON-decoded messages)", "nl": "Search the best and easiest creeper farms that are effortless to build and provide a lot of gunpowder.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FindCreeperFarms\nTASK FindCreeperFarms : LIST[REF[STRING]] {\n  ACTION search_web(target=creeper_farm, category=cat_minecraft, rank_field=rank_ease_of_build, rank_direction=dir_desc) -> farms : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  RETURN farms\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The search is expressible, but 'best' combines ease and high gunpowder output; search-value has no output-yield criterion or deterministic multi-criterion ranking representation. The requested links also lack a typed link-extraction/output construct."}, {"item_id": "1775488035768", "source": "ThoughtTrace (SCAI-JHU/ThoughtTrace, Parquet column-projected sample, JSON-decoded messages)", "nl": "Hi! How to join the military engineering school", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT AskMilitaryEngineeringAdmission\nCONVO AskMilitaryEngineeringAdmission {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(topic=topic_join_military_engineering_school)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The request can be represented as an assumed topic-value, but country, educational background, and admission requirements are not represented as typed slots."}, {"item_id": "1773875884407", "source": "ThoughtTrace (SCAI-JHU/ThoughtTrace, Parquet column-projected sample, JSON-decoded messages)", "nl": "hello, i wanna plan a trip to morroco", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PlanMoroccoTrip\nCONVO PlanMoroccoTrip {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(topic=topic_plan_trip_to_morocco)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The initial planning intent and destination are represented by an assumed topic symbol. A useful itinerary still needs compositional dates, budget, party, interests, and route constraints."}, {"item_id": "1775494752255", "source": "ThoughtTrace (SCAI-JHU/ThoughtTrace, Parquet column-projected sample, JSON-decoded messages)", "nl": "hello", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT Greeting\nCONVO Greeting {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER acknowledge()\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The bare greeting maps to the existing acknowledge speech act. It does not encode the later travel-destination conversation because that later content is not the sampled nl request."}], "cross_check": {"used": true, "agreement": "low", "notes": "Independent translations disagree materially: one omits ENTRYPOINT/TASK wrappers while another includes them; pillow placement differs on whether relation=on is required; the goblet task differs on source and placement interpretation; and open/code requests differ between GAP placeholders and newly minted atomic symbols. The proposal improves category distinctions but does not provide canonical document wrapping, optional-modifier policy, handle naming, or a deterministic member-selection procedure."}, "required_changes": [{"target": "Types & Lexicon", "change": "Make N3 enforcement internally valid: remove bare STRING as an attribute-value alternative, or explicitly limit it to non-attribute variables/results. Define ISO_DATE and UTC_TIMESTAMP as named types/literal forms usable in signatures, and define category-id as a glossary-category reference with a validity rule requiring an existing category entry."}, {"target": "attribute-name", "change": "Replace every listed 'Transitional STRING pending ...' domain with its named category domain now. In particular, ordering, procedure, food, meal, message_structure, policy, amenity, ticket, and seat must each name a concrete category or be removed together with every construct/signature that uses them. Do not claim N3 compliance while any attribute accepts unqualified STRING."}, {"target": "Action", "change": "Reconcile the normative Action signature table with operation-vocabulary: add book, select_schedule, set_active_store, and all other retained operations to operation-vocabulary with canonical meanings, or remove them from signatures. Preserve every current operation/capability, including the currently exemplified book_hotel behavior or an explicitly typed canonical replacement."}, {"target": "Action", "change": "Publish one source-of-truth domain for every attribute occurrence. Resolve source's conflicting entity-name/code-value definition by operation-specific signatures in the attribute index; likewise correct destination so its index does not contradict location-name overloads. Add the missing set_active_store(target:REF[STRING]) signature explicitly if it is retained."}, {"target": "Generate", "change": "Restore all currently legal Generate attributes that the revision drops, including max_walk_duration and max_walk_duration_unit, and define gen_type or replace it with the revised type production. Add missing value categories/units needed by retained examples, including a paragraph quantity unit if paragraph-count requests are supported."}, {"target": "Utterance", "change": "Define each speech-act's legal attribute signature or a normative shared signature. The current blanket list permits nonsensical combinations and does not determine whether, for example, ask versus inform must carry recipient, topic, content, constraints, or target."}, {"target": "topic-value / constraint-value / transformation-value", "change": "Add compositional constructs/categories for propositions, event ordering, relations, comparative/ranking criteria, factual recency/source requirements, character properties, and explicit exclusions. Do not rely on a fresh monolithic topic_/content_/constraint_ atom for an entire request when the request contains independently meaningful constraints."}, {"target": "basis", "change": "Add canonical encoding rules for mandatory document wrapping, optional modifiers such as inferred spatial relations, handle naming, and selection between content, topic, and constraints. These are necessary for N7 convergence and are exposed by the supplied independent translations."}], "logic_issues": ["The proposed Types & Lexicon grammar does not define ISO_DATE or UTC_TIMESTAMP as types, yet Action signatures use ISO_DATE and UTC_TIMESTAMP as if they were types.", "The proposal claims every attribute has an exact category domain, but attribute-name explicitly assigns several legacy attributes unqualified transitional STRING domains. This directly violates N3 rather than merely leaving future work.", "The Action table introduces book and select_schedule although operation-vocabulary does not define them, while replacing the prior operation surface without preserving currently used book_hotel behavior.", "The attribute index states source is entity-name or code-value and destination is entity-name, but the signature table gives source operation-specific domains and allows location-name destinations. The claimed exact one-domain index is therefore false.", "Generate grammar returns gen_type although the revision only defines type; it also drops current Generate attributes max_walk_duration and max_walk_duration_unit.", "topic-value, constraint-value, and transformation-value use broad open prefix rules but do not specify a canonical translation or member lookup process, so equivalent requests can be encoded as a topic atom, content atom, or arbitrary combinations of constraints."], "notes_assessment": {"N2": {"status"