Proposed changes available for this translation:
- [revise] Types & Lexicon: grammar `type ::= "NUMBER" | "STRING" [ "<" category-id ">" ] | "BOOL" | "LIST" "[" type "]" | "REF" "[" type "]" | "ISO_DATE" | "UTC_TIMESTAMP"
category-id ::= [a-z0-9-]+
value ::= STRING | NUMBER | IDENT | "TRUE" | "FALSE" | list_lit | diff
list_lit ::= "[" value ("," value)* "]"
diff ::= IDENT "-" NUMBER
IDENT ::= [a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*
STRING ::= "\"" ( [^"\\\n] | "\\\"" | "\\\\" | "\\n" | "\\t" | "\\u" HEXHEXHEXHEX )* "\""
COMMENT ::= "#" through end of physical line.` — A bare glossary symbol has static type STRING<its-category>; an unquoted symbol belongs to exactly one category. category-id must exactly match an existing glossary category name. ISO_DATE and UTC_TIMESTAMP are named types for date/time literal strings. A quoted STRING literal has type STRING with no category qualifier. LET, parameters, and results retain their declared type exactly. An attribute in an Action, Generate, or Utterance signature MUST declare a specific STRING<category-id> or base type; unqualified STRING is illegal for attributes, enforcing N3. A list literal has type LIST[T] only when every member has exactly T.
- [revise vocabulary] attribute-name (open): This category indexes every legal attribute. Exact category domains are determined by the operation signatures in Action, Generate, and Utterance. Members: target, recipient, audience, tone, format, style, locale, content, topic, constraints, transformations, events, character_properties, quantity, quantity_unit, duration, duration_unit, max_walk_duration, max_walk_duration_unit, stop_min_per_day, stop_requirement, budget, currency, availability, category, genre, rank_field, rank_direction, max_price, min_rating, limit, color, size, gender, shape, state, platform, location, origin, destination, source, relation, date, deadline, metric, discount_percent, trending, file, method, property, call, assertion, expected_output, actual_output, reproduction_step, revision; membership rule: This index is exhaustive across all retained constructs and Action/Generate/Utterance signatures. Legacy transitional STRING attributes have been removed to enforce N3. The exact domain (e.g., STRING<entity-name> vs STRING<code-value>) is determined by the specific operation signature.
