- [revise vocabulary] operation-vocabulary (open): The initial index of normative Action and UTTER operations. Missing domains use a deterministic custom rule. Members: open_page, click, select_filter, apply_filters, sort, search_travel, search_transit, search_web, fill_field, submit, extract, read_page, save_favorite, add_to_cart, set_active_store, book_hotel, select_schedule, pick_up, place, heat, chill, rinse, slice, pour, open_container, close_container, turn_on, turn_off, modify_code, run_tests, add_file, delete_file, send_email, send_message, call, check_replied, file_age_days, path_in_folder, create_list, add_to_list, check_support_status, offer_discount, offer_expedited_shipping, ask, inform, respond, propose, correct, acknowledge, confirm, decline; membership rule: A self-contained deterministic mapping procedure: operations are strictly limited to the enumerated members. If a domain-specific operation is required but missing, it uses the atomic token rule custom_<domain>_<action>.
