   "semantics": "A BrainCode document declares exactly one ENTRYPOINT naming a top-level TASK or CONVO. Canonical encoding rules for N7: (1) Mandatory document wrapping: every request must be wrapped in an ENTRYPOINT and corresponding TASK or CONVO block. (2) Handle naming: bound variable names must derive from the target or result semantic name (e.g., `farms` for a list of farms, `farm_ref` for a single reference). (3) Optional modifiers: spatial relations (e.g. `relation=on`) are included only when explicitly stated in the natural language; otherwise omitted. `CONTEXT execution_date=ISO_DATE` is a translation-time-only annotation. Task names and Variable names are disjoint namespaces. Variable scoping is lexical and block-structured.",
