logies", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "attribute-name", "glossary_gloss": "This category indexes every legal attribute. Exact category domains are determined by the operation signatures in Action, Generate, and Utterance.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "target", "gloss": "Operation target.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "recipient", "gloss": "Message recipient.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "audience", "gloss": "Artifact audience.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "tone", "gloss": "Tone.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "format", "gloss": "Output layout.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "style", "gloss": "Production style.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "locale", "gloss": "Locale.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "content", "gloss": "Symbolic substance.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "topic", "gloss": "Subject matter.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "constraints", "gloss": "List of constraints.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "transformations", "gloss": "List of transformations.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "events", "gloss": "List of narrative events.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "character_properties", "gloss": "List of character traits.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "quantity", "gloss": "Numeric output amount.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "quantity_unit", "gloss": "Unit for quantity.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "duration", "gloss": "Numeric duration magnitude.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "duration_unit", "gloss": "Duration unit.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "max_walk_duration", "gloss": "Numeric walking bound.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "max_walk_duration_unit", "gloss": "Walking-bound unit.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "stop_min_per_day", "gloss": "Numeric daily minimum.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "stop_requirement", "gloss": "Required stop class.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "budget", "gloss": "Maximum monetary amount.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "currency", "gloss": "Monetary unit.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "availability", "gloss": "Availability.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "category", "gloss": "Search category.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "genre", "gloss": "Genre.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "rank_field", "gloss": "Ranking field.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "rank_direction", "gloss": "Ranking direction.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "max_price", "gloss": "Maximum price.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "min_rating", "gloss": "Minimum rating.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "limit", "gloss": "Maximum extracted count.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "color", "gloss": "Color.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "size", "gloss": "Size.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "gender", "gloss": "Demographic facet.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "shape", "gloss": "Shape.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "state", "gloss": "Condition.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "platform", "gloss": "Platform.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "location", "gloss": "Location from STRING<location-name>.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "origin", "gloss": "Travel origin.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "destination", "gloss": "Destination from STRING<entity-name>.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "source", "gloss": "Source from STRING<entity-name> or STRING<code-value> depending on signature.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "relation", "gloss": "Spatial relation.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "date", "gloss": "Calendar date.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "deadline", "gloss": "Deadline.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "metric", "gloss": "Status metric.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "discount_percent", "gloss": "Percentage.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "trending", "gloss": "Boolean trending filter.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "file", "gloss": "Code path.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "method", "gloss": "Code symbol.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "property", "gloss": "Code symbol.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "call", "gloss": "Code-call symbol.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "assertion", "gloss": "Test assertion.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "expected_output", "gloss": "Expected code outcome.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "actual_output", "gloss": "Actual code outcome.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "reproduction_step", "gloss": "Reproduction case.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "revision", "gloss": "Code change.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "This index is exhaustive across all retained constructs and Action/Generate/Utterance signatures. Legacy transitional STRING attributes have been removed to enforce N3. The exact domain (e.g., STRING<entity-name> vs STRING<code-value>) is determined by the specific operation signature.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Find dog collars.", "braincode": "ACTION search_web(target=dog_collar) -> collars : LIST[REF[STRING]]"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Removes transitional STRING attributes entirely to comply with N3. Defers exact domain typing to operation signatures to handle context-dependent attributes like source.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Action", "grammar": "action ::= \"ACTION\" operation-id \"(\" action-attr (\",\" action-attr)* \")\" (\"->\" IDENT \":\" type)?\naction-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value\n-- target is first; remaining attributes are alphabetical.", "semantics": "Every signature is normative; bracketed attributes are optional. Result references REF[STRING] carry no category provenance. Search/Nav: search_web(target:STRING<entity-name>,[availability:STRING<search-value>,category:STRING<search-value>,color:STRING<product-attribute-value>,currency:STRING<currency-value>,gender:STRING<product-attribute-value>,genre:STRING<search-value>,location:STRING<location-name>,max_price:NUMBER,min_rating:NUMBER,platform:STRING<platform-name>,shape:STRING<shape-value>,size:STRING<product-attribute-value>,trending:BOOL])->LIST[REF[STRING]]; search_travel(origin:STRING<location-name>,destination:STRING<location-name>,date:ISO_DATE)->LIST[REF[STRING]]; search_transit(origin:STRING<location-name>,destination:STRING<location-name>,date:ISO_DATE)->LIST[REF[STRING]]; browse_trending(target:STRING<entity-name>,[location:STRING<location-name>])->LIST[REF[STRING]]; open_page(target:STRING<entity-name>); open_page(target:STRING<platform-name>); read_page(target:STRING<entity-name>)->STRING; read_page(target:STRING<platform-name>)->STRING. Interact: click(target:STRING<entity-name>); select_filter(target:STRING<entity-name>); apply_filters(target:STRING<entity-name>); fill_field(target:STRING<entity-name>,content:STRING<content-value>); submit(target:STRING<entity-name>). List/Extract: extract(target:LIST[REF[STRING]],limit:NUMBER)->REF[STRING]; sort(target:LIST[REF[STRING]],rank_direction:STRING<search-value>,rank_field:STRING<search-value>)->LIST[REF[STRING]]; create_list(target:STRING<entity-name>)->REF[STRING]; add_to_list(target:REF[STRING],content:STRING<content-value>). Physical: pick_up(target:STRING<entity-name>,[color:STRING<product-attribute-value>,shape:STRING<shape-value>,source:STRING<entity-name>,state:STRING<state-value>])->REF[STRING]; pick_up(target:STRING<entity-name>,[color:STRING<product-attribute-value>,location:STRING<location-name>,shape:STRING<shape-value>,state:STRING<state-value>])->REF[STRING]; place(target:REF[STRING],destination:STRING<entity-name>,[relation:STRING<spatial-relation>,state:STRING<state-value>]); place(target:REF[STRING],location:STRING<location-name>,[relation:STRING<spatial-relation>,state:STRING<state-value>]); heat(target:REF[STRING],[destination:STRING<entity-name>])->REF[STRING]; chill(target:REF[STRING],[destination:STRING<entity-name>])->REF[STRING]; rinse(target:REF[STRING],[destination:STRING<entity-name>])->REF[STRING]; slice(target:REF[STRING])->REF[STRING]; pour(target:REF[STRING],destination:STRING<entity-name>); open_container(target:REF[STRING]); close_container(target:REF[STRING]); turn_on(target:REF[STRING]); turn_off(target:REF[STRING]). Shopping/Booking: add_to_cart(target:REF[STRING]); save_favorite(target:REF[STRING]); set_active_store(target:REF[STRING]); book_hotel(target:STRING<entity-name>); book_hotel(target:STRING<location-name>); select_schedule(target:REF[STRING]). Comm/Status: send_email(recipient:STRING<recipient-value>,[content:STRING<content-value>,tone:STRING<tone-value>]); send_message(recipient:STRING<recipient-value>,[content:STRING<content-value>,tone:STRING<tone-value>]); call(recipient:STRING<recipient-value>,[content:STRING<content-value>]); check_replied(target:STRING<recipient-value>,deadline:UTC_TIMESTAMP)->BOOL; check_support_status(target:STRING<entity-name>,metric:STRING<metric-value>)->BOOL; check_support_status(target:REF[STRING],metric:STRING<metric-value>)->BOOL; offer_discount(target:STRING<entity-name>,[content:STRING<content-value>,discount_percent:NUMBER]); offer_discount(target:REF[STRING],[content:STRING<content-value>,discount_percent:NUMBER]); offer_expedited_shipping(target:STRING<entity-name>); offer_expedited_shipping(target:REF[STRING]). Code/Files: modify_code(target:STRING<platform-name>,file:STRING<code-value>,[actual_output:STRING<code-value>,assertion:STRING<code-value>,call:STRING<code-value>,expected_output:STRING<code-value>,method:STRING<code-value>,property:STRING<code-value>,reproduction_step:STRING<code-value>,revision:STRING<code-value>]); modify_code(target:STRING<entity-name>,file:STRING<code-value>,[actual_output:STRING<code-value>,assertion:STRING<code-value>,call:STRING<code-value>,expected_output:STRING<code-value>,method:STRING<code-value>,property:STRING<code-value>,reproduction_step:STRING<code-value>,revision:STRING<code-value>]); run_tests(target:STRING<platform-name>,[assertion:STRING<code-value>,content:STRING<content-value>]); run_tests(target:STRING<entity-name>,[assertion:STRING<code-value>,content:STRING<content-value>]); add_file(target:STRING<platform-name>,file:STRING<code-value>,[content:STRING<content-value>]); add_file(target:STRING<entity-name>,file:STRING<code-value>,[content:STRING<content-value>]); delete_file(target:STRING<platform-name>,file:STRING<code-value>); delete_file(target:STRING<entity-name>,file:STRING<code-value>); file_age_days(file:STRING<code-value>)->NUMBER; path_in_folder(file:STRING<code-value>,source:STRING<code-value>)->BOOL. custom_<domain>_<action> requires target:STRING<entity-name> and may use content:STRING<content-value>.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Delete an old file from the file system.", "braincode": "ACTION delete_file(target=file_system, file=path_old_log)"}, "glossary_gloss": "Action performs an external operation using a complete, operation-specific signature. Overloads allow operations to accept different target categories without union types.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Provides an exhaustive, exact-typed signature table covering all existing operations, preserving Mind2Web and embodied coverage while enforcing N3 category provenance. Adds book_hotel, set_active_store, select_schedule.", "cites_source": "Why Agentic Systems Need Ontologies", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "operation-vocabulary", "glossary_gloss": "The initial index of normative Action and UTTER operations. Missing domains use a deterministic custom rule.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "open_page", "gloss": "Navigate to a page.", "nl_synonyms": ["go to"]}, {"symbol": "click", "gloss": "Click an element.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "select_filter", "gloss": "Apply one filter.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "apply_filters", "gloss": "Apply multiple filters.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "sort", "gloss": "Rank a list.", "nl_synonyms": ["rank", "order by"]}, {"symbol": "search_travel", "gloss": "Search travel.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "search_transit", "gloss": "Search transit.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "search_web", "gloss": "Search the web.", "nl_synonyms": ["find", "look for"]}, {"symbol": "fill_field", "gloss": "Fill a form field.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "submit", "gloss": "Submit a form.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "extract", "gloss": "Select members of a list.", "nl_synonyms": ["select"]}, {"symbol": "read_page", "gloss": "Read page content.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "save_favorite", "gloss": "Save to favorites.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "add_to_cart", "gloss": "Add to cart.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "set_active_store", "gloss": "Set active store.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "book_hotel", "gloss": "Book a hotel.", "nl_synonyms": ["book"]}, {"symbol": "select_schedule", "gloss": "Select a schedule.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "pick_up", "gloss": "Acquire an object.", "nl_synonyms": ["grab", "take"]}, {"symbol": "place", "gloss": "Put an object.", "nl_synonyms": ["put"]}, {"symbol": "heat", "gloss": "Heat an object.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "chill", "gloss": "Chill an object.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "rinse", "gloss": "Wash an object.", "nl_synonyms": ["wash"]}, {"symbol": "slice", "gloss": "Cut into pieces.", "nl_synonyms": ["chop", "cut"]}, {"symbol": "pour", "gloss": "Pour a liquid.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "open_container", "gloss": "Open a container.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "close_container", "gloss": "Close a container.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "turn_on", "gloss": "Turn on a device.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "turn_off", "gloss": "Turn off a device.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "modify_code", "gloss": "Change code.", "nl_synonyms": ["fix"]}, {"symbol": "run_tests", "gloss": "Run tests.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "add_file", "gloss": "Add a file.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "delete_file", "gloss": "Delete a file.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "send_email", "gloss": "Send email.", "nl_synonyms": ["email"]}, {"symbol": "send_message", "gloss": "Send message.", "nl_synonyms": ["text"]}, {"symbol": "call", "gloss": "Make a call.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "check_replied", "gloss": "Check for reply.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "file_age_days", "gloss": "Get file age.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "path_in_folder", "gloss": "Check path.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "create_list", "gloss": "Create a list.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "add_to_list", "gloss": "Add to list.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "check_support_status", "gloss": "Query support.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "offer_discount", "gloss": "Offer discount.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "offer_expedited_shipping", "gloss": "Offer shipping.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "ask", "gloss": "Ask a question.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "inform", "gloss": "State information.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "respond", "gloss": "Answer.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "propose", "gloss": "Propose an idea.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "correct", "gloss": "Correct a statement.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "acknowledge", "gloss": "Acknowledge.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "confirm", "gloss": "Confirm.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "decline", "gloss": "Decline.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "A self-contained deterministic mapping procedure: operations are strictly limited to the enumerated members. If a domain-specific operation is required but missing, it uses the atomic token rule custom_<domain>_<action>.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Examine a book.", "braincode": "ACTION custom_household_examine(target=book, content=content_examine)"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Adds missing operations book_hotel, set_active_store, select_schedule to align with the normative Action signatures.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Generate", "grammar": "generation ::= \"GENERATE\" \"(\" generate-attr (\",\" generate-attr)* \")\" \"->\" IDENT \":\" type\ngenerate-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value\n-- Legal attributes: target, audience, budget, character_properties, constraints, content, currency, duration, duration_unit, events, format, locale, max_walk_duration, max_walk_duration_unit, quantity, quantity_unit, stop_min_per_day, stop_requirement, style, tone, topic, transformations.", "semantics": "target requires STRING<artifact-value>; audience requires STRING<recipient-value>; tone, format, style, locale, currency, duration_unit, max_walk_duration_unit, and quantity_unit require their named categories; duration, quantity, max_walk_duration, stop_min_per_day, budget require NUMBER. constraints requires LIST[STRING<constraint-value>]; transformations requires LIST[STRING<transformation-value>]; events requires LIST[STRING<event-value>]; character_properties requires LIST[STRING<character-property-value>]. topic requires STRING<topic-value>. content requires STRING<content-value>. stop_requirement requires STRING<semantic-category-value>. Target is first; remaining attributes are alphabetical.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Write a 2-paragraph story about a camper.", "braincode": "GENERATE(target=art_story, events=[event_camper_in_sludge_pit], quantity=2, quantity_unit=unit_paragraph, topic=topic_camp_sludge) -> story : STRING"}, "glossary_gloss": "Generate creates a non-effectful artifact with governed descriptive constraints, topics, events, and transformations.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Restores max_walk_duration attributes, uses standard type production, and adds compositional lists for events and character_properties to improve expressivity.", "cites_source": "HTML", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Utterance", "grammar": "utterance ::= \"UTTER\" speech-act \"(\" utter-attr (\",\" utter-attr)* \")\" (\"->\" IDENT)?\nutter-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value\n-- Legal attributes are determined by the specific speech-act signature.", "semantics": "UTTER signatures are normative. ask(topic:STRING<topic-value>,[constraints:LIST[STRING<constraint-value>],recipient:STRING<recipient-value>,tone:STRING<tone-value>]); inform(topic:STRING<topic-value>,[recipient:STRING<recipient-value>,tone:STRING<tone-value>]); respond(topic:STRING<topic-value>,[recipient:STRING<recipient-value>]); propose(topic:STRING<topic-value>,[recipient:STRING<recipient-value>]); correct(topic:STRING<topic-value>,[recipient:STRING<recipient-value>]); acknowledge([recipient:STRING<recipient-value>]); confirm([recipient:STRING<recipient-value>,topic:STRING<topic-value>]); decline([recipient:STRING<recipient-value>,topic:STRING<topic-value>]). A bound UTTER result is STRING and must use content, content_2, etc.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Ask for realistic, respectful pickup lines.", "braincode": "CONVO PickupAdvice {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(topic=topic_pickup_lines, constraints=[constraint_realistic, constraint_respectful])\n  }\n}"}, "glossary_gloss": "Utterance records a speech act using exact normative signatures for ask, inform, etc., with named recipients, tones, topics, and structured constraints.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Defines exact legal attribute signatures for each speech act to prevent nonsensical combinations, bringing Utterance into full N3 compliance.", "cites_source": "Why Agentic Systems Need Ontologies", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Task", "grammar": "document ::= entrypoint (task | conversation)*\nentrypoint ::= \"ENTRYPOINT\" IDENT\ntask ::= \"TASK\" IDENT param_list? (\"CONTEXT\" execution_date_param)? (\":\" type)? (\"DECREASES\" IDENT)? \"{\" step+ return_stmt? \"}\"\nexecution_date_param ::= \"execution_date\" \"=\" ISO_DATE\nparam_list ::= \"(\" param (\",\" param)* \")\"\nparam ::= IDENT \":\" type\nreturn_stmt ::= \"RETURN\" value\nstep ::= action | flow_if | flow_for | bind | task_call | utterance | generation\ntask_call ::= IDENT arg_list? ( \"->\" IDENT )?\narg_list ::= \"(\" arg (\",\" arg)* \")\"\narg ::= IDENT \"=\" value", "semantics": "A BrainCode document declares exactly one ENTRYPOINT naming a top-level TASK or CONVO. Canonical encoding rules for N7: (1) Mandatory document wrapping: every request must be wrapped in an ENTRYPOINT and corresponding TASK or CONVO block. (2) Handle naming: bound variable names must derive from the target or result semantic name (e.g., `farms` for a list of farms, `farm_ref` for a single reference). (3) Optional modifiers: spatial relations (e.g. `relation=on`) are included only when explicitly stated in the natural language; otherwise omitted. `CONTEXT execution_date=ISO_DATE` is a translation-time-only annotation. Task names and Variable names are disjoint namespaces. Variable scoping is lexical and block-structured.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Go to the flight booking site, search flights from Tel Aviv to Berlin next Tuesday, and list the three cheapest options.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT BookFlight\n\nTASK BookFlight CONTEXT execution_date=\"2025-06-03\" : LIST[REF[STRING]] {\n  ACTION open_page(target=\"flight_booking_site\")\n  ACTION search_travel(date=\"2025-06-10\", destination=\"Berlin\", origin=\"Tel Aviv\") -> raw_flights : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION sort(rank_direction=dir_asc, rank_field=rank_price, target=raw_flights) -> sorted_flights : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION extract(limit=3, target=sorted_flights) -> cheapest_flights : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  RETURN cheapest_flights\n}"}, "glossary_gloss": "Task is a document-level container of steps. It enforces canonical encoding rules for document wrapping, handle naming, and optional modifiers to ensure deterministic translation.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Adds canonical encoding rules for N7 convergence as requested by the Critic.", "cites_source": null, "addresses_note": "N7"}]
Critic's decision: needs-rework
Critic's reasoning: The bundle makes real N3 progress by eliminating unqualified STRING from the revised Action, Generate, and Utterance signatures and by giving values explicit category provenance. It cannot be accepted because category provenance is undefined for overlapping symbols and because the Action and operation vocabularies directly contradict each other, producing an invalid sampled expression. The listed vocabulary additions are self-contained, non-regressive improvements and can land while the coupled type/signature revisions are repaired.
Required changes (address every one explicitly): [{"target": "Types & Lexicon", "change": "Replace the assertion that every unquoted symbol belongs to exactly one category with an unambiguous category-resolution rule. Either namespace category members so operation call and attribute call cannot collide, or state that static category provenance is resolved from the signature position and define how this applies to every overlapping token."}, {"target": "Action / operation-vocabulary", "change": "Make the two normative operation inventories identical. Add browse_trending to operation-vocabulary with its canonical mapping and signature, or remove its Action signature and provide a typed replacement. Audit every Action signature against operation-vocabulary in the same edit."}, {"target": "Action", "change": "Add a typed containment/placement form that permits destination=REF[STRING] when placing an acquired object into an acquired container, and add a compositional location-relation representation so one object can be on counter and in_front_of toaster without dropping either relation."}, {"target": "Task / Generate / Utterance", "change": "Publish a normative canonical selection rule for topic versus content versus events versus character_properties versus constraints, including when a proposition must be decomposed into multiple attributes rather than minted as one topic_/content_ atom. The current handle and attribute-order rules do not resolve this principal N7 divergence."}, {"target": "topic-value / constraint-value / event-value / character-property-value", "change": "Add compositional vocabulary or constructs for participants, propositions, causal relations, temporal/event ordering, comparisons, evidence/source and recency requirements, body-part relations, and multi-location relations. Do not treat an entire complex request as one newly minted topic or content symbol merely because the category is open."}, {"target": "Generate", "change": "Add typed food/meal, ingredient, preparation-method, preparation-time, dietary/nutrition, and satiety categories or a structured meal-plan signature. This is required for the dinner request to improve an agent's plan rather than merely label it with opaque constraints."}]
Logic issues: ["Types & Lexicon says an unquoted symbol belongs to exactly one category, but call is simultaneously an operation-vocabulary member and an attribute-name member. This makes category provenance and hence typed signature validation undefined.", "Action retains browse_trending but revised operation-vocabulary strictly limits operations to listed members and does not list browse_trending; the sampled trending-search expression therefore has no valid parse/operation-id.", "The Task worked example violates the proposal's own typed-signature semantics by supplying quoted STRING literals where search_travel and open_page require category-provenance symbols; it also places sort's rank attributes before target despite the stated target-first canonical ordering.", "The proposed Action signatures cannot express placement into an already bound container REF[STRING], and a single relation attribute cannot preserve multiple independently stated spatial relations.", "The claimed canonical N7 rules do not decide whether substance belongs in topic, content, event lists, character-property lists, or constraints; this remains visible in the independent translations."]
Pre-KPI assessment: {"coverage": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Typed signatures add coverage for code modification, hotel booking, itinerary constraints, symbolic generation constraints, and several speech acts. However, the revised operation vocabulary omits browse_trending while Action retains it, and the Action table cannot express the sampled cup-with-knife task because place accepts an entity-name/location-name destination but not a REF[STRING] container destination."}, "expressivity": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "The proposal captures several formerly prose-hidden attributes, including itinerary stop requirements, narrative events, character properties, code facts, output quantities, and constraints. But relational composition remains insufficient: a cup containing a knife and itself positioned both on a counter and in front of a toaster cannot be represented, while topic/content atoms still collapse complex propositions, evidence requirements, and relations into a single opaque symbol."}, "determinism": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Canonical attribute ordering, mandatory document wrapping, and typed operation signatures are genuine progress. But the core provenance claim is internally contradictory because call is both an operation-vocabulary member and an attribute-name member despite the rule that an unquoted symbol belongs to exactly one category; selection between topic, content, events, and constraints is also not canonically defined. Independent translations continue to diverge on artifact target, location symbol, return behavior, and whether an item requires a gap."}, "interpretability": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Operation-specific signatures make legal attributes substantially easier to inspect than the former transitional STRING channels. Conversely, the very large Action signature paragraph, overloaded symbols without a resolution rule, and a glossary index whose domains must be reconstructed from distant signatures make lookup and parsing less clear than claimed."}, "improvement": {"impact": "benefit", "reasoning": "A weaker planner benefits from knowing, for example, that stop_requirement is a semantic class, that code assertions/revisions have separate provenance rules, and that narrative events and character properties are lists. The added structure is operationally useful even though several complex requests still need more compositional relations and criteria."}}
Simulated examples that exposed gaps: [{"item_id": "held-trip-1", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "Plan a 3-day itinerary in Kyoto that includes at least one temple per day and avoids anything more than a 20-minute walk from the last stop.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PlanKyotoItinerary\nTASK PlanKyotoItinerary : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_itinerary, duration=3, duration_unit=unit_day, max_walk_duration=20, max_walk_duration_unit=unit_minute, stop_min_per_day=1, stop_requirement=class_temple, topic=topic_kyoto_trip) -> plan : STRING\n  RETURN plan\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "Generate and semantic-category-value preserve all actionable itinerary constraints; the proposed paragraph unit is irrelevant."}, {"item_id": "held-support-1", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "If the customer's order is late and they're a first-time buyer, offer a 10% discount; if they're a repeat buyer, offer free expedited shipping instead.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ResolveLateOrder\nTASK ResolveLateOrder {\n  ACTION check_support_status(target=order, metric=metric_order_late) -> is_late : BOOL\n  ACTION check_support_status(target=customer, metric=metric_first_time_buyer) -> is_first_time : BOOL\n  ACTION check_support_status(target=customer, metric=metric_repeat_buyer) -> is_repeat : BOOL\n  IF is_late AND is_first_time THEN {\n    ACTION offer_discount(target=order, discount_percent=10)\n  } ELSE {\n    IF is_repeat THEN {\n      ACTION offer_expedited_shipping(target=order)\n    }\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The exact Action signatures and existing metric-value category carry the branch conditions and discount quantity."}, {"item_id": "6ca55141-9ba6-4ed7-8c07-77df6c24029d", "source": "Mind2Web (osunlp/Mind2Web, train, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Find the lowest-priced gray-colored round-shaped mirror in stock in Atlanta, Georgia, with a maximum price of 20 dollars.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FindMirror\nTASK FindMirror : LIST[REF[STRING]] {\n  ACTION search_web(target=mirror, availability=avail_in_stock, color=color_gray, currency=curr_usd, location=atlanta_georgia, max_price=20, shape=shape_round) -> mirrors : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION sort(target=mirrors, rank_direction=dir_asc, rank_field=rank_price) -> sorted_mirrors : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  RETURN sorted_mirrors\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "Action provides a useful typed search-and-sort plan. The independent translators disagree on atlanta versus atlanta_georgia and whether to return the result."}, {"item_id": "62806bef-eeeb-4892-b4d5-6a8d2005c58d", "source": "Mind2Web (osunlp/Mind2Web, train, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Browse the trending searches in Columbus.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT BrowseTrendingSearches\nTASK BrowseTrendingSearches : LIST[REF[STRING]] {\n  ACTION browse_trending(target=trending_searches, location=columbus) -> searches : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  RETURN searches\n}", "coverage": "Fail", "notes": "The Action table retains browse_trending, but operation-id must be an operation-vocabulary member and the revised operation-vocabulary omits browse_trending. Thus this otherwise sensible expression is statically invalid."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190907_134455_194210#0", "source": "ALFRED (json_2.1.0, train)", "nl": "Place a white cup with a knife in it on the counter in front of the toaster.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PlaceCupWithKnife\nTASK PlaceCupWithKnife {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=knife) -> knife_ref : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION pick_up(target=cup, color=color_white) -> cup_ref : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=cup_ref, destination=counter, relation=on)\n}", "coverage": "Fail", "notes": "The valid fragment loses the knife-in-cup relation and the cup-in-front-of-toaster relation. place cannot take cup_ref as destination, and one relation attribute cannot encode both counter/on and toaster/in_front_of."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190908_185043_273617#2", "source": "ALFRED (json_2.1.0, train)", "nl": "Put a warm coffee cup in the coffee maker.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PlaceWarmCoffeeCup\nTASK PlaceWarmCoffeeCup {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=cup, state=state_warm) -> cup_ref : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=cup_ref, destination=coffee_maker, relation=in)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The state and spatial-relation categories preserve the requested final state and destination; the omitted heating trajectory is not required by the task-shaped request."}, {"item_id": "pydata__xarray-4356", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified (princeton-nlp/SWE-bench_Verified, test, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "sum: min_count is not available for reduction with more than one dimensions.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FixXarraySum\nTASK FixXarraySum {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=xarray, actual_output=outcome_min_count_error_multiple_dimensions, file=path_xarray_core_nanops_py, method=sym_sum, reproduction_step=repro_sum_min_count_multiple_dimensions, revision=chg_replace_mask_shape_axis_with_np_take_shape_product)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The code-value provenance rules and modify_code signature materially improve this request. The individual symbols are assumed to be complete-category members under N6."}, {"item_id": "django__django-12155", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified (princeton-nlp/SWE-bench_Verified, test, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "docutils reports an error rendering view docstring when the first line is not empty.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FixDjangoDocstringTrim\nTASK FixDjangoDocstringTrim {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=django, actual_output=outcome_default_role_no_content_error, file=path_django_contrib_admindocs_utils_py, method=sym_trim_docstring, reproduction_step=repro_nonempty_first_docstring_line, revision=chg_skip_first_line_when_computing_indent)\n  ACTION modify_code(target=django, file=path_django_contrib_admindocs_views_py, revision=chg_update_admindocs_docstring_rendering)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "Code-value categories support the files, method, failure, repro, and requested revisions, subject to N6's complete-category assumption."}, {"item_id": "c892", "source": "PRISM (HannahRoseKirk/prism-alignment, conversations config)", "nl": "The people in our country say that we are so generous and warm, but I know that people will look for a chance to take advantage of others as soon as they can.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT NationalTrustStatement\nCONVO NationalTrustStatement {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER inform(topic=topic_national_generosity_and_exploitation)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The expression records the speech act but the entire substantive proposition is a monolithic topic atom. This is formally symbolic under N6, but not a rich compositional account."}, {"item_id": "c5375", "source": "PRISM (HannahRoseKirk/prism-alignment, conversations config)", "nl": "Are androids better than iphones", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT AskPhoneComparison\nCONVO AskPhoneComparison {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(topic=topic_android_vs_iphone_comparison)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "Utterance's ask signature preserves the request type, but the comparison relation is hidden inside topic-value."}, {"item_id": "c2151", "source": "PRISM (HannahRoseKirk/prism-alignment, conversations config)", "nl": "it pains me to say but racism seems to be just a moving slider between one ethnic group to another. what is going on?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT AskRacismDynamics\nCONVO AskRacismDynamics {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(topic=topic_racism_between_ethnic_groups)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The question speech act is captured, but the user's emotional framing and causal metaphor have no independently compositional representation."}, {"item_id": "c1195", "source": "PRISM (HannahRoseKirk/prism-alignment, conversations config)", "nl": "I believe people with qualifications should be paid more in the workplace than those without any.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT QualificationsPayStatement\nCONVO QualificationsPayStatement {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER inform(topic=topic_qualifications_should_increase_workplace_pay)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The inform act is represented; the comparative policy proposition remains one topic-value atom."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-38835", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns)", "nl": "Create a newsletter in upto 800 words from Applied Observability.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT CreateObservabilityNewsletter\nTASK CreateObservabilityNewsletter : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_newsletter, content=content_applied_observability_source_article, format=format_newsletter, quantity=800, quantity_unit=unit_word, topic=topic_applied_observability) -> newsletter : STRING\n  RETURN newsletter\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The proposed quantity_unit addition helps. The supplied article is nonetheless collapsed into a content-value atom, with no symbolic representation of its claims, sources, examples, or requested selection."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-111541", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns)", "nl": "hi", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT Greeting\nCONVO Greeting {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER acknowledge()\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The acknowledgement speech act is sufficient for a greeting."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-55500", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns)", "nl": "Give a Longer Description Backstory about Donatello/Donnie meeting Dragon Ball Super characters with extensive god-like abilities.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT GenerateDonatelloBackstory\nTASK GenerateDonatelloBackstory : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_story, character_properties=[char_donatello_godlike, char_donatello_martial_artist, char_donatello_no_weaknesses], events=[event_donatello_meets_dragon_ball_super_characters], quantity=1, quantity_unit=unit_item, topic=topic_donatello_dragon_ball_super_crossover) -> story : STRING\n  RETURN story\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "event-value and character-property-value provide a better decomposition than one content atom, though the very long ability list still requires many assumed atomic members and has no ordering or causal structure."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-30875", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns)", "nl": "Hi,", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT Greeting\nCONVO Greeting {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER acknowledge()\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The acknowledgement speech act is sufficient for the sampled greeting."}, {"item_id": "1775708977070", "source": "ThoughtTrace (SCAI-JHU/ThoughtTrace)", "nl": "I need help planning a healthy light dinner for tonight that keeps me full and avoids late-night hunger. I prefer simple ingredients and something quick to prepare.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT GenerateLightDinnerPlan\nTASK GenerateLightDinnerPlan : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_meal_plan, constraints=[constraint_healthy, constraint_light, constraint_satiety, constraint_simple_ingredients, constraint_quick_preparation, constraint_avoid_late_night_hunger], topic=topic_tonight_dinner) -> dinner_plan : STRING\n  RETURN dinner_plan\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The request is structurally representable using assumed constraint-value members, but no food, meal, preparation-time, or nutrition-composition construct gives the planner executable meal-planning structure."}, {"item_id": "1775686840693", "source": "ThoughtTrace (SCAI-JHU/ThoughtTrace)", "nl": "o fungo nos dedos do pé, se eu passar a mão e depois passar a mão em outra parte do corpo, eu espalho o fungo de local?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT AskFungalTransmission\nCONVO AskFungalTransmission {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(topic=topic_foot_fungus_self_transmission)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The question act is represented, but the body-part relation and medical causality remain an opaque topic atom."}, {"item_id": "1775962320176", "source": "ThoughtTrace (SCAI-JHU/ThoughtTrace)", "nl": "Hello", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT Greeting\nCONVO Greeting {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER acknowledge()\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "No additional construct is needed for the greeting."}, {"item_id": "1775436940555", "source": "ThoughtTrace (SCAI-JHU/ThoughtTrace)", "nl": "I was absent from work for a week due to illness, while there were no vacations available to me at the time. I would like you to suggest an email message that I can send to my boss in a friendly manner so that he does not prevent me from working.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT GenerateReturnToWorkEmail\nTASK GenerateReturnToWorkEmail : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_email, audience=role_manager, constraints=[constraint_one_week_illness_absence, constraint_no_available_vacation, constraint_request_permission_to_resume_work], tone=tone_friendly, topic=topic_return_to_work_after_illness) -> email : STRING\n  RETURN email\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The email artifact, audience, tone, and stated conditions are symbolically typed under N6, but the desired message proposition is still distributed across assumed constraint atoms rather than a compositional message structure."}]
