      "semantics": "A BrainCode document declares exactly one ENTRYPOINT naming a top-level TASK or CONVO. Canonical encoding rules for N7: (1) Mandatory document wrapping: every request must be wrapped in an ENTRYPOINT and corresponding block. (2) Handle naming: bound variable names derive from the target semantic name (e.g., `farms` for a list of farms). (3) Canonical Attribute Selection: Do not mint a single `topic` or `content` atom for a complex request. Decompose it: use `events` for narrative sequences; `character_properties` for traits; `constraints` for explicit rules; `participants` for entities involved in a claim; `predicates` for relations/comparisons between participants; `evidence_requirements` for source rules. Use `topic` ONLY for the high-level subject matter. Use `content` only for literal text payloads. `CONTEXT execution_date=ISO_DATE` is a translation-time-only annotation.",
