utter-attr ::= attribute-name "=" value
-- Legal attributes are determined by the specific speech-act signature.` — UTTER signatures are normative. ask(topic:STRING<topic-value>,[constraints:LIST[STRING<constraint-value>],evidence_requirements:LIST[STRING<evidence-value>],participants:LIST[STRING<participant-value>],predicates:LIST[STRING<predicate-value>],recipient:STRING<recipient-value>,tone:STRING<tone-value>]); inform(topic:STRING<topic-value>,[constraints:LIST[STRING<constraint-value>],evidence_requirements:LIST[STRING<evidence-value>],participants:LIST[STRING<participant-value>],predicates:LIST[STRING<predicate-value>],recipient:STRING<recipient-value>,tone:STRING<tone-value>]); respond(topic:STRING<topic-value>,[recipient:STRING<recipient-value>]); propose(topic:STRING<topic-value>,[recipient:STRING<recipient-value>]); correct(topic:STRING<topic-value>,[recipient:STRING<recipient-value>]); acknowledge([recipient:STRING<recipient-value>]); confirm([recipient:STRING<recipient-value>,topic:STRING<topic-value>]); decline([recipient:STRING<recipient-value>,topic:STRING<topic-value>]). A bound UTTER result is STRING and must use content, content_2, etc.
- [revise] Task: grammar `document ::= entrypoint (task | conversation)*
entrypoint ::= "ENTRYPOINT" IDENT
task ::= "TASK" IDENT param_list? ("CONTEXT" execution_date_param)? (":" type)? ("DECREASES" IDENT)? "{" step+ return_stmt? "}"
execution_date_param ::= "execution_date" "=" ISO_DATE
param_list ::= "(" param ("," param)* ")"
param ::= IDENT ":" type
return_stmt ::= "RETURN" value
step ::= action | flow_if | flow_for | bind | task_call | utterance | generation
task_call ::= IDENT arg_list? ( "->" IDENT )?
arg_list ::= "(" arg ("," arg)* ")"
