  "summary": "Shaper proposed a large N3-compliance package: signature-position category provenance for all attribute types, an exhaustive rewrite of Action/Generate/Utterance signatures with typed categories, and new compositional vocabularies (predicate-value, participant-value, evidence-value, food-value, dietary-value) to decompose propositions and meal plans instead of using opaque topic/content atoms. The Critic ruled needs-rework despite crediting genuine N3 progress: overloaded signatures (e.g. open_page accepting both entity-name and platform-name targets) leave category provenance undecidable from position alone, and removing previously-legal quoted entity/recipient strings regressed hard note N2's no-coverage-loss requirement during the build phase — these two issues, plus unresolved proposition argument-role structure (participant+predicate lists can't bind roles, as shown in the Boris Johnson and veganism-claim simulations), were decisive. Doc hygiene passed, but the Critic's required changes (unique provenance rule, restored transitional string support, proposition argument roles, algorithmic handle naming) sent the proposal back for rework."
