   },
   "glossary_gloss": "Canonical-Form is the fixed rulebook making two independent translators write identical BrainCode: it defines exactly which messages count as 'the request' (ISR), picks TASK vs CONVO and turn/handle names mechanically, resolves which operation-id a phrase maps to, decides when repeated instances become repeated steps versus a FOR EACH loop, decomposes an explicit final-state request into a fixed causal stage order without inventing unstated steps, fixes how a conversational follow-up is REPLY_TO vs REVISES, and fixes attribute order everywhere.",
