  {
   "op": "revise",
   "construct_name": "Flow-If",
   "grammar": "flow_if ::= \"IF\" check \"THEN\" \"{\" step+ \"}\" ( \"ELSE\" \"{\" step+ \"}\" )?",
   "semantics": "Conditional branching, identical inside TASK and CONVO TURN bodies. The Check is evaluated when control reaches the IF; THEN runs if true, ELSE (if present) if false, otherwise control passes on. THEN/ELSE each open a fresh child scope, invisible to each other and to siblings. An IF nested in a TURN body may contain UTTER exactly as ACTION; the same nesting in a TASK body is a static error per Utterance's restriction. A preceding Action bound for use in the Check follows Canonical-Form's HNR, including the mandatory `_ref` suffix when the derived base would collide with a vocabulary symbol used as that Action's own `target`. When a Check depends on a preceding `check_replied` with a future `deadline`, the branch inherits that deferred timing.",
   "worked_example": {
