  {
   "op": "revise",
   "construct_name": "Task",
   "grammar": "document ::= entrypoint (task | conversation)*\ntask ::= \"TASK\" IDENT param_list? (\"CONTEXT\" execution_date_param)? (\":\" type)? (\"DECREASES\" IDENT)? \"{\" step+ return_stmt? \"}\"\nexecution_date_param ::= \"execution_date\" \"=\" ISO_DATE\nparam_list ::= \"(\" param (\",\" param)* \")\"\nparam ::= IDENT \":\" type\nreturn_stmt ::= \"RETURN\" value\nstep ::= action | flow_if | flow_for | bind | task_call | utterance | generation\ntask_call ::= IDENT arg_list? ( \"->\" IDENT )?\narg_list ::= \"(\" arg (\",\" arg)* \")\"\narg ::= IDENT \"=\" value\n-- ISO_DATE ::= exactly YYYY-MM-DD.",
   "semantics": "A document declares exactly one ENTRYPOINT naming a top-level TASK or CONVO, chosen by Canonical-Form's Input-Scope Rule (ISR) and Construct-Selection Rule (CSR) over the supplied request input only. The TASK's IDENT (and ENTRYPOINT name) is fixed by the Document-Naming Rule (DNR) from the first step's HNR base, after SOR fixes step order. If ENTRYPOINT names a TASK it takes zero parameters and runs once; other top-level TASKs are inert library declarations. `CONTEXT execution_date=ISO_DATE` is translation-time-only, resolving relative dates once, retained for audit, never re-read at runtime; malformed values are static errors. Task/Variable namespaces are disjoint; scoping is lexical and block-structured. `param_list`/`arg_list` use exact static type matching; a declared result type requires a matching terminal RETURN, else RETURN is forbidden. Recursion requires `DECREASES paramName` plus a per-call guarding IF-THEN. Steps are ordered, deduplicated/multiplied, and decomposed per Canonical-Form's SOR (including its Operation-Selection, Multiplicity, and Causal-Chain sub-rules), and every attribute list follows AOR.",
