   "semantics": "Legal Generate attributes: target, audience, content, topic, constraints, transformations, events, character_properties, duration, duration_unit, format, locale, quantity, quantity_unit, style, tone, stop_requirement, stop_min_per_day, max_walk_duration, max_walk_duration_unit — every one of these is a governed attribute-name member (see attribute-name vocabulary). `target` (always present) -> artifact-value and is also this step's HNR base, used verbatim as the bound result's IDENT unless the `_ref` collision rule applies. `audience`->recipient-value; `tone`->tone-value; `format`->format-value; `style`->style-value; `locale`->locale-value; `topic`->topic-value; `constraints`->LIST[constraint-value]; `transformations`->LIST[transformation-value]; `events`->LIST[event-value]; `character_properties`->LIST[character-property-value]; `stop_requirement`->semantic-category-value; `duration_unit`/`max_walk_duration_unit`/`quantity_unit`->duration-unit-value. `duration`, `quantity`, `stop_min_per_day`, `max_walk_duration` are NUMBER. `content` remains a transitional STRING channel pending N4, used only where no topic/content-value member yet exists. Canonical attribute order and result handle follow AOR/HNR.",
