   "user (None, score=None): how can i improve my lifestyle if im used to eating unhealthy food?",
   "model (command-light, score=99): It is possible to make small, gradual changes in your diet and lifestyle by incorporating healthier options. Here's a list of suggestions: \n\n1. Start by making small changes - Rather than overwhelming yourself by making drastic dietary changes, focus on making small, sustainable adjustments to your diet. Choose one or two healthy meals, or snacks each day to incorporate into your routine. For example, you can add more fruits or vegetables to your meal or as a snack. \n\n2. Replace unhealthy items with healthier alternatives - Choose healthier versions of the foods you usually consume. For instance, switch regular soda drinks with lemon water or unsweetened green tea. You can also experiment with low-fat or dairy-free yogurts. \n\n3. Add variety to your plate - Include a variety of colors, textures, and flavors in your meals. Different fruits and vegetables have different nutritional profiles and provide a wide range of health benefits. They also help in stabilizing your cravings for specific nutrients. \n\n4. Be mindful while eating - Give attention to your meal consumption. Focus on how the food tastes, and how it makes you feel emotionally and physically. Eating in front of the TV or while doing other activities might hinder your ability to recognize full satisfaction/hunger signals and may",
