 {
  "item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-5353",
  "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns, model=gpt-3.5-turbo-0301)",
  "domain": "GENERATING CREATIVE TEXT",
  "nl": "Write a 90 minute script for a GoT scene where Daenerys tries to talk with Sansa, Jon, and Arya, but all but Daenerys have northern accents that get thicker and slangier as the conversation goes on. Try your best to write Jon’s, Sansa’s, Arya’s dialogue in northern accents. Also include Daenerys starting to struggle as the accents get thicker. Also everything starts off normal and serious.",
  "trajectory_steps": [
   "assistant: FADE IN:\n\nEXT. WINTERFELL - DAY\n\nDaenerys, Jon, Sansa, and Arya are walking through the grounds of Winterfell. They all appear serious and focused.\n\nDAENERYS:\n(To Sansa)\nLady Stark, may we speak for a moment?\n\nSANSA:\nOf course, Your Grace.\n\nThey all stop walking and gather in a small circle.\n\nDAENERYS:\nI would like to discuss our next move in the upcoming battle.\n\nJON:\n(Smiling)\nAgreed. It's crucial we make a plan.\n\nARYA:\n(Grinning)\nI'm ready to stick them with the pointy end.\n\nSANSA:\n(Chuckling)\nArya, please. Let's be serious.\n\nDAENERYS:\n(Taken aback)\nIs there something funny?\n\nJON:\n(Quickly)\nNo, Your Grace. Sansa's right. We need to focus.\n\nDaenerys nods, then looks over at Arya.\n\nDAENERYS:\n(To Arya)\nWhat kind of weapons are you most comfortable with?\n\nARYA:\n(Grinning)\nThe ones with sharp edges.\n\nSANSA:\n(Smiling)\nArya's always been our best fighter.\n\nJON:\n(Agreeing)\nShe's a true warrior.\n\nDaenerys nods again, but seems to be struggling to keep up with the northern accents.\n\nDAENERYS:\n(To Sansa)\nWhat about the defenses here at Winterfell?\n\nSANSA:\n(Confidently)\nWe've been fortifying the walls and preparing our soldiers.\n\nARYA:\n(Nodding)\nAnd we have dragonglass ready for the White Walkers.\n\nJON:\n(Grinning)\nWe'll make them regret ever crossing us.\n\nDaenerys starts to look a bit panicked as the accents become thicker and slangier.\n\nDAENERYS:\n(Confused)\nI'm sorry, what was that?\n\nSANSA:\n(Raising her voice slightly)\nThe walls are secure and our troops are prepared.\n\nARYA:\n(A bit louder)\nAnd we have dragonglass for them walkers.\n\nJON:\n(Smiling widely)\nThey won't stand a chance.\n\nDaenerys looks completely lost at this point.\n\nDAENERYS:\n(Shaking her head)\nI'm sorry, I'm having trouble understanding.\n\nSANSA:\n(Realizing)\nOh, I'm sorry. We tend to slip into our native accents when we get comfortable.\n\nARYA:\n(Laughing)\nAye, sorry 'bout that.\n\nJON:\n(Chuckling)\nWe'll try to speak clearer.\n\nDaenerys nods, still looking a bit flustered.\n\nDAENERYS:\n(Tentatively)\nThank you. Let's continue with the planning.\n\nThey all continue walking and talking, with the occasional slip back into their natural accents.\n\nFADE OUT.",
   "user: Do your best to literally write the words of the dialogue of Jon, Arya, and Sansa, the way northerners say them. And actually add slang.",
   "assistant: Here's my attempt at writing the dialogue with northern accents and slang:\n\nDAENERYS:\n(To Sansa)\nLady Stark, may we speyk fer a moment?\n\nSANSA:\nOf course, yer grace.\n\nThey all stop walkin' and gather in a small circle.\n\nDAENERYS:\nI would like to discuss our next move in the upcomin' battle.\n\nJON:\n(Smiling)\nAgreed. It's crucial we make a plan.\n\nARYA:\n(Grinning)\nI'm ready to stick 'em with the pointy end.\n\nSANSA:\n(Chucklin')\nArya, please. Let's be serious.\n\nDAENERYS:\n(Taken aback)\nIs there somethin' funny?\n\nJON:\n(Quickly)\nNo, yer grace. Sansa's reyt. We need to focus.\n\nDaenerys nods, then looks over at Arya.\n\nDAENERYS:\n(To Arya)\nWhat kind of weapons are you most comfortable with?\n\nARYA:\n(Grinning)\nThe ones with sharp edges.\n\nSANSA:\n(Smiling)\nArya's always been our best fighter.\n\nJON:\n(Agreeing)\nShe's a true warrior.\n\nDaenerys nods again, but seems to be strugglin' to keep up with the northern accents.\n\nDAENERYS:\n(To Sansa)\nWhat aboot the defenses here at Winterfell?\n\nSANSA:\n(Confidently)\nWe've been fortifyin' the walls and preparin' our soldiers.\n\nARYA:\n(Nodding)\nAnd we have dragonglass ready for the White Walkers.\n\nJON:\n(Grinning)\nWe'll make 'em regret ever crossin' us.\n\nDaenerys starts to look a bit panicked as the accents become thicker and slangier.\n\nDAENERYS:\n(Confused)\nI'm sorry, what was that?\n\nSANSA:\n(Raising her voice slightly)\nThe walls are secure and oor troops are prepared.\n\nARYA:\n(A bit louder)\nAnd we have dragonglass for them walkers.\n\nJON:\n(Smiling widely)\nThey won't stand a chance.\n\nDaenerys looks completely lost at this point.\n\nDAENERYS:\n(Shaking her head)\nI'm sorry, I'm havin' trouble understandin'.\n\nSANSA:\n(Realizin')\nOh, I'm sorry. We tend to slip into oor native accents when we get comfortable.\n\nARYA:\n(Laughin')\nAye, sorry 'bout that.\n\nJON:\n(Chucklin')\nWe'll try to speak clearer.\n\nDaenerys nods, still lookin' a bit flustered.\n\nDAENERYS:\n(Tentatively)\nThank ye. Let's continue with the plannin'.\n\nThey all continue walkin' and talkin', with the occasional slip back into their natural accents.",
   "[annotations — LLM-generated, GPT-4o: coarse_tasks=['GENERATING CREATIVE TEXT'], writing_intents=[array(['GENERATE SCRIPT'], dtype=object)]]"
