1.20 - $2                |\n|                    | Sweet potatoes              | 4 medium    | £1.20 - £2.00            | $1.50 - $2.50            |\n| **Fruits**         | Bananas                     | 4 medium    | £0.50 - £0.80            | $0.60 - $1                |\n|                    | Apples                      | 3 medium    | £1.00 - £1.50            | $1.20 - $2                |\n|                    | Blueberries (frozen)        | 250g        | £2.00 - £3.00            | $2.50 - $4                |\n| **Other**          | Lactose-free protein powder  | 500g        | £15.00 - £25.00          | $20 - $30                |\n|                    | Chia seeds                  | 100g        | £1.50 - £2.50            | $2 - $3                  |\n|                    | Flaxseeds                   | 100g        | £1.00 - £2.00            | $1.20 - $2.50             |\n|                    | Black beans (canned)        | 2 cans      | £0.80 - £1.20            | $1 - $1.50               |\n|                    | Lentils (dry)               | 250g        | £1.00 - £1.50            | $1.20 - $2                |\n| **Total Estimated Cost** | | | **£70 - £100** | **$90 - $130** |\n\n---\n\n### **💰 Budget Breakdown**\n| **Category**       | **Cost (GBP)** | **Cost (USD)** |\n|--------------------|---------------|---------------|\n| **Proteins**       | £33 - £44     | $43 - $57     |\n| **Carbs**          | £7 - £11      | $9 - $14      |\n| **Fats**           | £13 - £20     | $17 - $26     |\n| **Vegetables**     | £7 - £11      | $9 - $14      |\n| **Fruits**         | £3 - £5       | $4 - $6       |\n| **Other**          | £20 - £32     | $26 - $42     |\n| **TOTAL**          | **£70 - £100**| **$90 - $130**|\n\n---\n### **💡 Money-Saving Tips**\n1. **Buy frozen fish/chicken** (often cheaper than fresh).\n2. **Use dried beans/lentils** instead of canned (soak overnight).\n3. **Choose store-brand oats, rice, and protein powder**.\n4. **Buy nuts in bulk** (cheaper per kg than small bags).\n5. **Seasonal veggies are cheaper** (e.g., swap asparagus for frozen green beans in winter).\n6. **Skip pre-cut veggies** (whole heads of broccoli/carrots are cheaper).\n\n---\n### **🛒 Where to Shop for Best Prices**\n| **Country** | **Cheapest Options** | **Mid-Range** | **Premium** |\n|------------|---------------------|--------------|------------|\n| **UK**     | Aldi, Lidl           | Tesco, Sainsbury’s | Waitrose, Ocado |\n| **US**     | Walmart, Aldi        | Kroger, Publix | Whole Foods, Trader Joe’s |\n| **Canada** | No Frills, Superstore | Loblaws, Sobeys | Whole Foods |\n| **Australia** | Woolworths Homebrand | Coles, IGA | Harris Farm |\n\n---\n### **📝 Meal Prep Tips to Save Time & Money**\n✔ **Cook proteins in bulk** (bake chicken/turkey for 3-4 days).\n✔ **Roast veggies in advance** (keep in fridge for 3-4 days).\n✔ **Use rice cooker** (hands-off cooking for grains).\n✔ **Portion nuts/seeds** (pre-portion to avoid overeating).\n✔ **Freeze extras** (e.g., cook 2x salmon and freeze half).\n\n---\n### **🚫 What to Avoid (Waste of Money)**\n❌ **Pre-marinated meats** (expensive, often high in sugar).\n❌ **Pre-cut veggies/fruits** (markup is huge).\n❌ **Expensive protein powders** (stick to store brands like **MyProtein, Bulk, or Optimum Nutrition**).\n❌ **Single-serve nut packs** (buy in bulk and portion yourself).\n\n---\n### **🔄 Substitutions (If Something’s Unavailable)**\n| **Missing Item** | **Swap** |\n|------------------|----------|\n| Salmon → Cod or mackerel | |\n| Quinoa → Bulgur wheat or couscous | |\n| Tahini → Peanut butter (for dressings) | |\n| Avocado → Extra olive oil + nuts | |\n| Lactose-free protein → Pea protein or soy protein | |\n\n---\n### **📌 Final Notes**\n- **Total cost:** **£70-£100 (~$90-$130)** for **5 days**.\n- **Per day cost:** **£14-£20 (~$18-$26)**.\n- **Protein powder is the biggest expense**—if budget is tight, prioritize other proteins (chicken, turkey, eggs if tolerated).\n- **Leftovers?** Freeze