  "nl": "hey i am planning on a weekend trip to sedona arizona in June. I will be going from Thursday to Sunday. Please draft a potential itenerary. I will fly out from Orlando to Phoenix on Thursday at 5 AM. I will be flying back sunday from phoenix to orlando at 10am. I am interested in hikes, shopping, and visiting places of natural beauty. I will be staying at an air bnb in town and am willing to drive up to 2 hours away for sights",
  "trajectory_steps": [
   "assistant: # Sedona Weekend Itinerary - June Trip 🌵\n\n---\n\n## Thursday\n\n**Early Morning - Travel Day**\n- 5:00 AM - Depart Orlando\n- Arrive Phoenix (roughly 7-8 AM local time with time zone change)\n- Pick up rental car at Phoenix Sky Harbor Airport\n- **Drive to Sedona** - approximately 2 hours from Phoenix\n\n**Midday - Arrive & Settle In**\n- Check into your Airbnb\n- Grab lunch in town - check out **Tlaquepaque Arts & Shopping Village** area for food options\n- Explore the shops at Tlaquepaque - great local art, jewelry, and souvenirs\n\n**Afternoon/Evening**\n- Take an easy, scenic hike to shake off travel fatigue\n- **Airport Mesa Trail** is a great first hike - relatively easy, stunning 360° red rock views, perfect for sunset\n- Grab dinner on **Uptown Sedona** - tons of restaurant options along AZ-89A\n\n> ☀️ **June heads up** - temperatures can reach 95-100°F. Plan hikes for early morning or evening whenever possible\n\n---\n\n## Friday\n\n**Early Morning**\n- Wake up early (6:00-6:30 AM) to beat the heat\n- **Devil's Bridge Trail** - probably the most iconic hike in Sedona\n  - About 4 miles round trip\n  - Features a stunning natural sandstone arch you can walk across\n  - Gets very crowded midday so early start is key\n  - Requires a parking shuttle or early arrival to access trailhead\n\n**Late Morning**\n- Cool down and grab breakfast/brunch back in town\n- **Uptown Sedona shopping** - browse the many boutiques, crystal shops, and galleries\n- Check out some of Sedona's famous **vortex sites** - Sedona is known for its spiritual energy spots\n  - **Bell Rock** is easy to access and walk around\n\n**Afternoon**\n- Rest during peak heat hours (12-3 PM) - this is important in June\n- Relax at the Airbnb or explore indoor shops and galleries\n\n**Evening**\n- Drive to **Slide Rock State Park** for a late afternoon swim 🏊\n  - Natural rock water slides in Oak Creek Canyon\n  - Only about 7 miles north of town\n  - Great way to cool off\n- Dinner back in Sedona - try **Elote Cafe** (reservations recommended) or **Mariposa Latin Inspired Grill** for upscale dining\n\n---\n\n## Saturday\n\n**Early Morning**\n- **Cathedral Rock Trail** at sunrise 🌅\n  - One of the most photographed spots in Arizona\n  - About 1.5 miles but moderately strenuous with some scrambling\n  - The sunrise colors on the red rocks are absolutely spectacular\n  - Arrive by 5:30-6:00 AM\n\n**Mid Morning**\n- Drive to the **Grand Canyon South Rim** - approximately 2 hours from Sedona\n  - This fits within your 2 hour driving radius\n  - Walk the **Rim Trail** for breathtaking views\n  - Check out **Mather Point** and **Yavapai Point**\n  - Visit the **Grand Canyon Visitor Center**\n\n> 🏜️ Grand Canyon in June is hot but absolutely worth it. Bring lots of water and sun protection\n\n**Afternoon**\n- Have lunch at the Grand Canyon - **El Tovar Dining Room** or grab something casual at the Bright Angel Lodge\n- Head back toward Sedona (stop in **Williams, AZ** if you want a quick Route 66 photo op)\n\n**Evening**\n- Back in Sedona for dinner\n- **Stargazing** - Sedona has remarkably dark skies and June nights are warm and clear\n  - Airport Mesa or any spot outside town is great for this\n\n---\n\n## Sunday\n\n**Early Morning**\n- Wake up early and pack up the Airbnb\n- Quick sunrise walk or coffee on the porch - soak in those last red rock views\n\n**Morning**\n- Depart Sedona by 6:30-7:00 AM for Phoenix\n- 2 hour drive back to Sky Harbor Airport\n- Return rental car\n- **Arrive airport by 8:00-8:30 AM** for your 10:00 AM flight\n\n> ✈️ Give yourself plenty of buffer time - Phoenix airport can be busy on Sunday mornings\n\n---\n\n## General Tips for June in Sedona 📝\n\n| Tip | Detail |\n|-----|--------|\n| **Hydration** | Bring at least 2-3 liters of water per hike |\n| **Sun Protection** | Sunscreen, hat, and sunglasses are essential |\n| **Start Early** | Hit trails by 6-7 AM before heat peaks |\n| **Parking** | Many trailheads require a **Red Rock Pass** (~$5/day) |\n| **Reservations** | Book popular restaurants in advance |\n| **Shoes** | Wear proper hiking shoes - trails are rocky |\n\n---\n\n## Quick Highlights Summary\n- 🥾 **Hikes:** Devil's Bridge, Airport Mesa, Cathedral Rock\n- 🛍️ **Shopping:** Tlaquepaque, Uptown Sedona\n- 🌄 **Natural Beauty:** Grand Canyon, Slide Rock, Bell Rock, Oak Creek Canyon\n\nHave an amazing trip! Sedona in June is stunning - just respect the heat and you'll have a fantastic time! 🌵",
