   "user: Great can you add in specific times so i can stay on schedule and make sure i hit everything i want",
   "  [feedback: context_grounding_and_constraints] want to be hyperspecific in my timeline to not overwhelm myself and stay on schedule",
   "assistant: # Sedona Weekend Itinerary - June Trip 🌵\n*With Detailed Schedule*\n\n---\n\n## Thursday\n\n| Time | Activity | Notes |\n|------|----------|-------|\n| **5:00 AM** | Depart Orlando International Airport | Arrive at airport by 3:30 AM for early flight |\n| **7:00-7:30 AM** | Arrive Phoenix Sky Harbor (MST) | Orlando is EST, gain 3 hours |\n| **7:30-8:15 AM** | Pick up rental car & grab breakfast near airport | Grab coffee and food before the drive - long day ahead |\n| **8:15 AM** | Depart Phoenix for Sedona | ~2 hour drive via I-17 N to AZ-179 |\n| **10:15 AM** | Arrive Sedona - Check into Airbnb | Drop bags, freshen up, change clothes |\n| **11:00 AM** | Head to Tlaquepaque Arts & Shopping Village | Browse shops, galleries, and local art |\n| **12:30 PM** | Lunch near Tlaquepaque | Try **René at Tlaquepaque** or nearby options |\n| **2:00 PM** | **Airport Mesa Trail** | Easy hike, great intro to Sedona red rocks |\n| **3:30 PM** | Return to Airbnb | Rest and recover from early morning travel |\n| **5:00 PM** | Explore **Uptown Sedona** shops | Crystals, jewelry, souvenirs, local boutiques |\n| **7:00 PM** | Dinner in Uptown Sedona | Try **Dahl & Di Luca** or **Picazzo's** |\n| **8:30 PM** | Evening stroll or relax at Airbnb | Early bedtime recommended - big day Friday! |\n| **9:30 PM** | Bedtime | Need to be up by 5:30 AM |\n\n> 💤 You will have been awake since roughly 3 AM EST - don't push too hard Thursday evening. Rest is important!\n\n---\n\n## Friday\n\n| Time | Activity | Notes |\n|------|----------|-------|\n| **5:30 AM** | Wake up | |\n| **5:45 AM** | Light breakfast at Airbnb | Prep snacks and water for hike |\n| **6:15 AM** | Depart for Devil's Bridge Trailhead | Arrive early to secure parking or catch shuttle |\n| **6:30 AM** | **Begin Devil's Bridge Trail** | 4 miles round trip - starts cool and shaded |\n| **9:00 AM** | Complete Devil's Bridge hike | Take lots of photos on the arch! |\n| **9:15 AM** | Drive back toward town | |\n| **9:45 AM** | Breakfast/Brunch | Try **The Hudson** or **Coffee Pot Restaurant** |\n| **11:00 AM** | **Bell Rock** visit and walk around | Easy, flat walk - great vortex site |\n| **12:00 PM** | Head back to Airbnb | |\n| **12:30 PM** | **Rest period** - avoid peak heat | Relax, nap, stay hydrated indoors |\n| **2:30 PM** | More Uptown Sedona shopping | Finish any browsing from Thursday |\n| **4:00 PM** | Drive to **Slide Rock State Park** | Only 7 miles north - about 15 min drive |\n| **4:15 PM** | **Slide Rock State Park** | Swim, cool off in Oak Creek, enjoy the scenery |\n| **6:00 PM** | Depart Slide Rock | |\n| **6:30 PM** | Freshen up at Airbnb | Change for dinner |\n| **7:30 PM** | Dinner | **Elote Cafe** or **Mariposa Latin Inspired Grill** - book ahead! |\n| **9:00 PM** | Return to Airbnb | |\n| **9:30 PM** | Bedtime | Early start again Saturday |\n\n> 🌊 Check Slide Rock State Park hours in advance - they sometimes limit entry capacity in summer\n\n---\n\n## Saturday\n\n| Time | Activity | Notes |\n|------|----------|-------|\n| **5:00 AM** | Wake up | |\n| **5:15 AM** | Quick snack and water prep | Sunrise hike today! |\n| **5:30 AM** | Depart for Cathedral Rock Trailhead | 10 min drive from most Airbnbs in town |\n| **5:45 AM** | **Begin Cathedral Rock Trail** | 1.5 miles - aim to reach top by sunrise ~5:15 AM (adjust based on exact June sunrise time) |\n| **7:30 AM** | Complete Cathedral Rock hike | |\n| **8:00 AM** | Return to Airbnb - Breakfast | Eat a solid meal before Grand Canyon drive |\n| **9:00 AM** | **Depart for Grand Canyon South Rim** | ~2 hour drive via AZ-89A to AZ-64 |\n| **11:00 AM** | **Arrive Grand Canyon South Rim** | Stop at **Mather Point** first - most iconic view |\n| **11:15 AM** | Walk the **Rim Trail** | Mather Point → Yavapai Point section is stunning |\n| **12:30 PM** | **Yavapai Geology Museum** | Free, air conditioned, great canyon overview |\n| **1:15 PM** | Lunch at Grand Canyon | **Bright Angel Lodge** casual dining or grab a quick bite |\n| **2:15 PM** | Continue Rim Trail or visit **Desert View Watchtower** | Desert View is 25 miles east but worth it for unique views |\n| **3:30 PM** | Begin drive back to Sedona | Stop in **Williams, AZ** for a quick Route 66 photo if interested |\n| **5:30 PM** | Arrive back in Sedona | |\n| **6:00 PM** | Freshen up at Airbnb | |\n| **7:00 PM** | Dinner in Sedona | Try somewhere you haven't been yet - **Cucina Rustica** or **Wildflower Bread Company** |\n| **8:30 PM** | **Stargazing** | Drive to Airport Mesa or any dark spot outside town - bring a blanket |\n| **10:00 PM** | Return to Airbnb | |\n| **10:30 PM** | Pack bags for departure | Don't leave this for Sunday morning! |\n| **11:00 PM** | Bedtime | Last early morning ahead |\n\n> 🌅 June sunrise in Sedona is around **5:15 AM** - adjust Cathedral Rock start time accordingly if you want to catch it at the top\n\n---\n\n## Sunday\n\n| Time | Activity | Notes |\n|------|----------|-------|\n| **5:30 AM** | Wake up | |\n| **5:45 AM** | Quick breakfast and final pack | Coffee, light food |\n| **6:15 AM** | Last look around Airbnb | Don't forget chargers, toiletries, etc. |\n| **6:30 AM** | **Depart Sedona for Phoenix** | ~2 hour drive |\n| **8:30 AM** | Arrive Phoenix Sky Harbor | |\n| **8:30-9:00 AM** | Return rental car | Budget 20-30 min for this process |\n| **9:00 AM** | Clear security | Give yourself full hour before flight |\n| **10:00 AM** | **Depart Phoenix for Orlando** | |\n| **5:00-6:00 PM** | Arrive Orlando (EST) | Welcome back! |\n\n> ✈️ **Sunday is tight** - do not linger in Sedona past 6:30 AM. The 2 hour drive plus rental car return plus security leaves very little buffer\n\n---\n\n## Full Trip At A Glance\n\n| Day | Morning | Afternoon | Evening |\n|-----|---------|-----------|---------|\n| **Thursday** | Fly & Drive to Sedona | Tlaquepaque Shopping & Airport Mesa Hike | Uptown Sedona Dinner |\n| **Friday** | Devil's Bridge Hike | Rest & Shopping | Slide Rock & Nice Dinner |\n| **Saturday** | Cathedral Rock Sunrise | Grand Canyon | Stargazing |\n| **Sunday** | Pack & Drive to Phoenix | Fly Home | Back in Orlando |\n\n---\n\n## Packing Checklist for June 📋\n\n- [ ] Sunscreen (SPF 50+)\n- [ ] Wide brim hat\n- [ ] Sunglasses\n- [ ] Hiking shoes\n- [ ] 2-3 water bottles or hydration pack\n- [ ] Light, breathable clothing\n- [ ] Layers for early morning hikes (it cools down at night)\n- [ ] Snacks for hikes\n- [ ] Red Rock Pass ($5/day or $15 weekly pass)\n- [ ] Camera or phone with extra storage\n- [ ] Portable phone charger\n\n---\n\nHave an incredible trip! 🌵🌄",
   "  [feedback: explicit_affirmation] gave exactly what I wanted plus a checklist at the end anticipating a need for that also.",
   "user: Can you rank all of the resturaunts youve mentioned?",
   "  [feedback: content_expectation] since AI gave me options I want to have information to make decisions.",
   "assistant: # Sedona Restaurant Rankings 🍽️\n\n*Based on overall reputation, food quality, atmosphere, and visitor experience*\n\n---\n\n## Tier 1 - Must Try ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\n\n| Rank | Restaurant | Cuisine | Price Range | Why It Stands Out |\n|------|-----------|---------|-------------|-------------------|\n| **#1** | **Elote Cafe** | Upscale Mexican | $$$ | Widely considered the best restaurant in Sedona. Chef Jeff Smedstad's menu is creative and locally celebrated. The elote (street corn) appetizer alone is worth the visit. Book weeks in advance |\n| **#2** | **Mariposa Latin Inspired Grill** | Latin/American | $$$$ | Stunning red rock views from the patio, exceptional food, and incredible atmosphere. One of the most beautiful dining settings in Arizona. Reservations essential |\n| **#3** | **René at Tlaquepaque** | French/Continental | $$$$ | Elegant dining inside the beautiful Tlaquepaque village. Long standing Sedona institution with excellent food and romantic atmosphere |\n\n---\n\n## Tier 2 - Excellent Choice ⭐⭐⭐⭐\n\n| Rank | Restaurant | Cuisine | Price Range | Why It Stands Out |\n|------|-----------|---------|-------------|-------------------|\n| **#4** | **Dahl & Di Luca** | Italian | $$$ | Beloved local Italian spot with cozy atmosphere and consistently great pasta and wine. Very popular with locals which is always a good sign |\n| **#5** | **Cucina Rustica** | Italian/Mediterranean | $$$ | Sister restaurant to Dahl & Di Luca, slightly more upscale with a beautiful hacienda setting. Great for a special evening out |\n| **#6** | **The Hudson** | American/Brunch | $$$ | Excellent brunch spot with creative dishes and a great patio. One of the better breakfast and lunch options in Sedona |\n\n---\n\n## Tier 3 - Solid & Reliable ⭐⭐⭐\n\n| Rank | Restaurant | Cuisine | Price Range | Why It Stands Out |\n|------|-----------|---------|-------------|-------------------|\n| **#7** | **Picazzo's** | Organic Italian/Pizza | $$ | Great casual option with organic ingredients and gluten free options. Good for a relaxed dinner without needing reservations |\n| **#8** | **Coffee Pot Restaurant** | American Diner/Breakfast | $ | Sedona institution open since 1950. Famous for having over 100 omelette options. Nothing fancy but a fun, classic diner experience great for a quick pre hike breakfast |\n| **#9** | **Wildflower Bread Company** | Bakery/Cafe | $ | Think Panera but local and better. Great for a quick casual meal. Good sandwiches, soups, and baked goods. Convenient and affordable |\n\n---\n\n## Grand Canyon Addition ⭐⭐⭐\n\n| Rank | Restaurant | Cuisine | Price Range | Why It Stands Out |\n|------|-----------|---------|-------------|-------------------|\n| **#10** | **El Tovar Dining Room** | American | $$$ | Historic and iconic restaurant right on the canyon rim. The location and atmosphere are unmatched. Food is solid but you are mostly paying for the experience and history |\n| **#11** | **Bright Angel Lodge Dining** | American Casual | $$ | Convenient and decent food. More about fueling up than fine dining. Good option given its location at the canyon |\n\n---\n\n## Summary Cheat Sheet\n\n| Priority | Restaurant | Best For |\n|----------|-----------|----------|\n| 🥇 **Book First** | Elote Cafe | Best overall food in Sedona |\n| 🌄 **Best Views** | Mariposa | Dining with red rock scenery |\n| 🍝 **Best Italian** | Dahl & Di Luca | Cozy local favorite |\n| 🍳 **Best Breakfast** | Coffee Pot Restaurant | Pre hike fuel |\n| 💰 **Best Budget** | Wildflower Bread Company | Quick and affordable |\n| 🏛️ **Most Historic** | El Tovar | Grand Canyon experience |\n\n---\n\n## Reservation Tips 📅\n\n> - **Elote Cafe** - Book 2-4 weeks in advance for June. They do not take reservations for the full party until everyone is present\n> - **Mariposa** - Book at least 1-2 weeks ahead, request a patio table for views\n> - **René at Tlaquepaque** - A few days to a week should be sufficient\n> - **Everything else** - Walk in friendly but calling ahead never hurts in peak June season\n\n---\n\n*Note: Always check current reviews on Google or Yelp before your trip as restaurant quality can change over time* 🌟",
   "  [feedback: explicit_affirmation] I like that it gives me them all separated by quality and by price. I also like that it broke them down into best of each type of resturaunt and vibe."
  ]
 },
