Shaper proposal: {"summary": "This increment establishes a single canonical-form rulebook for request scope, construct selection, operation mapping, decomposition, ordering, and naming. It also makes placement acquisition explicit, permits governed topic/constraint attributes on UTTER, and defines character-count units.", "note_position": "comply", "note_argument": "The changes replace translator discretion with mechanical scope, naming, ordering, operation-selection, multiplicity, placement, and temporal-anchor rules. Every resulting expression remains uniquely parseable while preserving the current build-phase STRING channels.", "foundations_overview": "BrainCode remains a statically typed context-free language, now with a normative canonical-form layer over its grammar. Canonical form fixes translation choices that grammar alone cannot determine: which supplied messages are encoded, whether they form a TASK or CONVO, canonical operation identifiers, action decomposition, source order, attribute order, and generated identifiers. Parsing remains determined by the context-free grammar; canonical form determines one preferred encoding among otherwise grammatical expressions.", "rebuttals": [], "changes": [{"op": "add", "construct_name": "canonical-form", "grammar": "-- No independent production. Normative translation rules referenced by Task, Conversation, Action, Generate, Bind, and Flow-If.", "semantics": "Canonical Form applies only to the supplied request field through its final human-authored message (ISR); evaluation traces, annotations, and omitted transcript turns are excluded. CSR emits a TASK for one supplied human message requiring ACTION or GENERATE; otherwise it emits a CONVO. A multi-message supplied input, an in-scope AGENT message, or an explicit correction marker emits one CONVO TURN per supplied message in order. TURN names are T1, T2, ...; the ENTRYPOINT and sole top-level declaration use PascalCase of the first step handle base. AOR orders attributes as target first, audience second, then remaining names in ASCII alphabetical order. HNR: an Action result base is its bare vocabulary-symbol target, otherwise its operation-id; a Generate result base is its artifact target; a task-call result base is its callee in snake_case; LET uses its first consuming attribute name, otherwise cond_1, cond_2, .... If that base is also a bare vocabulary symbol occurring anywhere as a literal value in the same body, append _ref; then append _2, _3, ... for repeated bases in source order. OSR first NFC-normalizes and Unicode-casefolds source text, treats whitespace and punctuation runs as separators, and finds maximal source spans exactly matching a synonym string in operation-vocabulary. Overlapping matches select the longest span, then the lexicographically smallest canonical operation-id. Each selected span emits its mapped operation; conjunction-separated matched spans are separate operations. An unmatched requested operation emits custom_general_x<bytes>, where <bytes> is the UTF-8 byte sequence of its normalized predicate span, each hexadecimal nibble encoded a-p; this is deterministic and matches operation-vocabulary's custom-token form. SOR orders dependent steps after their producers; independent steps retain source-span order; exact ties use operation-id order. An explicit numeric physical-entity count emits one independent sequence per unit; a prior LIST emits one FOR EACH. Direct imperative placement entails pick_up followed by place: each unit first binds the selected entity REF, then place consumes that REF. Explicit final states use ACQUIRE < TRANSFORM < CONDITION < PLACE, omitting unstated stages except this mandatory acquisition for PLACE. Relative dates require TASK CONTEXT execution_date; absent CONTEXT is a translation error, never a prose date. A correction changing a prior request's attributes is REVISES; pure continuation is REPLY_TO with constraint_continuation; unrelated follow-up is REPLY_TO.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Put two forks in the sink.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT Fork\n\nTASK Fork {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=fork) -> fork_ref : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=fork_ref, destination=sink)\n  ACTION pick_up(target=fork) -> fork_ref_2 : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=fork_ref_2, destination=sink)\n}"}, "glossary_gloss": "Canonical Form is the fixed translation rulebook for BrainCode. It decides request scope, TASK versus CONVO, operation mapping, decomposition, ordering, and generated names so independent encoders produce the same expression.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "N7 requires one encoding rather than merely one parse. This centralizes the mandatory choices and repairs prior undefined synonym matching, placement acquisition, temporal anchoring, and inconsistent handle examples.", "cites_source": "Formal language theory", "addresses_note": "N7"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Bind", "grammar": "bind ::= \"LET\" IDENT \":\" type \"=\" value\n-- Additional bind sites: action_result ::= \"->\" IDENT \":\" type ; task_call_result ::= \"->\" IDENT ; utterance_result ::= \"->\" IDENT ; generation_result ::= \"->\" IDENT \":\" type", "semantics": "Bind gives names to LET values and Action, task-call, UTTER, and GENERATE results. LET requires an exact static type match; a REF may only copy a visible REF of the same type. Every derived name follows Canonical Form HNR, including mandatory _ref when its unsuffixed base is also a literal vocabulary symbol in the same body. Scope, no-shadowing, and source-order visibility are unchanged.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Rinse one mug in the sink, then place that same mug in the coffee maker.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT Mug\n\nTASK Mug {\n  ACTION rinse(target=mug, destination=sink) -> mug_ref : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=mug_ref, destination=coffee_maker)\n}"}, "glossary_gloss": "Bind gives a value a name for later steps in its allowed scope. Canonical Form makes derived names predictable and adds _ref whenever a handle would otherwise look exactly like a vocabulary value.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Makes handle naming lexical and mechanical rather than dependent on inferred type or author preference.", "cites_source": "Formal language theory", "addresses_note": "N7"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Task", "grammar": "document ::= entrypoint (task | conversation)*\ntask ::= \"TASK\" IDENT param_list? (\"CONTEXT\" execution_date_param)? (\":\" type)? (\"DECREASES\" IDENT)? \"{\" step+ return_stmt? \"}\"\nexecution_date_param ::= \"execution_date\" \"=\" ISO_DATE\nparam_list ::= \"(\" param (\",\" param)* \")\"\nparam ::= IDENT \":\" type\nreturn_stmt ::= \"RETURN\" value\nstep ::= action | flow_if | flow_for | bind | task_call | utterance | generation", "semantics": "A TASK is the canonical encoding of a single supplied human request that requires ACTION or GENERATE. Its declaration and ENTRYPOINT names, step order, repeated physical-object sequences, result handles, and attribute order follow Canonical Form. Relative temporal language is legal only when TASK CONTEXT supplies a valid execution_date anchor, which resolves it once at translation time. All existing typing, recursion, return, and lexical-scoping rules remain unchanged.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Find fitness events for this weekend, assuming today is 2025-06-03.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FitnessEvent\n\nTASK FitnessEvent CONTEXT execution_date=\"2025-06-03\" {\n  ACTION search_web(target=fitness_event, date=\"2025-06-07\") -> fitness_event_ref : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n}"}, "glossary_gloss": "Task is the single-request container for work requiring an action or generated artifact. Its name, step sequence, handles, and relative-date resolution follow Canonical Form.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Connects TASK translation to the canonical rules and prevents unsupported prose relative dates.", "cites_source": "HTML", "addresses_note": "N7"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Conversation", "grammar": "conversation ::= \"CONVO\" IDENT \"{\" turn+ \"}\"\nturn ::= \"TURN\" IDENT \"SPEAKER\" \"=\" speaker_lit (\"REPLY_TO\" IDENT)? (\"REVISES\" IDENT)? \"{\" step+ \"}\"\nspeaker_lit ::= \"USER\" | \"AGENT\"", "semantics": "CONVO is selected by Canonical Form for a supplied multi-message input, an in-scope AGENT message, an explicit correction, or a single non-effectful request. It contains exactly one TURN per supplied message, in source order, with T1, T2, ... names. A changed prior request is REVISES; a continuation or unrelated response is REPLY_TO. Existing whole-body replacement, linear revision-chain, and per-turn scope rules remain unchanged.", "worked_example": {"nl": "User: Explain mash potato. User: Actually, explain it without peeling the potato.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT Ask\n\nCONVO Ask {\n  TURN T1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(topic=topic_mash_potato_method)\n  }\n  TURN T2 SPEAKER=USER REVISES T1 {\n    UTTER ask(constraints=[constraint_no_peeling], topic=topic_mash_potato_method)\n  }\n}"}, "glossary_gloss": "Conversation records the supplied conversational messages in a fixed order. Canonical Form fixes turn names and whether a follow-up replies to or replaces an earlier request.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Eliminates translator discretion over transcript scope, turn naming, and REPLY_TO versus REVISES.", "cites_source": "Why Agentic Systems Need Ontologies", "addresses_note": "N7"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Action", "grammar": "action ::= \"ACTION\" operation-id \"(\" action-attrs? \")\" (\"->\" IDENT \":\" type)?\naction-attrs ::= action-attr (\",\" action-attr)*\naction-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value\noperation-id ::= operation-vocabulary member", "semantics": "Action executes one external operation. Canonical Form OSR selects exactly one operation-id per matched source predicate, SOR fixes action sequence, AOR fixes attribute order, and HNR fixes any result handle. A place action requires a selected REF target; a direct placement request is therefore canonically expanded to pick_up followed by place under Canonical Form.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Find laptops with at least 16 GB RAM under $1,200, then choose the best rated one.", "braincode": "ACTION search_web(target=laptop, max_price=1200, min_ram_gb=16) -> laptop_ref : LIST[REF[STRING]]\nACTION sort(target=laptop_ref, rank_direction=dir_desc, rank_field=rank_rating) -> sort : LIST[REF[STRING]]\nACTION extract(target=sort, limit=1) -> extract : LIST[REF[STRING]]"}, "glossary_gloss": "Action executes an external operation with governed attributes. Canonical Form fixes its operation name, attribute order, sequence, and any result handle.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Applies the canonical operation and naming rules directly to executable actions.", "cites_source": "HTML", "addresses_note": "N7"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Generate", "grammar": "generation ::= \"GENERATE\" \"(\" generate-attr (\",\" generate-attr)* \")\" \"->\" IDENT \":\" gen_type\ngenerate-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value\ngen_type ::= \"NUMBER\" | \"STRING\" | \"BOOL\" | \"LIST\" \"[\" gen_type \"]\"", "semantics": "Generate creates a non-effectful artifact. Legal attributes are target, audience, character_properties, constraints, content, duration, duration_unit, events, format, locale, max_walk_duration, max_walk_duration_unit, quantity, quantity_unit, stop_min_per_day, stop_requirement, style, tone, topic, and transformations, governed by attribute-name. target is an artifact-value symbol and the HNR base; attributes follow AOR. content remains a transitional STRING channel during the current build phase.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Plan a 3-day Kyoto itinerary with one temple per day and no walk over 20 minutes.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ArtItinerary\n\nTASK ArtItinerary : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_itinerary, duration=3, duration_unit=unit_day, max_walk_duration=20, max_walk_duration_unit=unit_minute, stop_min_per_day=1, stop_requirement=class_temple, topic=topic_kyoto_trip) -> art_itinerary_ref : STRING\n  RETURN art_itinerary_ref\n}"}, "glossary_gloss": "Generate creates an artifact using governed requirements and formatting attributes. Its attributes and result name follow Canonical Form.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Repairs the prior handle contradiction and makes Generate's canonical ordering explicit.", "cites_source": "HTML", "addresses_note": "N7"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Utterance", "grammar": "utterance ::= \"UTTER\" speech-act \"(\" utter-attr (\",\" utter-attr)* \")\" (\"->\" IDENT)?\nspeech-act ::= operation-vocabulary member\nutter-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value", "semantics": "UTTER records a speech act inside a CONVO TURN. Legal attributes are audience, constraints, content, recipient, target, tone, and topic. audience and recipient require recipient-value; constraints requires LIST[constraint-value]; tone requires tone-value; topic requires topic-value; target follows its governing category; content remains transitional STRING. Attributes follow Canonical Form AOR. A bound UTTER result has type STRING and follows HNR.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Ask politely for realistic pickup lines.", "braincode": "CONVO Ask {\n  TURN T1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(constraints=[constraint_realistic], tone=tone_polite, topic=topic_pickup_lines)\n  }\n}"}, "glossary_gloss": "Utterance records what a speaker asks, states, or replies in a conversation. Topic and constraints are now legal governed attributes, so symbolic conversational requests do not need to misuse content.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Reconciles Conversation examples with UTTER's actual signature while preserving the transitional content channel.", "cites_source": "Why Agentic Systems Need Ontologies", "addresses_note": "N7"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Flow-If", "grammar": "flow_if ::= \"IF\" check \"THEN\" \"{\" step+ \"}\" (\"ELSE\" \"{\" step+ \"}\")?", "semantics": "Flow-If evaluates its Check when reached, executes THEN when true and ELSE when false, and gives each branch a fresh child scope. It may contain UTTER only inside a CONVO TURN. Bindings referenced by its Check follow Canonical Form HNR; all other existing Check timing and deferred-deadline behavior remains unchanged.", "worked_example": {"nl": "If my manager has not replied by Friday, send a polite follow-up.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT RoleManager\n\nTASK RoleManager CONTEXT execution_date=\"2025-06-03\" {\n  ACTION check_replied(target=role_manager, deadline=\"2025-06-06T23:59:59Z\") -> role_manager_ref : BOOL\n  IF NOT role_manager_ref THEN {\n    ACTION send_email(recipient=role_manager, tone=tone_polite, content=\"follow-up\")\n  }\n}"}, "glossary_gloss": "Flow-If runs one block when its Check is true and an optional alternative block when it is false. Its condition uses the same canonical handle names as the actions that produced its values.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Supplies the missing hygiene-required gloss and makes its canonical-handle example consistent with Bind.", "cites_source": null, "addresses_note": "N7"}, {"op": "revise", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "duration-unit-value", "glossary_gloss": "This category supplies canonical units for durations and generated-output quantities. unit_character counts output characters deterministically.", "closed": true, "members": [{"symbol": "unit_second", "gloss": "Second.", "nl_synonyms": ["seconds", "sec"]}, {"symbol": "unit_minute", "gloss": "Minute.", "nl_synonyms": ["minutes", "min"]}, {"symbol": "unit_hour", "gloss": "Hour.", "nl_synonyms": ["hours"]}, {"symbol": "unit_day", "gloss": "Day.", "nl_synonyms": ["days"]}, {"symbol": "unit_week", "gloss": "Week.", "nl_synonyms": ["weeks"]}, {"symbol": "unit_month", "gloss": "Month.", "nl_synonyms": ["months"]}, {"symbol": "unit_year", "gloss": "Year.", "nl_synonyms": ["years"]}, {"symbol": "unit_word", "gloss": "Rendered whitespace-delimited word.", "nl_synonyms": ["words"]}, {"symbol": "unit_item", "gloss": "Top-level generated list or report item.", "nl_synonyms": ["items", "entries"]}, {"symbol": "unit_paragraph", "gloss": "Paragraph of text.", "nl_synonyms": ["paragraphs", "paragraph"]}, {"symbol": "unit_character", "gloss": "One Unicode scalar value in the final rendered artifact; line endings are normalized to LF before counting.", "nl_synonyms": ["characters", "chars"]}], "membership_rule": null, "worked_example": {"nl": "Create a dialogue longer than 4,500 characters.", "braincode": "GENERATE(target=art_dialogue, quantity=4500, quantity_unit=unit_character) -> art_dialogue_ref : STRING"}, "change_type": "MINOR", "rationale": "Adds the missing governed unit required for deterministic character-length generation constraints.", "addresses_note": "N7"}], "_provider_used": "openai", "_model_used": "gpt-5.6-terra"}
Critic assessment: {"decision": "needs-rework", "kpi_assessment": {"coverage": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Explicit acquisition-and-placement expansion improves embodied-task coverage, and topic/constraint-capable UTTER improves conversational coverage. However, the new OSR fallback emits custom_general_x<bytes>, which is not a member form permitted by the current operation-vocabulary category, while relative-date requests without an externally supplied anchor are now translation errors; both create avoidable expressibility failures."}, "expressivity": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "The changes preserve useful distinctions for multiplicity, physical identity, correction, relative dates, topic, constraints, and character-count limits. But OSR reduces an unmatched requested operation to an opaque byte-derived token without defined attributes or operation signature, and the TASK-versus-CONVO rule does not operationally distinguish information seeking, advice, and artifact generation in difficult cases."}, "determinism": {"impact": "benefit", "reasoning": "This is substantial progress on N7: AOR, SOR, turn numbering, revision selection, date anchoring, placement expansion, repeated-object decomposition, and much of handle naming replace prior encoder discretion. Determinism remains incomplete because operation fallback conflicts with the actual vocabulary rule, HNR leaves key terms such as 'bare vocabulary-symbol target' and 'first step handle base' insufficiently defined, and canonical declaration naming is undefined for utterance-only conversations."}, "interpretability": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Explicit REF acquisition before PLACE and governed UTTER topic/constraints make generated expressions easier to read. Conversely, byte-encoded custom operations are not human-readable, and Canonical Form is a very dense cross-cutting rulebook whose terms are not all linked to stable lexical definitions."}, "improvement": {"impact": "benefit", "reasoning": "The canonical decomposition of physical placement, ordering of dependent operations, explicit correction links, and normalized length units give a weaker planning model materially more actionable structure than raw requests. The benefit is limited for custom-domain operations because the generated opaque fallback gives no useful planning semantics."}}, "simulations": [{"item_id": "held-trip-1", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "Plan a 3-day itinerary in Kyoto that includes at least one temple per day and avoids anything more than a 20-minute walk from the last stop.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ArtItinerary\n\nTASK ArtItinerary : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_itinerary, duration=3, duration_unit=unit_day, max_walk_duration=20, max_walk_duration_unit=unit_minute, stop_min_per_day=1, stop_requirement=class_temple, topic=topic_kyoto_trip) -> art_itinerary_ref : STRING\n  RETURN art_itinerary_ref\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "Generate, AOR, HNR, and duration-unit-value encode the closed actionable core; Canonical Form fixes the artifact handle."}, {"item_id": "dev-embodied-2", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "Put both pillows from the sofa onto the armchair, one at a time.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT Pillow\n\nTASK Pillow {\n  ACTION pick_up(source=sofa, target=pillow) -> pillow_ref : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(destination=armchair, target=pillow_ref)\n  ACTION pick_up(source=sofa, target=pillow) -> pillow_ref_2 : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(destination=armchair, target=pillow_ref_2)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "Canonical multiplicity and mandatory acquisition directly help. The rule should explicitly state that an explicit count of two denotes two distinct selected entities."}, {"item_id": "b30b9f84-0541-4826-a3af-98220b851f7c", "source": "Mind2Web (osunlp/Mind2Web, train, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Search for women's sports wear, size S.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT SportsWear\n\nTASK SportsWear {\n  ACTION search_web(gender=gender_women, size=size_small, target=sports_wear) -> sports_wear_ref : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "AOR makes the attribute order deterministic. This assumes the complete glossary's entity-name category contains sports_wear under N6."}, {"item_id": "33b57a14-f469-405c-8843-f7e8ceb5b1ed", "source": "Mind2Web (osunlp/Mind2Web, train, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Add 10 of the cheapest green shirt to my cart", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT Shirt\n\nTASK Shirt {\n  ACTION search_web(color=color_green, target=shirt) -> shirt_ref : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION sort(rank_direction=dir_asc, rank_field=rank_price, target=shirt_ref) -> sort : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION extract(limit=1, target=sort) -> extract : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION add_to_cart(quantity=10, target=extract)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "SOR preserves search, rank, choose, then cart addition. The current Action signature index must confirm quantity is legal on add_to_cart; Canonical Form itself does not supply that signature."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190907_164924_809101#1", "source": "ALFRED (json_2.1.0, train)", "nl": "Place a washed tomato on a table.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT Tomato\n\nTASK Tomato {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=tomato) -> tomato_ref : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION rinse(destination=sink, target=tomato_ref) -> rinse : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(destination=table, relation=on, target=rinse)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The proposed ACQUIRE < TRANSFORM < CONDITION < PLACE rule supplies a deterministic high-level plan. It still needs explicit operation-result typing for rinse and a rule for selecting the required sink when none is named in the user request."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190906_230132_658755#2", "source": "ALFRED (json_2.1.0, train)", "nl": "Put a warm glass on the shelf.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT Glass\n\nTASK Glass {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=glass) -> glass_ref : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION heat(destination=microwave, target=glass_ref) -> heat : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(destination=shelf, relation=on, target=heat)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "Canonical stage ordering improves the household plan. The inferred microwave is not licensed by the proposed rules, so independent encoders could diverge between a heat operation with no destination and an inferred microwave."}, {"item_id": "django__django-16819", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified (princeton-nlp/SWE-bench_Verified, test, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Reduce Add/RemoveIndex migration operations when optimizing migration operations.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT Django\n\nTASK Django {\n  ACTION modify_code(file=path_django_db_migrations_operations_models_py, revision=chg_reduce_add_remove_index_optimization, target=django)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The code-value category can carry the path and requested change under N6. Canonical operation mapping is unproven for 'reduce' because it is not listed as a synonym of modify_code."}, {"item_id": "matplotlib__matplotlib-23412", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified (princeton-nlp/SWE-bench_Verified, test, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "[Bug]: offset dash linestyle has no effect in patch objects.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT Matplotlib\n\nTASK Matplotlib {\n  ACTION modify_code(actual_output=outcome_patch_dash_offset_ignored, file=path_lib_matplotlib_patches_py, reproduction_step=repro_patch_dash_tuple_offset, revision=chg_honor_patch_dash_offset, target=matplotlib)\n  ACTION run_tests(assertion=assert_patch_dash_offset_applied, target=matplotlib)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The actionable bug-fix core is expressible through code-value categories under N6. The detailed code and screenshots are not structurally represented, but they are evidence rather than separate requested actions."}, {"item_id": "c6671", "source": "PRISM (HannahRoseKirk/prism-alignment, conversations config, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "I would like to follow a more healthier diet. I am a university student and I dont have much time to cook for myself. Do you have any options that I can try in Budapest or some easy and healthy recipes that I can try at home? Thank you, could you tell me exact places in budapest where i can eat healthy? how can i improve my lifestyle if im used to eating unhealthy food?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT Ask\n\nCONVO Ask {\n  TURN T1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(constraints=[constraint_healthy, constraint_time_limited], topic=topic_healthy_diet_budapest)\n  }\n  TURN T2 SPEAKER=USER REPLY_TO T1 {\n    UTTER ask(constraints=[constraint_exact_places], topic=topic_healthy_restaurants_budapest)\n  }\n  TURN T3 SPEAKER=USER REPLY_TO T2 {\n    UTTER ask(topic=topic_transition_from_unhealthy_diet)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "UTTER topic and constraints help sequence the follow-ups. The proposed declaration name is not canonically defined for an utterance-only CONVO because HNR defines no first-step handle base for an unbound UTTER."}, {"item_id": "c4355", "source": "PRISM (HannahRoseKirk/prism-alignment, conversations config, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "what is view on friendship? how do i become a good friend?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT Ask\n\nCONVO Ask {\n  TURN T1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(topic=topic_friendship)\n  }\n  TURN T2 SPEAKER=USER REPLY_TO T1 {\n    UTTER ask(topic=topic_becoming_a_good_friend)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The conversational sequence is retained, but topic symbols do not encode the desired opinion/advice distinction unless separate topic or speech-act vocabulary is added. CONVO naming remains underdefined."}, {"item_id": "c6745", "source": "PRISM (HannahRoseKirk/prism-alignment, conversations config, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "I'm enjoying our chats. Let's go with something really controversial, are you up for that? Is it jam first then cream, or cream first, then jam? Make your choice then make your argument! Spoken like a true Cornish AI! Well done.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT Ask\n\nCONVO Ask {\n  TURN T1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(constraints=[constraint_controversial_topic], topic=topic_controversial_discussion)\n  }\n  TURN T2 SPEAKER=USER REPLY_TO T1 {\n    UTTER ask(constraints=[constraint_make_choice, constraint_provide_argument], topic=topic_scone_jam_cream_order)\n  }\n  TURN T3 SPEAKER=USER REPLY_TO T2 {\n    UTTER acknowledge(topic=topic_cornish_choice)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "TURN order and REPLY_TO preserve the interaction. Exact nuance and humorous register remain outside the symbolic categories, which is acceptable for open prose during the build phase."}, {"item_id": "c3642", "source": "PRISM (HannahRoseKirk/prism-alignment, conversations config, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Hey chat, do you think that the legal age of adulthood should be lowered from 21 to 18 in the US? Are there any other legal ages that are below 21? But if people can start voting and serving the military at 18, wouldn't it make sense if people could start drinking alcohol at 18 as well?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT Ask\n\nCONVO Ask {\n  TURN T1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(topic=topic_us_age_of_majority_18)\n  }\n  TURN T2 SPEAKER=USER REPLY_TO T1 {\n    UTTER ask(topic=topic_us_legal_ages_below_21)\n  }\n  TURN T3 SPEAKER=USER REPLY_TO T2 {\n    UTTER ask(topic=topic_us_drinking_age_18_argument)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The three-turn argumentative sequence is preserved, but the request for the assistant's qualified view is only coarsely represented by ask plus topic."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-107765", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns, model=gpt-3.5-turbo-0613)", "nl": "中国电动车行业发展; cover letter; PHD COVER LETTER", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ArtCoverLetter\n\nTASK ArtCoverLetter : STRING {\n  GENERATE(format=format_email, target=art_phd_cover_letter, topic=topic_phd_application) -> art_phd_cover_letter_ref : STRING\n  RETURN art_phd_cover_letter_ref\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "CSR treats the final supplied human request as a generation request. The earlier topic change is excluded by ISR, but this conflicts with the separate statement that a multi-message supplied input emits one TURN per supplied message; the scope rules need reconciliation."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-18683", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns, model=gpt-3.5-turbo-0301)", "nl": "Напиши короткое описание для Windows приложений Clipboard Manager, Flow Launcher, Espanso, Everything. В виде списка, а не таблицы.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ArtShortText\n\nTASK ArtShortText : STRING {\n  GENERATE(constraints=[constraint_short_description_per_application], format=format_bullet_list, target=art_application_description_list, topic=topic_windows_apps_clipboard_manager_flow_launcher_espanso_everything) -> art_application_description_list_ref : STRING\n  RETURN art_application_description_list_ref\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The final correction from table to list is represented as a final generation request, but Canonical Form does not say whether the final user correction revises the prior generation or merely replaces source scope."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-9962", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns, model=gpt-3.5-turbo-0301)", "nl": "Create a Civil danger warning for Counties located in Central Oklahoma, listing counties, about an unknown anomaly that causes suicide from fear or despair upon viewing it through any form of media.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ArtCivilDangerWarning\n\nTASK ArtCivilDangerWarning : STRING {\n  GENERATE(constraints=[constraint_list_central_oklahoma_counties, constraint_vague_to_avoid_exposure], format=format_warning_bulletin, target=art_civil_danger_warning, topic=topic_central_oklahoma_media_anomaly) -> art_civil_danger_warning_ref : STRING\n  RETURN art_civil_danger_warning_ref\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Artifact type, warning format, geographic scope, and safety-oriented vagueness are structured under assumed complete categories. The fictional anomaly's substantive content remains an atomic topic."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-5353", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns, model=gpt-3.5-turbo-0301)", "nl": "Write a 90 minute script for a GoT scene where Daenerys talks with Sansa, Jon, and Arya; northern accents get thicker and slangier as the conversation goes on, while Daenerys struggles to understand.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ArtScript\n\nTASK ArtScript : STRING {\n  GENERATE(character_properties=[char_arya, char_daenerys, char_jon_snow, char_sansa_stark], constraints=[constraint_duration_90_minutes, constraint_serious_opening, constraint_progressively_thicker_northern_accents, constraint_include_northern_slang, constraint_daenerys_struggles_to_understand], target=art_script, topic=topic_game_of_thrones_northern_accent_scene) -> art_script_ref : STRING\n  RETURN art_script_ref\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The important structural constraints can be represented as symbols under N6, but the requested dialogue and stylistic realization remain opaque artifact substance."}, {"item_id": "1776027441532", "source": "ThoughtTrace (SCAI-JHU/ThoughtTrace, Parquet column-projected sample, JSON-decoded messages)", "nl": "How should I start going to the gym? I'm 180cm and 110kg, could you prepare a 3 day split? Could you prepare a diet for 5 days consisting of 4 meals for 2200kcal, lactose intolerant and no eggs? Could you prepare a shopping list for that diet and estimate cost?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ArtStructuredReport\n\nTASK ArtStructuredReport : STRING {\n  GENERATE(constraints=[constraint_three_day_weight_loss_split, constraint_lactose_free, constraint_exclude_eggs, constraint_five_days, constraint_four_meals_per_day, constraint_2200_kcal, constraint_include_shopping_list, constraint_estimate_grocery_cost], format=format_structured_report, target=art_diet_and_training_plan, topic=topic_gym_beginner_weight_loss_180cm_110kg) -> art_diet_and_training_plan_ref : STRING\n  RETURN art_diet_and_training_plan_ref\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The user’s successive corrections and narrowed scope are collapsed into the final request, losing the conversational correction history. A multi-message input should instead be a CONVO if canonical scope includes the supplied trajectory."}, {"item_id": "1775939473361", "source": "ThoughtTrace (SCAI-JHU/ThoughtTrace, Parquet column-projected sample, JSON-decoded messages)", "nl": "Plan a June Thursday-to-Sunday Sedona itinerary from Orlando via Phoenix, with hikes, shopping, natural beauty, an Airbnb in town, drives up to two hours, specific times, and restaurant rankings.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ArtItinerary\n\nTASK ArtItinerary : STRING {\n  GENERATE(constraints=[constraint_thursday_to_sunday, constraint_specific_times, constraint_include_hikes, constraint_include_shopping, constraint_include_natural_beauty, constraint_drive_limit_two_hours, constraint_rank_restaurants], duration=4, duration_unit=unit_day, format=format_structured_report, target=art_itinerary, topic=topic_sedona_june_trip_orlando_phoenix) -> art_itinerary_ref : STRING\n  RETURN art_itinerary_ref\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Temporal duration, transport endpoints, activity preferences, drive limit, schedule precision, and ranking requirement are represented at the request level. Exact flight times and named restaurant evaluation need further dedicated vocabulary if N4 closes prose."}, {"item_id": "1776023647092", "source": "ThoughtTrace (SCAI-JHU/ThoughtTrace, Parquet column-projected sample, JSON-decoded messages)", "nl": "My company is adopting AI and 30% of daily tasks are automated. How should I handle this with my team? What if one member is laid off? Give steps to manage the changes. The team is embracing AI agents; how do I keep momentum?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT Ask\n\nCONVO Ask {\n  TURN T1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(constraints=[constraint_ai_automates_30_percent_tasks], topic=topic_managing_team_ai_adoption)\n  }\n  TURN T2 SPEAKER=USER REPLY_TO T1 {\n    UTTER ask(topic=topic_manage_possible_layoff)\n  }\n  TURN T3 SPEAKER=USER REPLY_TO T2 {\n    UTTER ask(constraints=[constraint_step_by_step], topic=topic_manage_ai_driven_change)\n  }\n  TURN T4 SPEAKER=USER REPLY_TO T3 {\n    UTTER ask(constraints=[constraint_team_already_embracing_agents], topic=topic_sustain_ai_adoption_momentum)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Conversation sequencing is useful and preserves the follow-up progression. It remains noncanonical because utterance-only CONVO declaration naming has no HNR-defined base."}, {"item_id": "1775828997466", "source": "ThoughtTrace (SCAI-JHU/ThoughtTrace, Parquet column-projected sample, JSON-decoded messages)", "nl": "Can you help me organize my daily life and responsibilities more effectively?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT Ask\n\nCONVO Ask {\n  TURN T1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(topic=topic_organize_daily_life_and_responsibilities)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The advice-request speech act and topic are retained, but no canonical declaration name is defined because the first step has no result handle."}], "cross_check": {"used": false, "agreement": "n/a", "notes": "No independent translations were supplied. Simulated convergence is substantially better for the itinerary and direct-placement items because AOR, SOR, multiplicity, and REF naming are specified; it remains low for unmatched operations, utterance-only CONVO names, source-scope selection, and inferred equipment/locations."}, "required_changes": [{"target": "canonical-form", "change": "Replace OSR's `custom_general_x<bytes>` fallback with a token form that is explicitly legal under operation-vocabulary, has a glossary-defined membership rule, a static signature/attribute policy, and a human-readable deterministic domain/action decomposition. Alternatively remove fallback emission and make unmatched operations a translation error until a glossary operation is added. Do not claim an undefined `custom-token form`."}, {"target": "canonical-form", "change": "Define HNR completely and mechanically for every Bind site: define 'bare vocabulary-symbol target,' distinguish a literal vocabulary value from an identifier reference, specify whether `_ref` is part of the first-step handle base used for declaration names, and give a declaration-name rule for a first step with no result, including UTTER-only CONVOs."}, {"target": "canonical-form", "change": "Reconcile ISR/CSR scope rules. State exactly whether a supplied dataset transcript includes all human turns or only the final human message, and remove the contradiction between 'through its final human-authored message' and 'a multi-message supplied input ... emits one CONVO TURN per supplied message.' Specify how final-request artifact generation interacts with preceding corrections."}, {"target": "canonical-form", "change": "Define deterministic implicit-resource policy for decompositions: when a request says washed/warm but names no sink or microwave, either require a source/destination symbol in the request, define a canonical abstract resource symbol, or reject the translation. Also specify result types and REF identity preservation for transform operations such as rinse and heat."}, {"target": "Task", "change": "Update stale Task/Action/Bind/Generate/Conversation worked examples and glossary examples to obey the adopted canonical handle and ordering rules, including required `_ref` collisions and canonical TASK/CONVO declaration names. Normative examples that violate canonical form undermine deterministic encoding."}], "logic_issues": ["OSR says custom_general_x<bytes> 'matches operation-vocabulary's custom-token fo