  "note_argument": "The changes replace translator discretion with explicit canonical rules while retaining one unambiguous parse. Unmatched operations remain legal through the existing custom operation category, but now have a deterministic readable token derivation and a fixed signature policy.",
  "foundations_overview": "BrainCode is a statically typed context-free request language with a normative Canonical Form translation layer. Grammar determines a unique parse; Canonical Form determines one emitted document shape for a supplied request by fixing request scope, declaration selection and naming, vocabulary-symbol selection, attribute order, result handles, dependency order, transcript links, and required embodied-action expansion. Vocabulary members supply canonical meanings for synonyms, while transitional STRING channels remain available during the N2/N3 build phase.",
