   "user: i am pharmacist and i wanna know what is the main side effect of captopril?",
   "  [feedback: task_motivation] i wanna make sure about the side effects",
   "assistant: **Main side effect of Captopril:**\n\nThe **most characteristic and common side effect** of captopril is **dry cough**.\n\n### Why does it happen?\nCaptopril is an ACE inhibitor. It blocks the enzyme that converts angiotensin I to angiotensin II, but it also increases bradykinin levels in the lungs. This increase in bradykinin is the main reason for the persistent dry cough.\n\n### Other important side effects (ranked by clinical importance):\n\n| Frequency | Side Effect                  | Notes |\n|-----------|------------------------------|-------|\n| Very common | Dry cough                    | Main reason patients stop the drug |\n| Common      | Hyperkalemia                 | Especially in kidney disease or with potassium supplements |\n| Common      | Dizziness / Hypotension      | Especially after first dose |\n| Serious     | Angioedema                   | Can be life-threatening (swelling of face, lips, tongue) |\n| Serious     | Acute kidney injury          | Especially in patients with renal artery stenosis |\n| Serious     | Neutropenia / Agranulocytosis| Rare but more common with high doses |\n\n### Quick tips for you as a pharmacist:\n- Cough usually appears within 1–2 weeks but can start even after months.\n- Switching to an ARB (like losartan, valsartan) usually solves the cough.\n- Captopril has a **short half-life**, so it’s taken 2–3 times daily (unlike other ACE inhibitors).\n\nWould you like me to also give you the counseling points you should tell patients when dispensing captopril?",
   "  [feedback: explicit_affirmation] I feel like i got every thing i want because it was a well organized and very satisfying for me ."
  ]
 }
